            "text": "* [Technology Vendors][1]\n* [Recent Research][2]\n* [Newsletter][3]\n* [Media Support][4]\n* [Login][5]\n[[CB Insights]][6]\n* Who We Serve\n* Function\n* [Corporate Strategy][7]\n* [Corporate Venture Capital][8]\n* [Venture Capital][9]\n* [IT][10]\n* [Corporate Innovation][11]\n* [Featured Item]\n\n### How VCs Use CB Insights\n\n[Go to the video gallery \u2192][12]\n* Industries\n* [Consumer & Retail][13]\n* [Tech][14]\n* [Insurance][15]\n* [Healthcare][16]\n* [Industrials][17]\n* [Financial Services][18]\n* [Professional Services][19]\n* [Featured Item]\n\n### Professional Services\n\n[Learn More\u2192][20]\n* [Success Stories][21]\n* How We Help\n* [Understand Tech Markets][22]\n* [Anticipate Competitor Strategy][23]\n* [Determine Tech Strategy][24]\n* [Connect with Tech Vendors & Partners][25]\n* [Turbocharge Digital Transformation][26]\n* What We Offer\n* Platform\n* [Overview][27]\n* [Technology Search Engine][28]\n* [Market Analytics and Visualizations][29]\n* [Team Management and Collaboration][30]\n* [Featured Item]\n\n### Platform Overview\n\n[Learn More\u2192][31]\n* [Data][32]\n* [Research][33]\n* [Personal Briefing][34]\n* [GenAI Instant Insights][35]\n* [Public Equity Data][36]\n* [Buyer Interview Transcripts][37]\n* [Analyst Briefings][38]\n* [API & Data Feeds][39]\n* Integrations\n* [Overview][40]\n* [Chrome and Edge][41]\n* [Salesforce][42]\n* [Affinity][43]\n* [Microsoft Excel][44]\n* [Google Sheets][45]\n* [Microsoft Teams][46]\n* [Slack][47]\n* [Google Slides][48]\n* [App Partners][49]\n* [Browser Extension][50]\n* [Pricing][51]\n* About Us\n* [Overview][52]\n* Our teams\n* [Business Development][53]\n* [Engineering][54]\n* [Operations][55]\n* [Product][56]\n* [See all \u2192][57]\n* [Open Jobs][58]\n\nLoading...\n\n[Quotient Technology company logo]\n\n# Quotient Technology\n\nUnclaimed\n[quotient.com][59]\n* [Overview & Products][60]\n* [Financials][61]\n* [People][62]\n* [Alternatives & Competitors][63]\n\n## Founded Year\n\n1998\n\n## Stage\n\nTake Private | Acquired\n\n## Total Raised\n\n$242M\n\n## Valuation\n\n$0000 View\n\n## Revenue\n\n$0000 View\n\n## About Quotient Technology\n\nQuotient Technology focuses on retail marketing solutions within the omnichannel marketing sector.\nThe company provides services that include in-store media networks, digital incentives, and digital\nout-of-home advertising. It primarily serves the retail industry, offering data-driven marketing\nstrategies and campaign optimization. The company was formerly known as Coupons.com. Quotient\nTechnology was founded in 1998 and is based in Salt Lake City, Utah. On 20 Jun 2023, it was acquired\nby Neptune Retail Solutions.\n\n## Headquarters Location\n\n1260 East Stringham Avenue Suite 600\n\nSalt Lake City, Utah, 84106,\n\nUnited States\n\n650-605-4600\n\nLoading...\n\n## ESPs containing Quotient Technology\n\nThe ESP matrix leverages data and analyst insight to identify and rank leading companies in a given\ntechnology landscape.\n\n[Location intelligence][64]\nEnterprise Tech / BI & Operational Intelligence\n\nThe location intelligence market provides businesses with valuable insights into how consumers\ninteract with physical spaces, allowing for data-driven decision making in areas such as real\nestate, retail, healthcare, and advertising. This market is becoming increasingly important as\nprivacy regulations and changing consumer behaviors make it more difficult to gather accurate data.\nCompanies in thi\u2026\n\nQuotient Technology named as Highflier among 15 other companies, including [IBM][65],\n[Salesforce][66], and [Foursquare][67].\n\nView all ESPs\n][68]\n\nLoading...\n\n## Expert Collections containing Quotient Technology\n\nExpert Collections are analyst-curated lists that highlight the companies you need to know in the\nmost important technology spaces.\n\nQuotient Technology is included in **4 Expert Collections,** including **E-Commerce**.\n\n# E-Commerce\n\n11,526 items\n\nCompanies that sell goods online (B2C), or enable the selling of goods online via tech solutions\n(B2B).\n\n# Grocery Retail Tech\n\n831 items\n\nStartups providing B2B solutions to grocery businesses to improve their store and omni-channel\nperformance. Includes customer analytics platforms, in-store robots, predictive inventory management\nsystems, online enablement for grocers and consumables retailers, and more.\n\n# Conference Exhibitors\n\n5,302 items\n\n# Retail Media Networks\n\n467 items\n\nTech companies helping retailers build and operate retail media networks. Includes solutions like\ndemand-side platforms, AI-generated content, digital shelf displays, and more.\n\nLearn more by requesting a demo\n\n## Quotient Technology Patents\n\nQuotient Technology has filed 43 patents.\n\nThe 3 most popular patent topics include:\n* data management\n* online auction websites\n* payment systems\n\n[patents chart]\nView Patents Chart\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\nApplica\u2502Gran\u2502Title \u2502Related Topics \u2502Sta\ntion \u2502t \u2502 \u2502 \u2502tus\nDate \u2502Date\u2502 \u2502 \u2502\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\n11/3/20\u25027/4/\u2502[Localized facility-specific \u2502Metadata, Data management, Promotion and \u2502Gra\n20 \u25022023\u2502presentation of digital temporary \u2502marketing communications, Product management, \u2502nt\n\u2502 \u2502offer data][69] \u2502Brand management \u2502\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nApplication \u250211/3/2020\nDate \u2502\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nGrant Date \u25027/4/2023\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nTitle \u2502[Localized facility-specific presentation of digital temporary offer data][70]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nRelated \u2502Metadata, Data management, Promotion and marketing communications, Product management,\nTopics \u2502Brand management\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStatus \u2502Grant\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nLearn more by requesting a demo\n\n## Latest Quotient Technology News\n\n[Eagle Eye lets major US partner out of its sight, loses contract][71]\n\nJun 2, 2025\n\nThe Guildford, England-based digital marketing firm said that Neptune Retail Solutions, an\nadvertising company focused on digitised shopping incentives, had terminated Eagle Eye's contract\nwith a national US grocery chain. The CPG-funded contract runs out on August 2, Eagle Eye said. The\nfirm explained this was due to Neptune's 2023 acquisition of a Quotient Technology Inc, a Salt Lake\nCity, US-based marketer specialising in online promotions. Eagle Eye said it was working on cost\nreduction measures to ease the blow's impact, which comes amid the firm's move towards the\nsoftware-as-a-service business. The London market did not appear to share Eagle Eye's confidence in\nweathering the storm - Eagle Eye shares dropped 38% to 220.00 pence each on Monday morning. The\ncompany admitted the contract loss would likely have a material impact on full-year performance.\nNonetheless, Eagle Eye predicted it will meet market expectations, which are for revenue of about\nGBP47.7 million, with an adjusted margin for earnings before interest, taxation, depreciation and\namortisation of 24%. \"The strength of recent renewals means that 83% of revenue from the remaining\ntop 10 customers is under contract to at least financial 2027. Net recurring revenue excluding the\nNRS contract remains strong at 117%, as at April 30, 2025,\" Eagle Eye said. \"While the news of this\ncontract termination is clearly disappointing, it reflects commercial changes at NRS, outside of our\ncontrol, and we are taking measures to mitigate the financial impact of the loss,\" said Eagle Eye\nChief Executive Tim Mason. \"This is a short-term set back and the fundamentals of the business are\nstrong. We have the industry-leading loyalty and promotions capability globally, with attractive\ngrowth prospects and an unchanged opportunity.\" By Holly Munks, Alliance News reporter Comments and\nquestions to newsroom@alliancenews.com Copyright 2025 Alliance News Ltd. All Rights Reserved.\n\nFeb 12, 2025\n[Influencer Marketing Platform Market to Grow by USD 80.3 Billion from 2025-2029, Driven by Vendor\nPartnerships and M&amp;A, Report on Market Evolution Powered by AI - Technavio][72]\nJan 28, 2025\n[Influencering Platform Market size is set to grow by USD 80.3 billion from 2025-2029, increasing\npartnerships and mergers and acquisitions among vendors boost the market- Technavio][73]\nNov 25, 2024\n[Influencer Marketing Platform Market size is set to grow by USD 52.23 billion from 2024-2028,\nincreasing partnerships and mergers and acquisitions among vendors to boost the revenue-\nTechnavio][74]\nJun 24, 2024\n[Retail Intelligence Software market segments, driver, restraints, and trends][75]\nLearn more by requesting a demo\n\n### Quotient Technology Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)\n* When was Quotient Technology founded?\n\nQuotient Technology was founded in 1998.\n* Where is Quotient Technology's headquarters?\n\nQuotient Technology's headquarters is located at 1260 East Stringham Avenue, Salt Lake City.\n* What is Quotient Technology's latest funding round?\n\nQuotient Technology's latest funding round is Take Private.\n* How much did Quotient Technology raise?\n\nQuotient Technology raised a total of $242M.\n* Who are the investors of Quotient Technology?\n\nInvestors of Quotient Technology include Neptune Retail Solutions, Greylock Partners, T. Rowe\nPrice, Passport Capital, G & H Partners and 6 more.\n* Who are Quotient Technology's competitors?\n\nCompetitors of Quotient Technology include Blis, Inmar, Reveal Mobile, RetailMeNot, Perch\nInteractive and 7 more.\n\nLoading...\n\n## Compare Quotient Technology to Competitors\n\n[StreetMetrics][76]\n\nStreetMetrics provides analytics and measurement solutions for the out-of-home (OOH) media industry.\nThe company has tools for planning, measuring, and attributing the performance of OOH advertising\ncampaigns, focusing on media performance, audience reach, and advertising effectiveness. It serves\nOOH media operators and advertisers. StreetMetrics was formerly known as Axle Advertisements. It was\nfounded in 2018 and is based in Birmingham, Alabama.\n\n[InMarket Logo]\n[InMarket][77]\n\nInMarket oeprates as a digital advertising market leader focused on real-time marketing and\nmeasurement within the advertising industry. The company offers a platform that connects brands with\nconsumers by leveraging data-driven insights to optimize ad spend and drive growth. InMarket's\nservices include audience segmentation, programmatic solutions, omnichannel activation, predictive\nmodeling, campaign optimization, and commerce analytics. It was formerly known as Checkpoints. It\nwas founded in 2010 and is based in Wichita Falls, Texas.\n\n[Adsquare Logo]\n[Adsquare][78]\n\nAdsquare is a location intelligence platform that provides services related to advertising campaigns\nthrough geospatial data. The company offers services such as campaign planning, activation,\nmeasurement, and attribution to assist various stakeholders including advertisers, media agencies,\nand out-of-home operators. Adsquare serves the advertising and marketing technology sectors,\noffering solutions for DSPs, DMPs, SSPs, and data owners. It was founded in 2012 and is based in\nHennigsdorf, Germany.\n\n[Karma][79]\n\nKarma is an AI-powered shopping assistant that operates in the e-commerce industry. The company\noffers a browser extension and mobile app that help users save money by tracking prices, finding\ncoupons, and managing shopping lists. Karma primarily serves individual consumers looking to\noptimize their online shopping experience. It was founded in 2014 and is based in Tel Aviv, Israel.\n\n[Syndeca][80]\n\nSyndeca specializes in no-code visual commerce solutions within the digital marketing and "
          },
