            "text": "* [Technology Vendors][1]\n* [Recent Research][2]\n* [Newsletter][3]\n* [Media Support][4]\n* [Login][5]\n[[CB Insights]][6]\n* Who We Serve\n* Function\n* [Corporate Strategy][7]\n* [Corporate Venture Capital][8]\n* [Venture Capital][9]\n* [IT][10]\n* [Corporate Innovation][11]\n* [Featured Item]\n\n### How VCs Use CB Insights\n\n[Go to the video gallery \u2192][12]\n* Industries\n* [Consumer & Retail][13]\n* [Tech][14]\n* [Insurance][15]\n* [Healthcare][16]\n* [Industrials][17]\n* [Financial Services][18]\n* [Professional Services][19]\n* [Featured Item]\n\n### Professional Services\n\n[Learn More\u2192][20]\n* [Success Stories][21]\n* How We Help\n* [Understand Tech Markets][22]\n* [Anticipate Competitor Strategy][23]\n* [Determine Tech Strategy][24]\n* [Connect with Tech Vendors & Partners][25]\n* [Turbocharge Digital Transformation][26]\n* What We Offer\n* Platform\n* [Overview][27]\n* [Technology Search Engine][28]\n* [Market Analytics and Visualizations][29]\n* [Team Management and Collaboration][30]\n* [Featured Item]\n\n### Platform Overview\n\n[Learn More\u2192][31]\n* [Data][32]\n* [Research][33]\n* [Personal Briefing][34]\n* [GenAI Instant Insights][35]\n* [Public Equity Data][36]\n* [Buyer Interview Transcripts][37]\n* [Analyst Briefings][38]\n* [API & Data Feeds][39]\n* Integrations\n* [Overview][40]\n* [Chrome and Edge][41]\n* [Salesforce][42]\n* [Affinity][43]\n* [Microsoft Excel][44]\n* [Google Sheets][45]\n* [Microsoft Teams][46]\n* [Slack][47]\n* [Google Slides][48]\n* [App Partners][49]\n* [Browser Extension][50]\n* [Pricing][51]\n* About Us\n* [Overview][52]\n* Our teams\n* [Business Development][53]\n* [Engineering][54]\n* [Operations][55]\n* [Product][56]\n* [See all \u2192][57]\n* [Open Jobs][58]\n\nLoading...\n\n[Acquia company logo]\n\n# Acquia\n\nUnclaimed\n[acquia.com][59]\n* [Overview & Products][60]\n* [Financials][61]\n* [People][62]\n* [Alternatives & Competitors][63]\n\n## Founded Year\n\n2007\n\n## Stage\n\nAcq - Fin | Alive\n\n## Total Raised\n\n$178.5M\n\n## Valuation\n\n$0000 View\n\n## Mosaic Score\n## The Mosaic Score is an algorithm that measures the overall financial health and market potential\n## of private companies.\n\n+52 points in the past 30 days\n\n## About Acquia\n\nAcquia is a company that offers digital experience platforms (DXP) within the technology sector. Its\nmain offerings include tools for content management, customer data management, and digital asset\nmanagement. Acquia serves sectors such as healthcare, government, retail, financial services,\neducation, and others that require digital presence and engagement. It was founded in 2007 and is\nbased in Boston, Massachusetts.\n\n## Headquarters Location\n\n53 State Street 10th Floor\n\nBoston, Massachusetts, 02109,\n\nUnited States\n\n888-922-7842\n\nLoading...\n\n## ESPs containing Acquia\n\nThe ESP matrix leverages data and analyst insight to identify and rank leading companies in a given\ntechnology landscape.\n\n[Omnichannel customer engagement][64]\nEnterprise Tech / Marketing & Ad Tech\n\nThe omnichannel customer engagement market provides platforms that unify customer data and\norchestrate personalized communications across multiple channels including email, SMS, push\nnotifications, social media, and mobile apps. These platforms enable real-time customer journey\norchestration, AI-powered personalization, and automated campaign management to improve customer\nretention and lifetime v\u2026\n\nAcquia named as Highflier among 15 other companies, including [Braze][65], [MoEngage][66], and\n[Pegasystems][67].\n\nView all ESPs\n][68]\n\nLoading...\n\n## Expert Collections containing Acquia\n\nExpert Collections are analyst-curated lists that highlight the companies you need to know in the\nmost important technology spaces.\n\nAcquia is included in **4 Expert Collections,** including **Grocery Retail Tech**.\n\n# Grocery Retail Tech\n\n831 items\n\nStartups providing B2B solutions to grocery businesses to improve their store and omni-channel\nperformance. Includes customer analytics platforms, in-store robots, predictive inventory management\nsystems, online enablement for grocers and consumables retailers, and more.\n\n# Tech IPO Pipeline\n\n286 items\n\n# Conference Exhibitors\n\n5,302 items\n\n# Targeted Marketing Tech\n\n453 items\n\nThis Collection includes companies building technology that enables marketing teams to identify,\nreach, and engage with consumers seamlessly across channels.\n\nLearn more by requesting a demo\n\n## Latest Acquia News\n\n[Acquia Launches Fair Trade Initiative, Committing 2% of Every Eligible Partner Deal to the Drupal\nAssociation][69]\n\nMay 14, 2026\n\nEvery Eligible Partner Deal to the Drupal Association New structural commitment embeds open source\nsustainability directly into Acquia's partner co-sell flow, making every Acquia partner a recognized\nDrupal contributor May 14, 2026 08:00 ET Acquia Inc. BOSTON, May 14, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Acquia\ntoday announced the Fair Trade Initiative , a commitment that directs 2% of every revenue-driven\ntransaction closed with a partner to the Drupal Association, credited in the partner\u2019s name. The\ninitiative is built directly into the new Acquia Partner Program, not structured as a one-time grant\nor discretionary sponsorship, but embedded into the economics of every deal. The move addresses what\nAcquia describes as the hardest unsolved problem in open source: connecting commercial success to\ncommunity sustainability at scale. As Acquia partners grow their Drupal practices, a corresponding\npercentage of that growth automatically flows back to the foundation that stewards the project. \u201cFor\ntoo long, the open source model has relied on the goodwill of individuals and the discretion of\ncompanies to reinvest in the communities they profit from. The Fair Trade Initiative changes that,\u201d\nsaid James Sims, Vice President, Partners at Acquia. \u201cWhen Drupal grows, Acquia grows. When Acquia\npartners win, Drupal wins. That alignment should be structural, and now it is.\u201d What the Fair Trade\nInitiative Means for Partners Under the initiative, every Acquia partner\u2019s full revenue and\nincentives remain unchanged. The 2% Drupal Association contribution is funded by Acquia, not\ndeducted from partner margins. Contributions are tracked and publicly attributed in the Acquia\nPartner Portal, formally recognizing partners as Drupal community contributors. Donations may also\nbe applied toward Drupal Association-led partner and membership programs for which partners qualify,\npotentially unlocking additional community benefits and recognition. What the Fair Trade Initiative\nMeans for Customers When organizations contract directly with Acquia for Drupal implementations, a\nportion of every engagement is automatically reinvested in the open source platform their digital\nexperience depends on, at no additional cost. The 2% contribution comes entirely from Acquia.\nCustomers get the same world-class Drupal expertise, with community reinvestment built in.\nAvailability The Fair Trade Initiative is effective immediately as part of the new Acquia Partner\nProgram, terms and conditions apply. For more information, visit acquia.com/partners. About Acquia\nAcquia is the digital experience platform built for a world where your audience is both humans and\nagents. As AI agents become active participants in how people discover, consume, and act on digital\ncontent, Acquia gives enterprise teams the platform to create, manage, and distribute experiences\ndesigned for both. Powered by agentic AI that orchestrates, not just advises, Acquia automates\ncomplex digital workflows within the governance guardrails large organizations require. Acquia\nprovides Acquia Source as a digital command center, a unified intelligent workspace where digital\nteams manage content, applications, AI agents, and analytics in one place. Acquia. Built for what's\nnext. About the Drupal Association Drupal is one of the world's most trusted open source content\nmanagement platforms, powering millions of websites and digital experiences since its creation in\n2001. From humble beginnings in a university dorm room, Drupal has grown into a global force in web\ntechnology, supported by a community of thousands of active contributors worldwide. Drupal's\ncommitment to innovation, security, and accessibility has made it a cornerstone of the open web.\nThrough continuous community-driven development and a dedication to web standards, Drupal has\nconsistently evolved to meet the changing needs of the digital world while maintaining its core\nvalues of flexibility, security, and community collaboration. Media Contact\n\nMay 14, 2026\n[Acquia Launches Fair Trade Initiative, Committing 2% of Every Eligible Partner Deal to the Drupal\nAssociation][70]\nApr 28, 2026\n[Acquia Announces Significant Updates to Acquia Source and Launches Acquia AI][71]\nApr 28, 2026\n[Acquia Announces Significant Updates to Acquia Source and Launches Acquia AI][72]\nApr 28, 2026\n[Acquia Announces Significant Updates to Acquia Source and Launches Acquia AI][73]\nLearn more by requesting a demo\n\n### Acquia Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)\n* When was Acquia founded?\n\nAcquia was founded in 2007.\n* Where is Acquia's headquarters?\n\nAcquia's headquarters is located at 53 State Street, Boston.\n* What is Acquia's latest funding round?\n\nAcquia's latest funding round is Acq - Fin.\n* How much did Acquia raise?\n\nAcquia raised a total of $178.5M.\n* Who are the investors of Acquia?\n\nInvestors of Acquia include Vista Equity Partners, ESO Fund, SharesPost, Split Rock Partners, NEA\nand 17 more.\n* Who are Acquia's competitors?\n\nCompetitors of Acquia include Radiant, CrownPeak, Movable Ink, Prepr, Dynamic Yield and 7 more.\n\nLoading...\n\n## Compare Acquia to Competitors\n\n[Sitecore Logo]\n[Sitecore][74]\n\nSitecore is a company that specializes in digital experience management within the marketing\ntechnology sector. Its offerings include a platform for managing content, data, and personalization\nto facilitate customer engagement. Sitecore serves sectors that require digital marketing\ncapabilities, such as ecommerce and enterprise content management. It was founded in 2001 and is\nbased in San Francisco, California.\n\n[Contentful Logo]\n[Contentful][75]\n\nContentful is a digital experience platform that manages and delivers content within various\nbusiness sectors. The company provides tools for creating, managing, and optimizing content across\nmultiple channels and brands, using AI for personalization and workflow efficiency. Contentful\nserves sectors that require content management and delivery solutions, such as e-commerce,\nmarketing, and web development. It was founded in 2013 and is based in Berlin, Germany.\n\n[Liferay][76]\n\nLiferay is a company that specializes in digital experience platforms (DXP) and operates within the\ntechnology sector. Its main offerings include a platform that integrates content management, digital\nasset management, commerce, AI, low-code development, and personalization tools. Liferay's solutions\ncater to a variety of sectors including financial services, manufacturing, public sector, energy and\nutilities, and healthcare. It was founded in 2004 and is based in Diamond Bar, California.\n\n[Kentico Software Logo]\n[Kentico Software][77]\n\nKentico Software provides digital experience platforms that focus on content management, digital\nmarketing, and e-commerce within the technology sector. The company offers a platform that allows\nbusinesses to manage content, engage in online marketing, and facilitate e-commerce activities while\nusing artificial intelligence to improve customer journeys. Kentico serves sectors including\nfinancial services, manufacturing, healthcare, education, travel and tourism, and sports. Kentico\nSoftware was formerly known as Kentico CMS. It was founded in 2004 and is based in Brno, Czech\nRepublic.\n\n[Sitecore][78]\n\nSitecore is a leading provider of digital experience software, operating in the software industry.\nThe company offers a SaaS-enabled, composable platform that enables brands to deliver memorable\ncustomer interactions. It was founded in 2001 and is based in San Francisco, California.\n\n[Bloomreach Logo]\n[Bloomrea"
