[111]\n[Dossier 360][112]\n[Go To Market Strategy][113]\n[Paid Press Release][114]\n\n## Expertise & Services\n\n[Industry Speaks][115]\n[Terms & Conditions][116]\n[Privacy Policy][117]\n[Disclaimer][118]\n[FAQ's][119]\n[Site Map][120]\n[IT Support][121]\n[Website Issue][122]\n\n## How We Are Different?\n\n[Ken Research Vs. BCC Research][123]\n[Ken Research Vs. Euromonitor Int.][124]\n[Ken Research Vs. Nielsen][125]\n[Ken Research Vs. Marketsand Markets][126]\n[Ken Research Vs. McKinsey][127]\n[Ken Research Vs. Mordor][128]\n[Ken Research Vs. S&P Global][129]\n[Ken Research Vs. Grand View Research][130]\n[Ken Research Vs. Frost & Sullivan][131]\n\n## Company Overview\n\n## India\n\n[Unit 14, Tower B3, Spaze I Tech Business Park, Sohna Road, sector 49 Gurgaon, Haryana - 122001,\nIndia][132]\n\n## UAE\n\n[105, Al Jaz1b, Street no 2 the Greens Dubai United Arab Emirates][133]\n\n## Indonesia\n\n[The Icon BSD City, Jl. Verdant View IIIA No.15, Tangerang Regency, Province Banten-15345,\nIndonesia][134]\n\n## QATAR\n\n[Office no. 9, Building no. 171 Zone no. 42, Street no. 230, Al-Rehab Complex, C-Ring road,\nDoha][135]\n\nKen\n\nKen\n\nFor Sale Enquiries: +91-9015378249\n\n][136][\n\nankur.gupta@kenresearch.com\n\n][137]\n\nSubscribe to our Newsletter\n\nNever miss out on an update from us\n\nSubscribe\n[Terms & Conditions][138][Privacy Policy][139][Cookie Policy][140]\n\n\u00a9 Copyright 2026, Ken Research Pvt. Ltd. All rights reserved.\n\nIndia Financial Education Market Sees 25% Enrolment Surge\n\n# How a Leading Financial Education Provider Optimized Course Pricing to Drive 25% Enrolment Growth\n\nKen Research\n\nOctober 29, 2025 - 2 min read\n\n[Financial Education]\n\n###### October 29, 2025 by Ananya Singh\n\n## Who\n\nA leading financial education institution in India, operating as the training and certification arm\nof a major national stock exchange, sought to expand its reach among working professionals. The\norganization offers certification and upskilling programs in banking, financial services, and\nliteracy \u2014 catering to both entry-level and mid-career learners.\n\n## What\n\nAmid the COVID-19 pandemic, the institution faced declining course enrolments and inconsistent\naudience engagement. Despite offering industry-relevant programs, the client observed gaps in\nconsumer affordability perception and pricing sensitivity. They needed clarity on which learner\nsegments were most willing to invest in upskilling and at what price points \u2014 while also exploring\nstrategic acquisition opportunities in the EdTech space.\n\n## When\n\nThis engagement took place during the COVID-19 lockdown period, when remote learning was surging\nglobally but competition in [**India EdTech market**][141] had intensified dramatically. The\ninstitution wanted to make swift, data-driven adjustments to stay competitive in a price-sensitive\nenvironment.\n\n## Where\n\nThe study was conducted across India, focusing on urban and semi-urban markets where working\nprofessionals were seeking re-skilling opportunities during economic uncertainty. The insights were\ncritical for refining pricing and positioning strategies for both B2C and B2B (corporate learning)\nsegments.\n\n## Why\n\nThe pandemic disrupted traditional training formats and consumer spending patterns. Many\nprofessionals were hesitant to pay premium prices for virtual learning, while new entrants in the\nEdTech ecosystem were aggressively discounting courses. The client needed a clear understanding of\nthe **desirability, affordability, and perceived value** of its offerings to sustain enrolments and\nexplore platform acquisitions for long-term scalability.\n\n## How\n\nKen Research conducted a **comprehensive Consumer Behaviour Assessment** using a three-pronged\napproach:\n1. **Quantitative Consumer Analysis:** Surveys and financial appetite assessments to segment\nlearners based on affordability and motivation to upskill.\n2. **Pricing Strategy Calibration:** Evaluated elasticity of demand to identify optimal pricing\ntiers that balance perceived value with profitability.\n3. **Market Scouting for Acquisition:** Benchmarked top EdTech players on product portfolios, unit\neconomics, and learner engagement metrics to identify acquisition-fit platforms.\n\nThis analysis provided a **360\u00b0 view of learner preferences**, financial capabilities, and value\nperception across demographic cohorts. The team collaborated closely with the client\u2019s business and\nstrategy units to realign offerings and recommend a viable acquisition target.\n\n## Impact and Results\n* **360\u00b0 Customer Insight:** Delivered a holistic understanding of learner preferences and\npandemic-driven behavioural shifts.\n* **25% Increase in Enrolments:** Achieved through refined targeting and adjusted pricing strategies\nfor specific professional segments.\n* **10% Market Share Growth:** Enabled by the strategic acquisition of an e-learning platform that\ncomplemented the client\u2019s in-house offerings and digital expansion goals.\n\nA senior leader at the institution noted:\n\n\u201c[**Ken Research**][142]\u2019s insights helped us tailor our pricing, target the right audience, and\nidentify an ideal e-learning partner \u2014 enhancing both our reach and operational efficiency.\u201d\n\nThrough data-backed consumer insights and strategic evaluation, Ken Research enabled the client to\nreposition their upskilling programs for higher market resonance and sustainable growth. The project\nnot only optimized course affordability but also guided a successful EdTech acquisition \u2014\nstrengthening the institution\u2019s competitive foothold in India\u2019s post-pandemic learning environment.\n\n## Related tags\n\nEducation\n\nEducation and Recruitment\n\n### Get started\n\nWe've helped companies around the world future-proof\ntheir businesses - and we can do the same for you.\n\nGet started\n\n[1]: /procurement-research\n[2]: /expert-panel\n[3]: /about-us\n[4]: /careers#leadership\n[5]: /careers\n[6]: /contact-us\n[7]: /terms-and-conditions#privacyPolicy\n[8]: /\n[9]: /report-store\n[10]: /report-store\n[11]: /report-store#Segements\n[12]: /report-store#beseSellingReports\n[13]: /report-store#latestInsights\n[14]: /report-store\n[15]: /report-store?reportTypes=global-market-research-reports\n[16]: /country-reports\n[17]: /report-store?reportTypes=competition_benchmarking\n[18]: /custom-form\n[19]: /talk-to-us\n[20]: /report-store\n[21]: /report-store?industry=agriculture-animal-care-market\n[22]: /report-store?industry=automotive-transportation-and-warehousing-market\n[23]: /report-store?industry=banking-financial-services-and-insurance-market\n[24]: /report-store?industry=consumer-products-and-retail-market\n[25]: /report-store?industry=defense-and-security-market\n[26]: /report-store?industry=education-and-recruitment-market\n[27]: /report-store?industry=energy-and-utilities-market\n[28]: /report-store?industry=food-beverage-and-tobacco-market\n[29]: /report-store?industry=healthcare-market\n[30]: /report-store?industry=metal-mining-and-chemicals-market\n[31]: /report-store?industry=manufacturing-and-construction-market\n[32]: /report-store?industry=media-and-entertainment-market\n[33]: /report-store?industry=public-sector-and-administration-market\n[34]: /report-store?industry=technology-and-telecom-market\n[35]: /report-store?industry=agriculture-animal-care-market&topics=agriculture-chemical\n[36]: /report-store?industry=agriculture-animal-care-market&topics=fertilizer\n[37]: /report-store?industry=agriculture-animal-care-market&topics=protected-cultivation\n[38]: /report-store?industry=agriculture-animal-care-market&topics=net-wrap\n[39]: /report-store?industry=agriculture-animal-care-market&topics=agricultural-implements-and-equip\nments\n[40]: /report-store?industry=agriculture-animal-care-market&topics=combine-harvesters\n[41]: /report-store?industry=agriculture-animal-care-market&topics=tillers\n[42]: /report-stor