 Impact\n][59][\nArticles\n][60][\nPerspective\n][61]\nQUICK ACCESS[\nExplore SurveysBrowse all templates\n][62][\nCustom SurveyTailored Research\n][63]\nNeed help choosing?\n\nOur research team can recommend the right approach.\n\n[Talk to an expert ][64]\n[Consulting][65]\nCAPABILITIES\nStrategy Consulting\n][66][\nDeals & IPO Advisory\n][67]\nSTRATEGY CONSULTING\n[Market Entry][68]\n[Market Penetration][69]\n[Product Strategy][70]\n[Startup Acceleration Strategy][71]\nPUBLICATIONS\nClient Impact\n][72][\nDeal Spotlight\n][73][\nArticles\n][74][\nPerspective\n][75]\nGET IN TOUCH\n[Talk to Consultant][76]\nFEATURED\nCASE STUDY\nIsrael Logistics Market\n\nDiscover the growth opportunities in Israel's road freight and warehousing market\n\n[Read more ][77]\n[Request on demand][78]\nInsights\nBROWSE\nBy Industry\nFeatured\nBY INDUSTRY\n[Agriculture & Animal Care][79]\n[Automotive, Transportation & Warehousing][80]\n[BFSI][81]\n[Consumer Products & Retail][82]\n[Defense & Security][83]\n[Education & Recruitment][84]\n[Energy & Utilities][85]\n[Food, Beverage & Tobacco][86]\n[Healthcare][87]\n[Metal, Mining and Chemicals][88]\n[Manufacturing & Construction][89]\n[Media & Entertainment][90]\n[Public Sector and Administration][91]\n[Technology & Telecom][92]\nPUBLICATIONS\nArticles\n][93][\nCase studies\n][94][\nPerspective\n][95][\nBlogs\n][96]\nFEATURED\nLATEST\nMarket Penetration Strategy for Al-Dawaa in the KSA Retail Pharmacy Market\n\nExplore Al-Dawaa\u2019s strategy in the KSA retail pharmacy market\n\n[Read more ][97]\nSubscribe to Updates\nSearch\n[Book discovery call][98]\n[Book discovery call][99]\n\nWelcome\n\nAccess your account\n\nSign inExisting account\nSign upCreate free account\n\n## About Ken Research\n\n[Home][100]\n[About Us][101]\n[Services][102]\n[Categories][103]\n[News][104]\n[Careers][105]\n[Contact Us][106]\n\n## Resources\n\n[Blogs][107]\n[Industry Reports][108]\n[Company Research Reports][109]\n[Country Research Reports][110]\n[Bundle Reports][111]\n[Dossier 360][112]\n[Go To Market Strategy][113]\n[Paid Press Release][114]\n\n## Expertise & Services\n\n[Industry Speaks][115]\n[Terms & Conditions][116]\n[Privacy Policy][117]\n[Disclaimer][118]\n[FAQ's][119]\n[Site Map][120]\n[IT Support][121]\n[Website Issue][122]\n\n## How We Are Different?\n\n[Ken Research Vs. BCC Research][123]\n[Ken Research Vs. Euromonitor Int.][124]\n[Ken Research Vs. Nielsen][125]\n[Ken Research Vs. Marketsand Markets][126]\n[Ken Research Vs. McKinsey][127]\n[Ken Research Vs. Mordor][128]\n[Ken Research Vs. S&P Global][129]\n[Ken Research Vs. Grand View Research][130]\n[Ken Research Vs. Frost & Sullivan][131]\n\n## Company Overview\n\n## India\n\n[Unit 14, Tower B3, Spaze I Tech Business Park, Sohna Road, sector 49 Gurgaon, Haryana - 122001,\nIndia][132]\n\n## UAE\n\n[105, Al Jaz1b, Street no 2 the Greens Dubai United Arab Emirates][133]\n\n## Indonesia\n\n[The Icon BSD City, Jl. Verdant View IIIA No.15, Tangerang Regency, Province Banten-15345,\nIndonesia][134]\n\n## QATAR\n\n[Office no. 9, Building no. 171 Zone no. 42, Street no. 230, Al-Rehab Complex, C-Ring road,\nDoha][135]\n\nKen\n\nKen\n\nFor Sale Enquiries: +91-9015378249\n\n][136][\n\nankur.gupta@kenresearch.com\n\n][137]\n\nSubscribe to our Newsletter\n\nNever miss out on an update from us\n\nSubscribe\n[Terms & Conditions][138][Privacy Policy][139][Cookie Policy][140]\n\n\u00a9 Copyright 2026, Ken Research Pvt. Ltd. All rights reserved.\n\nWarehousing Efficiency Benchmark in Singapore & Malaysia\n\n# How a Leading FMCG Conglomerate Optimized Warehousing Efficiency Across Singapore and Malaysia\n# Through Strategic Supplier Identification\n\nKen Research\n\nOctober 29, 2025 - 3 min read\n\n[Malaysia FMCG Market]\n\n###### October 29, 2025 by Ananya Singh\n\n## Who: The Client\n\nA leading Singapore-based consumer goods conglomerate with diversified interests across food &\nbeverage, publishing, and property development engaged **Ken Research** to streamline its\nwarehousing and logistics operations across **Singapore and Malaysia**. With a strong regional\nfootprint and an expanding product portfolio, the client aimed to enhance **cost efficiency,\nscalability, and supplier performance visibility** through a structured, data-driven benchmarking\nstudy.\n*(Client identity withheld under NDA.)*\n\n## What: The Challenge\n\nDespite having a well-established distribution network, the client\u2019s **warehousing ecosystem had\nbecome increasingly cost-inefficient and fragmented**. Multiple vendors operated without\nstandardized performance metrics, leading to inconsistent service levels, rising costs, and limited\nscalability.\nKen Research observed that **the root cause was not capacity constraints but the lack of supplier\nsegmentation and KPI-based performance evaluation**. Leadership required a structured framework to\nidentify, assess, and partner with warehousing providers capable of supporting high-volume,\ncross-border operations while maintaining service reliability and cost competitiveness.\n\n## When: The Context\n\nBetween **2023 and 2024**, the company undertook a major **strategic logistics review** to align its\nwarehousing model with expansion goals across Southeast Asia. Post-pandemic volatility and rising\noperational costs reinforced the need for **data-backed supplier selection**, **risk mitigation**,\nand **scalable warehousing solutions** that could sustain business continuity in both domestic and\nexport markets.\n\n## Where: The Geography\n\nThe project spanned **Singapore and Malaysia**, the company\u2019s two key logistics hubs.\n* **Singapore** served as the strategic control center, focusing on oversight, compliance, and\ncoordination.\n* **Malaysia** functioned as the high-volume operational base for inventory storage and last-mile\ndispatch.\nKen Research\u2019s cross-country benchmarking enabled the client to identify **geographically optimal\nsuppliers** aligned with each market\u2019s logistical and regulatory environment.\n\n## Why: The Business Problem\n\nThe client struggled with:\n* A **fragmented supplier base** with varying pricing and service consistency.\n* **Lack of centralized visibility** into supplier capacity, scalability, and operational KPIs.\n* **Overreliance on legacy relationships** without performance-based evaluation.\n\nAs a result, warehousing decisions were often made on instinct rather than insight\u2014leading to cost\nleakages, underutilized capacity, and inefficiencies in vendor performance management.\n\n## How: Ken Research\u2019s Approach\n\n### 1. Comprehensive Ecosystem Mapping\n\nKen Research identified **50+ warehousing service providers** across Singapore and Malaysia,\nclassifying them by **storage capacity, service scope, technology adoption, and industry focus**.\nA detailed **Ecosystem Intelligence Database** was built to map each vendor\u2019s operational footprint,\nclient portfolio, and infrastructure readiness.\n\n### 2. Feasibility & KPI Alignment Assessment\n\nA shortlist of high-potential vendors underwent **feasibility and KPI alignment analysis** covering:\n* Cost per square meter\n* Inventory throughput efficiency\n* On-time delivery accuracy\n* Scalability potential\n* Technology integration (WMS/TMS readiness)\n\nThis benchmarking established **objective performance baselines** and revealed gaps in efficiency\nversus cost.\n\n### 3. Strategic Partner Selection Framework\n\nKen Research developed a **Decision-Support Matrix** integrating operational KPIs, pricing models,\nscalability scores, and risk profiles.\nFrom this analysis, **20+ strategic suppliers** were identified as capable of supporting future\nexpansion and cost optimization objectives.\n\n## Key Deliverables\n* Regional **Supplier Evaluation Dashboard**\n* **Warehousing Efficiency Benchmark Report** with KPI comparisons\n* **Decision-Support Matrix** for supplier selection\n* **Cost Optimization Framework** outlining potential savings and contract renegotiation levers\n\n## Results: The Measurable Impact\n* **50+ warehousing providers mapped** across Singapore and Malaysia.\n* **20+ strategic suppliers shortlisted** aligned with operational and growth needs.\n* **~20% reduction in warehousing costs** achieved through supplier consolidation and renegotiation\n(within the first year of implementation).\n* **Improved cost predictability, service reliability, and scalability** across regional operations.\n\nAccording to the client\u2019s Project Head:\n\n> \u201cKen Research\u2019s benchmarking approach helped us redesign our warehousing partnerships based on\n> quantifiable performance metrics rather than legacy contracts. The outcome was measurable\n> efficiency gains and greater agility across our supply chain.\u201d\n\n## The Strategic Outcome\n\nThrough this engagement, the client successfully transformed its warehousing model from **fragmented\nvendor management to a data-driven, performance-optimized supplier network**.\nThe project delivered long-term strategic value by:\n* Institutionalizing **performance-based supplier governance**\n* Enhancing **cross-border operational visibility**\n* Enabling **cost-efficient scalability** across Southeast Asia\n\nKen Research\u2019s structured benchmarking approach empowered the leadership team to **shift procurement\nfrom reactive contracting to strategic supply chain management**, reinforcing the company\u2019s\noperational resilience and competitive edge.\n\n## Related tags\n\nLogistics\n\nLogistics and Shipping\n\nAutomotive, Transportation and Warehousing\n\n### Get started\n\nWe've helped companies around the world future-proof\ntheir businesses - and we can do the same for you.\n\nGet started\n\n[1]: /procurement-research\n[2]: /expert-panel\n[3]: /about-us\n[4]: /careers#leadership\n[5]: /careers\n[6]: /contact-us\n[7]: /terms-and-conditions#privacyPolicy\n[8]: /\n[9]: /report-store\n[10]: /report-store\n[11]: /report-store#Segements\n[12]: /report-store#beseSellingReports\n[13]: /report-store#latestInsights\n[14]: /report-store\n[15]: /report-store?reportTypes=global-market-research-reports\n[16]: /country-reports\n[17]: /report-store?reportTypes=competition_benchmarking\n[18]: /custom-form\n[19]: /talk-to-us\n[20]: /report-store\n[21]: /report-store?industry=agriculture-animal-care-market\n[22]: /report-store?industry=automotive-transportation-and-warehousing-market\n[23]: /report-store?industry=banking-financial-services-and-insurance-market\n[24]: /report-store?industry=consumer-produc"
