 PMC Full-Text Archive Search in PMC [Search]\n* [ Journal List ][9]\n\nPubMed Central^{\u00ae} (PMC) is a free full-text archive of biomedical and life sciences journal\nliterature at the U.S. National Institutes of Health's National Library of Medicine (NIH/NLM)\n* ## [ About PMC ][10]\n  \n  Discover a digital archive of scholarly articles, spanning centuries of scientific research.\n* ## [ User Guide ][11]\n  \n  Learn how to find and read articles of interest to you.\n* ## [ Collections ][12]\n  \n  Browse the PMC Journal List or learn about some of PMC's unique collections.\n* ## [ For Authors ][13]\n  \n  Navigate the PMC submission methods to comply with a funder mandate, expand access, and ensure\n  preservation.\n* ## [ For Publishers ][14]\n  \n  Learn about deposit options for journals and publishers and the PMC selection process.\n* ## [ For Developers ][15]\n  \n  Find tools for bulk download, text mining, and other machine analysis.\n\n## 12.1 million articles are archived in PMC.\n\nContent provided in part by:\n* 3025\n  Full Participation Journals\n  \n  Journals deposit the complete contents of each issue or volume.\n* 249\n  NIH Portfolio Journals\n  \n  Journals deposit all NIH-funded articles as defined by the NIH Public Access Policy.\n* 44\n  Selective Deposit Programs\n  \n  Publisher deposits a subset of articles from a collection of journals.\n\n## New in PMC\n\nApril 13, 2026\n\n### [Update on PMC Article Dataset Distribution Changes][16]\n\nAs announced on February 12, major changes to PMC's Article Dataset Distribution Services are\nunderway. Please note the follow\u2026\n\nFeb. 12, 2026\n\n### [Changes to PMC Article Dataset Distribution Services Coming in 2026][17]\n\nThe National Center for Biotechnology Information (NCBI) will be making major changes to PMC's\nArticle Dataset Distribution Se\u2026\n\nhighlights\n\n### [Updated Full-Text Search Now Available][18]\n\n[Screenshot showing a search results webpage in PMC]\n\nNCBI has updated the PubMed Central (PMC) full-text search functionality and user experience.\n\n[Read More][19]\nFollow NCBI\n[ NCBI on X (formerly known as Twitter) ][20] [ NCBI on Facebook ][21] [ NCBI on LinkedIn ][22] [\nNCBI on GitHub ][23] [ NCBI RSS feed ][24]\n\nConnect with NLM\n\n[ NLM on X (formerly known as Twitter) ][25] [ NLM on Facebook ][26] [ NLM on YouTube ][27]\n\n[National Library of Medicine\n8600 Rockville Pike\nBethesda, MD 20894][28]\n* [ Web Policies ][29]\n* [ FOIA ][30]\n* [ HHS Vulnerability Disclosure ][31]\n* [ Help ][32]\n* [ Accessibility ][33]\n* [ Careers ][34]\n* [ NLM ][35]\n* [ NIH ][36]\n* [ HHS ][37]\n* [ USA.gov ][38]\n\n[1]: #main-content\n[2]: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/\n[3]: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/myncbi/\n[4]: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/myncbi/collections/bibliography/\n[5]: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/account/settings/\n[6]: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/myncbi/\n[7]: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/myncbi/collections/bibliography/\n[8]: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/account/settings/\n[9]: /journals/\n[10]: /about/intro/\n[11]: /about/userguide/\n[12]: /about/collections/\n[13]: /about/submission-methods/\n[14]: /pub/pubinfo/\n[15]: /tools/developers/\n[16]: /about/new-in-pmc/#2026-04-13\n[17]: /about/new-in-pmc/#2026-02-12\n[18]: about/new-in-pmc/#2025-09-09\n[19]: about/new-in-pmc/#2025-09-09\n[20]: https://twitter.com/ncbi\n[21]: https://www.facebook.com/ncbi.nlm\n[22]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/ncbinlm\n[23]: https://github.com/ncbi\n[24]: https://ncbiinsights.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/\n[25]: https://twitter.com/nlm_nih\n[26]: https://www.facebook.com/nationallibraryofmedicine\n[27]: https://www.youtube.com/user/NLMNIH\n[28]: https://www.google.com/maps/place/8600+Rockville+Pike,+Bethesda,+MD+20894/%4038.9959508,      \n       -77.101021,17z/data%3D!3m1!4b1!4m5!3m4!1s0x89b7c95e25765ddb%3A0x19156f88b27635b8!8m2!3d38.995\n9508!             4d-77.0988323\n[29]: https://www.nlm.nih.gov/web_policies.html\n[30]: https://www.nih