*Friday 2nd January. **\n\nWe use Royal Mail and DPD to deliver across the UK.\n* Free UK Delivery on orders over \u00a345\n* Standard Delivery (Royal Mail Tracked): \u00a33.99 on orders under \u00a345.\n* Next Day Delivery (DPD): \u00a35.99.\n\nYou have a full 60 days from the date of purchase to try out our foods and supplements. If you find\nyourself not completely satisfied within this period, simply reach out to our customer service team\nand let them know.\n\n**\u2713 **HASSLE-FREE RETURNS\n\n**\u2713 **RISK-FREE ONLINE PURCHASES\n\n**\u2713 **FULL REFUND ON RETURN OF GOODS\n\nMore detail on our 60-day money-back guarantee can be found [here][67].\n\n[Klarna] [American Express] [Apple Pay] [PayPal] [Shop Pay] [Visa]\nIngredients & Nutritional Label ][68] [\nSuggested Serving Size ][69]\nSubscribe & Save 10% 60-Day Money Back Guarantee Subscribe & Save 10% 60-Day Money Back Guarantee\nSubscribe & Save 10% 60-Day Money Back Guarantee Subscribe & Save 10% 60-Day Money Back Guarantee\nSubscribe & Save 10% 60-Day Money Back Guarantee Subscribe & Save 10% 60-Day Money Back Guarantee\nSubscribe & Save 10% 60-Day Money Back Guarantee Subscribe & Save 10% 60-Day Money Back Guarantee\nSubscribe & Save 10% 60-Day Money Back Guarantee\n\n## What to expect over time\n* ### Week 1\n\nFeel the difference in your digestion. Gentle on the stomach and naturally soothing for your gut.\n* ### Month 1\n\nNotice improved energy and focus, with reduced bloating and a greater feeling of fullness between\nmeals.\n* ### Month 2-3\n\nExperience stronger hair and nails, smoother skin, and easier post-workout recovery thanks to\nsteady collagen and protein support.\n* ### Month 3-6\n\nEnjoy lasting benefits: resilient joints, healthy gut balance, and visible radiance that shows\nfrom the inside out.\n\n## Bone Broth Showdown\n\n[Grass Fed Beef Bone Broth] Our Bone Broth\nThe Other Guys\nProtein Content\n15g per serving\nMinimal\nConvenience\nTravel-friendly, powder format\nNot easily portable\nPrice Per Serve\n\u00a31.35 per serving\n\u00a34+ per serving\nSustainability\nGrass fed European cattle\nUnknown sourcing\nStorage\nShelf-stable, easily stored\nNeeds refrigeration, spoils quickly\n[Try Now ][70]\n\nLab tested for purity\n\n## Only real ingredients\n\nNo unnecessary fillers, bulkers or chemical preservatives! Other brands are not the same.\n\n[Ingredients & Nutritional Label][71]\n[Grass Fed Beef Bone Broth] Ingredients\n\nBeef Bone Broth, Bovine Collagen, Carrot, Pink Himalayan Salt, Beef Extract, Tomato, Onion,\nRosemary, Garlic, Sage, Black Pepper\n\n## Traditional nourishment, modern convenience\n\n### Traditional bone broth, made easy\n\nClassic bone broth takes hours of simmering. Ours delivers the same level of ancestral nutrition\nwithout the hours of preparation and is made from premium beef bones sourced from grass fed European\ncattle, including marrow, knuckle, and connective tissue-rich cuts, selected for their nutrient\ndensity. Alongside vegetables and herbs, these bones are made into a rich, glossy broth packed with\ncollagen, amino acids, and minerals. We then gently dry it into a powder to create a simple,\nnutritious and ready-to-use format. Just add hot water and whisk to transform the powder into rich,\nnourishing broth.\n\n### More than just a drink\n\nYes, you can sip it from a mug. But our bone broth powder works brilliantly in cooking, too. You can\nmake it into a paste that dissolves straight into hot dishes, adding 15g of protein per serving to\nwhatever you're making. Make gravies without stock cubes. Add depth to sauces and casseroles. Boost\nstews and soups with a hit of real nutrition. Since it's a powder, you control exactly how much you\nuse. No waste from half-empty liquid packs going off in the fridge. Just keep it in your cupboard\nand use it whenever you need it.\n\n### Bovear-free, non-GMO and no artificial ingredients\n\nBovaer is a synthetic feed additive given to cattle. Our cattle don't get any. They graze on\nnutrient-rich European pastures, eating grass as nature intended. No GMO feed either. We also test\nfor heavy metals and work only with farms that meet high welfare standards. While most broths are\nbulked out with yeast extracts and \"natural flavours\", ours keeps it clean and simple. No MSG, no\nartificial flavour enhancers, no chemical preservatives.\n\nWatch Video\n][72]\n\nHi, we\u2019re Amy and Jeff, co-founders of Hunter & Gather, an ancestrally inspired lifestyle brand.\n\nAfter our own health journeys led us to a more natural way of living, we launched Hunter & Gather in\n2017. Eight years on, we\u2019re proud to have supported hundreds of thousands of people on their path to\nbetter health.\n\n### Modern life moves quickly, and it's easy to lose sight of what your body truly needs.\n\nWe\u2019re here to help you reconnect, with real food, practical guidance and the tools you need to\nthrive.\n\n[Our Story][73]\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions\n\nWhat are the benefits of drinking bone broth?\n\nDrinking bone broth supports gut health and aids digestion due to its high glutamine and glycine\ncontent, which helps to restore the gut lining. It also provides essential amino acids that promote\nhealthy skin, hair, and nails while supporting joint mobility.\n\nWhat does \"grass fed\" mean in relation to beef bone broth?\n\nGrass fed means that the bones are sourced from cattle that have spent their lives grazing on\nnatural pastures rather than being fed grains. This results in a higher quality, more nutrient-dense\nbroth that is free from the hormones and antibiotics often found in intensive farming\n\nWhat nutrients are found in bone broth?\n\nThis broth is rich in collagen and amino acids like glycine and glutamine that aid the maintenance\nof healthy joints, muscle growth and skin hydration.\n\nHow can I use bone broth?\n\nYou can enjoy it as a nourishing warm drink by simply mixing it with hot water, or use it as a base\nfor soups, stews, and sauces. It is also an excellent way to add extra protein and depth of flavour\nto dishes like risotto or mashed vegetables.\n\nHow long does bone broth last, and how should it be stored?\n\nOur powdered bone broth is shelf-stable and should be stored in a cool, dark place, where it will\nlast until the best-before date indicated on the packaging.\n\n[ Read all FAQs Here ][74]\n\n## CUSTOMER REVIEWS\n\n## Return Policy\n\nWe guarantee that our goods are of high quality. You must inspect the goods and notify us promptly\nin writing or by phone of any dissatisfaction with your order. We will fully refund the price of any\ngoods that do not meet your reasonable satisfaction or arrange for the delivery of replacement\ngoods, provided that you notify us within 30 days of delivery of the goods.\n\nView our full [terms of service][75]\n\n## Save on your first order\n\n### Shop\n* [Shop All][76]\n* [Collagen][77]\n* [Mayonnaise][78]\n* [Sauces][79]\n* [Electrolytes][80]\n* [Bone Broth][81]\n* [Oils & Fats][82]\n* [Supplements][83]\n* [Coffee][84]\n* [Julia's Favourites][85]\n\n### Lifestyle\n* [Refined Sugar free][86]\n* [Gluten Free][87]\n* [Keto][88]\n* [Paleo][89]\n* [Carnivore][90]\n* [Dairy Free][91]\n\n### Learn\n* [Articles][92]\n* [Recipes][93]\n* [Pillar Articles][94]\n* [eBook Library][95]\n* [About Us][96]\n* [Investors][97]\n\n### Store\n* [Account][98]\n* [Help][99]\n* [Contact Us][100]\n* [Rewards][101]\n* [Delivery Info][102]\n* [Stockist Log In][103]\n* [Klarna Payments][104]\n* [B-Corp][105]\n* [Money Back Guarantee][106]\n* [Subscription T&Cs][107]\n* [Easter Bank Holiday Information ][108]\n\n### Socials\n\n\u00a9 2026 Hunter & Gather.\n\n[Privacy Policy][109] [Cookies][110] [Sitemap][111]\n* [Klarna]\n* [American Express]\n* [Apple Pay]\n* [Bancontact"
