        "crawl_text": "Fairoils EPZ Limited Fair Trade Certified Africa Europe Fairtrade Organic Fair Trade Certified ISO9001 Certified FSSC22000 Certified Ethical sourcing Support for local farmers High-quality production standards Ethical sourcing from small-scale farmers Integrated supply chain management High-quality natural oils Fair Trade Standards ISO Quality Standards Unit 2, Capital Industrial Park, Export Processing zone, Athi River, Kenya \u2013 00204 Avenue de l\u2019Innovation 5, 7822 Ghislenghien, Belgium Athi River, Kenya Thika, Kenya Lunga Lunga, Kenya Mara, Kenya Mt Kenya, Kenya Nosy Be, Madagascar Mananjary, Madagascar Ochero, Uganda Kenya Madagascar Tanzania Uganda Belgium Kenya Madagascar Athi River, Kenya Africa Europe Fairoils supports over 12,137 small scale farmers in Africa. Fairoils employs 389 people based in Africa. Sustainable and ethical production of essential and vegetable oils. Strengthening local communities through fair trade practices. Dependence on agricultural output and climate conditions. Market competition from other essential oil producers. Expansion into new markets in Europe and beyond. Increasing demand for ethically sourced products. Fairoils is positioned as a leader in ethical essential and vegetable oil production, focusing on sustainability and community support. Growing global demand for natural and organic products. Increased consumer awareness of ethical sourcing. Sustainable, Ethical Essential Oils &amp; Vegetable Oils | Fairoils\n\nSkip to content\n\nHome\n\nPure, natural oils. Ethically produced.\n\nFairoils leads the way in the responsible and ethical production of quality essential and vegetable oils. Our partnerships support local growers and strengthen communities in Africa.\n\nGet in touch\n\nLearn about our impact\n\nWe believe that responsible business makes the world a better place.\n\nAt the heart of Fairoils is the determination to help farmers and communities in Africa.\nFrom seed through to supply, we manage every step of the production process. This stewardship allows us to embed ethics and quality at every stage.\nThe result is pure, natural oils, produced to the highest ethical standards.\n\nFairoils embraces the United Nations\u2019 Sustainable Development Goals as a clear blueprint for the prosperity of people and our planet. We\u2019re advancing these goals across our operations.\u200b\n\nFind out how\n\nLocal cooperatives with real reach.\n\nWe know what&#8217;s possible when people work together, bonded by a common goal. Fairoils unites the efforts of small-scale growers, commercial farms and local processing facilities to make a difference.\n\nSmall scale grower projects\n\nOur growers work as a collective, gaining a secure, additional income.\n\nLearn about our impact\n\nCommercial farms\n\nCommercial farms help secure supply and demonstrate co-commitment.\nLearn about how we farm\n\nProcessing facilities\n\nCrops are processed in state-of-the-art processing facilities in Kenya &amp; Madagascar.\nLearn about processing\n\nOur projects in Africa\n\nEach of our projects is shaped by the local community. Through careful design, we create meaningful impact at every step.\n\nLearn about our impact\n\nSkills and income for farmers.\n\nOur grower projects establish a farming cooperative between small-scale farmers. We foster the skills farmers need to successfully grow crops for essential and vegetable oils. We also make resources more accessible\u2014seed, organic fertiliser, equipment and education.\nAnd we help local farmers find new ways to work together, so they can collectively reach new markets. Fairoils ensures that farmers gain secure, reliable income. Our farmers are paid quickly, receiving a fair and transparent price for their crop.\n\nOur fair trade commitment\n\nOUR PROJECTS\n\nMadagascar\n\nOur grower projects establish a farming cooperative between small-scale farmers. We foster the skills farmers need to successfully grow crops for essential and vegetable oils. We also make resources more accessible\u2014seed, organic fertiliser, equipment and education.\nAnd we help local farmers find new ways to work together, so they can collectively reach new markets. Fairoils ensures that farmers gain secure, reliable income. Our farmers are paid quickly, receiving a fair and transparent price for their crop.\n\nOver 50 pure, natural oils.\n\nWe\u2019re proud to supply essential and vegetable oils to world-leading brands that share our commitment to ethical production. We produce oils of the highest quality and purity.\nOur innovative business model allows us to supply large volumes of vegetable and essential oils, year round.\n\nExplore our full range of oils\n\nOur quality assurance\n\nEthical out-\ngrower projects\n\n12,137\n\nSmall scale farmers\nworking with Fairoils\n\n389\n\nFairoils employees\nbased in Africa\n\nFarming\nfor good.\n\nFairoils is committed to producing the highest quality natural oils for the cosmetic and personal care industry, with a particular emphasis\non products with an ethical farming story.\n\nView Projects\n\nWatch our video\n\nWe see a bright future for Africa\n\nPartner with us to strengthen local communities.\n\nGet in touch\n\nLearn about our impact\n\nOur key oils\n\nCurrent projects\n\nContact us\n\nOur key oils\n\nYlang ylang\nFresh ginger\nTea tree\nRose geranium\nCinnamon bark\n\nClove bud\nEucalyptus citriodora\nAvocado\nMacadamia nut\nSesame\n\nCurrent projects\n\nLunga Lunga &#8211; Kenyan Coast\n\nMt Kenya &#8211; Kenyan Highlands\n\nNosy Be &#8211; Madagascar North\n\nMananjary &#8211; Madagascar South\n\nMara &#8211; Western Kenya\n\nThika &#8211; Central Kenya\n\nLunga Lunga &#8211; Kenyan Coast\n\nMt Kenya &#8211; Kenyan Highlands\n\nNosy Be &#8211; Madagascar North\n\nMananjary &#8211; Madagascar South\n\nMara &#8211; Western Kenya\n\nThika &#8211; Central Kenya\n\nContact us\n\nDistribution\nFairoils SRL\nAvenue de l\u2019Innovation 5\n7822 Ghislenghien &#8211; Belgium\nE: info@fairoils.com\nP: + 32 68 28 43 16\n\n\u00a9 2026 Fairoils Limited | Web design by Excite Media | Fairoils Terms and Conditions of sale\n\nFacebook\n\nLinkedin [Skip to content][1]\n\n# Contact\n\n## Contact\n\n### Natural Oils.\n### Ethical Partnerships.\n\nHead Office\n\nFairoils EPZ Limited\n\nUnit 2, Capital Industrial Park\n\nExport Processing zone\n\nAthi River\n\nKenya \u2013 00204\n\nE: info@fairoils.com\n\nDistribution\n\nAvenue de I\u2019Innovation 5\n7822 Ghislenghien\nBelgium\nP: +32 68 28 43 16\n\n[ Explore our full range of oils ][2]\n\n##### In-Cosmetics New Products\n\n[ Muyao product data sheet ][3]\n[ Moringa oil product data sheet ][4]\nFairoils has a whole team of people ready to help you with your requirements. We can assist you\nwith:\n\n* Essential and vegetable oil samples\n* Packaging and shipping information\n* Technical and quality assurance documents\n* Sales advice and marketing assistance\n* Information on our grower projects and how you can get involved\n* Certification information (Fairtrade, organic, food-grade etc)\n\n##### Get in touch\n\n\"*\" indicates required fields\n\nX/Twitter\nThis field is for validation purposes and should be left unchanged.\nFirst name*\nLast name*\nEmail*\nPhone number*\nCompany name\nCompany role\nHow can we help?*\nCAPTCHA\n\n## We see a bright future for Africa\n\nPartner with us to strengthen local communities.\n\n[ Get in touch ][5]\n[ Learn about our impact ][6]\n\n###### Our key oils\n\n###### Current projects\n\n###### [Contact us][7]\n\n###### Our key oils\n\n[Ylang ylang][8]\n[Fresh ginger][9]\n[Tea tree][10]\n[Rose geranium][11]\n[Cinnamon bark][12]\n[Clove bud][13]\n[Eucalyptus citriodora][14]\n[Avocado][15]\n[Macadamia nut][16]\n[Sesame][17]\n\n###### Current projects\n* [Lunga Lunga \u2013 Kenyan Coast][18]\n* [Mt Kenya \u2013 Kenyan Highlands][19]\n* [Nosy Be \u2013 Madagascar North][20]\n* [Mananjary \u2013 Madagascar South][21]\n* [Mara \u2013 Western Kenya][22]\n* [Thika