          {
            "url": "https://www.fairoils.com/products/ylang-ylang/",
            "text": "[Skip to content][1]\n\n## Ylang ylang\n\nCananga odorata\n\n[Home][2] / [Products][3] / Ylang ylang\n\n[DSC03640]\n[DSCF8925]\n[IMG_0387]\n[IMG_0728]\n[ylang flower (4)]\n\nWith its rich, heady fragrance, ylang ylang is widely considered the \u2018flower of flowers\u2019. Its\npotential as a fragrance was noted in the nineteenth century by French perfumers.\n\nYlang ylang oil is distilled from the yellow, star-shaped flowers of the ylang ylang tree. This\nplant is endemic to the lush, tropical rainforests of Indonesia and the Philippines.\n\nYlang ylang trees have been cultivated for centuries on the islands off the east coast of Africa,\nnamely The Comores, Reunion and Nosy Be (Madagascar).\n\nFairoils grows ylang ylang across two key projects\u2014one on Nosy Be, an island off the north coast of\nMadagascar, and one on the south coast of Kenya. Ylang Ylang is also planted at the Fairoils\nLandless project, in the middle of the Lunga Lunga outgrowers group.\n\n[Request a Sample & Technical Specifications][4]\n\n#### Ylang ylang production and extraction\n\nThe ylang ylang tree belongs to the Annonaceae family, which is the largest group within the\nmagnolia species. This fast-growing tree grows up to 35 metres and requires pruning and training to\nkeep flowers low and harvestable from the ground.\n\nYlang ylang flowers all year round. Across our farms, the flowers are picked each day, early in the\nmorning. Harvesting before sunrise helps preserve the blossoming flowers from the heat of the day.\n\nYlang ylang flowers can only be picked by hand, once the flowers have reached the right maturity.\nThis skill is traditionally undertaken by the females within our partnering African communities.\nOften, you can hear collectors singing together during the early morning harvests.\n\nYlang ylang flowers are hydro distilled for five hours in purpose-built, stainless steel\ndistillation units. We produce four oil fractions (ylang ylang extra, ylang ylang grade 1, ylang\nylang grade 2 and ylang ylang grade 3) and a complete oil (containing all fractions) within our\nprocessing facilities.\n\nYlang ylang extra and first grade are considered the highest quality fractions and are used in\nperfume-grade fragrance products. These highest-grade fractions are captured during the early stages\nof distillation, while the lower, heavier fractions are extracted later in the distillation process.\nWe also produce a complete oil which contains all fractions.\n\n###### Fairoils can produce and supply up to 20 metric tonnes of ylang ylang oil per year.\n* Ethically Sourced\n* Organic\n* Pure & Natural\n* Hydro Distilled\n* Essential Oil\n* Out Grower Grown\n* Commercially Grown\n\n#### Grown at our projects\n\n#### [Lunga Lunga Project][5]\n\nKenyan Coast\n\n#### [Nosy Be Project][6]\n\nMadagascar North\n\n## Pure and Natural.\n\nWork with us to source pure, natural oils produced to the highest ethical standards.\n\n[ Get in touch ][7]\n[ Learn about our impact ][8]\n\n###### Our key oils\n\n###### Current projects\n\n###### [Contact us][9]\n\n###### Our key oils\n\n[Ylang ylang][10]\n[Fresh ginger][11]\n[Tea tree][12]\n[Rose geranium][13]\n[Cinnamon bark][14]\n[Clove bud][15]\n[Eucalyptus citriodora][16]\n[Avocado][17]\n[Macadamia nut][18]\n[Sesame][19]\n\n###### Current projects\n* [Lunga Lunga \u2013 Kenyan Coast][20]\n* [Mt Kenya \u2013 Kenyan Highlands][21]\n* [Nosy Be \u2013 Madagascar North][22]\n* [Mananjary \u2013 Madagascar South][23]\n* [Mara \u2013 Western Kenya][24]\n* [Thika \u2013 Central Kenya][25]\n* [Lunga Lunga \u2013 Kenyan Coast][26]\n* [Mt Kenya \u2013 Kenyan Highlands][27]\n* [Nosy Be \u2013 Madagascar North][28]\n* [Mananjary \u2013 Madagascar South][29]\n* [Mara \u2013 Western Kenya][30]\n* [Thika \u2013 Central Kenya][31]\n\n###### Contact us\n\nDistribution\nFairoils SRL\nAvenue de l\u2019Innovation 5\n7822 Ghislenghien \u2013 Belgium\nE: info@fairoils.com\nP: + 32 68 28 43 16\n\n\u00a9 2026 Fairoils Limited | [Web design][32] by Excite Media | [Fairoils Terms and Conditions of\nsale][33]\n\n[ Facebook ][34] [ Linkedin ][35]\n[ ][36]\n\n[1]: #content\n[2]: https://fairoils.com/\n[3]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/\n[4]: https://www.fairoils.com/contact/\n[5]: https://fairoils.com/projects/kenyan-coast-lunga-lunga-project/\n[6]: https://fairoils.com/projects/madagascar/\n[7]: https://www.fairoils.com/contact/\n[8]: https://www.fairoils.com/our-impact/\n[9]: /contact\n[10]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/ylang-ylang/\n[11]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/ginger/\n[12]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/tea-tree/\n[13]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/rose-geranium/\n[14]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/cinnamon-bark/\n[15]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/clove-bud/\n[16]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/eucalyptus-citriodora/\n[17]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/avocado/\n[18]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/macadamia-nut/\n[19]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/sesame-oil/\n[20]: https://fairoils.com/projects/kenyan-coast-lunga-lunga-project/\n[21]: https://fairoils.com/projects/mount-kenya/\n[22]: https://fairoils.com/projects/madagascar/\n[23]: https://fairoils.com/projects/madagascar-south-mananjary-project/\n[24]: https://fairoils.com/projects/mara-location/\n[25]: https://fairoils.com/projects/thika-project/\n[26]: https://fairoils.com/projects/kenyan-coast-lunga-lunga-project/\n[27]: https://fairoils.com/projects/mount-kenya/\n[28]: https://fairoils.com/projects/madagascar/\n[29]: https://fairoils.com/projects/madagascar-south-mananjary-project/\n[30]: https://fairoils.com/projects/mara-location/\n[31]: https://fairoils.com/projects/thika-project/\n[32]: https://www.excitemedia.com.au/\n[33]: https://fairoils.com/wp-content/uploads/Fairoils-Terms-and-Conditions-of-Sale_V1.pdf\n[34]: https://www.facebook.com/Fairoils/\n[35]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/fairoils/\n[36]: #top"
