            "url": "https://fairoils.com/about",
            "text": "[Skip to content][1]\n\n# Our purpose\n\n## Our purpose\n\nCananga odorata\n\n### At Fairoils, we responsibly produce pure, natural oils.\n\nFairoils partners with thousands of small-scale farmers in Africa, ensuring they receive a fair,\nreliable and transparent price for their crops.\n\nOur business model benefits everyone involved\u2014from local growers and their families to the clients\nwho share our values.\n\nTogether, we\u2019re strengthening the livelihood of entire communities.\n\n##### We\u2019ve built an integrated supply chain, managing a production process that begins at the farm.\n##### And we embed quality and ethical standards every step of the way.\n\n### We grow alongside our farmers.\n\nFairoils was founded in 2013 by founded by Campbell Walter & Wayne Barratt, after working with\ncommunities to produce natural oils for more than two decades. In the beginning, our crops were\ngrown solely on small-scale farms in Kenya and Madagascar. In 2017, we bought our first Fairoils\nfarm, as part of our long-term commitment to the region. Today, we offer an extensive selection of\n100% pure essential and vegetable oils, derived from optimum growing and processing conditions.\n\n### We\u2019re driven to make a positive change.\n\nFairoils employs a passionate team, working in different countries throughout the world. Our people\nare experts in their fields, from agronomy to industrial chemistry and quality assurance.\n\nFairoils\u2019 diverse team speaks many different languages\u2014Swahili, French, Flemish, German, Italian,\nEnglish and Japanese\u2014but we all share a commitment to improving lives and communities.\n\nOur team members have varied industry experiences, which helps us better meet the needs of the\ncommunities we work with.\n\n[ Meet our team ][2]\n\n### We lead with our values.\n\nWe are proud to be suppliers of both certified organic and Fairtrade oils.\n\nWe build strong trade connections to help people out of poverty.\n\nOur work culture prioritises people over profit.\n\nWe uphold the highest industry standards for quality and traceability.\n\nOur oils are high quality, natural and 100% pure.\n\nConducting business ethically is embedded in everything we do.\n\n### Meet the Fairoils group.\n\nThe Fairoils group brings together four companies, operating in different countries.\n\nFairoils EPZ and Fairoils SPL lead our production and distribution. Kutoka Ardhini and Fairoils\nMadagascar are focused on farming, processing and working directly with small-scale farmers.\n\n##### Fairoils EPZ Ltd (Kenya)\n\n##### Fairoils SPL (Belgium)\n\n##### Kutoka Ardhini Ltd (Kenya)\n\n##### Fairoils Madagascar SPL\n\n## Building communities.\n\nPartner with us to strengthen local communities.\n\n[ Get in touch ][3]\n[ Learn about our impact ][4]\n\n###### Our key oils\n\n###### Current projects\n\n###### [Contact us][5]\n\n###### Our key oils\n\n[Ylang ylang][6]\n[Fresh ginger][7]\n[Tea tree][8]\n[Rose geranium][9]\n[Cinnamon bark][10]\n[Clove bud][11]\n[Eucalyptus citriodora][12]\n[Avocado][13]\n[Macadamia nut][14]\n[Sesame][15]\n\n###### Current projects\n* [Lunga Lunga \u2013 Kenyan Coast][16]\n* [Mt Kenya \u2013 Kenyan Highlands][17]\n* [Nosy Be \u2013 Madagascar North][18]\n* [Mananjary \u2013 Madagascar South][19]\n* [Mara \u2013 Western Kenya][20]\n* [Thika \u2013 Central Kenya][21]\n* [Lunga Lunga \u2013 Kenyan Coast][22]\n* [Mt Kenya \u2013 Kenyan Highlands][23]\n* [Nosy Be \u2013 Madagascar North][24]\n* [Mananjary \u2013 Madagascar South][25]\n* [Mara \u2013 Western Kenya][26]\n* [Thika \u2013 Central Kenya][27]\n\n###### Contact us\n\nDistribution\nFairoils SRL\nAvenue de l\u2019Innovation 5\n7822 Ghislenghien \u2013 Belgium\nE: info@fairoils.com\nP: + 32 68 28 43 16\n\n\u00a9 2026 Fairoils Limited | [Web design][28] by Excite Media | [Fairoils Terms and Conditions of\nsale][29]\n\n[ Facebook ][30] [ Linkedin ][31]\n[ ][32]\n\n[1]: #content\n[2]: https://www.fairoils.com/meet-our-team/\n[3]: https://www.fairoils.com/contact/\n[4]: https://www.fairoils.com/our-impact/\n[5]: /contact\n[6]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/ylang-ylang/\n[7]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/ginger/\n[8]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/tea-tree/\n[9]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/rose-geranium/\n[10]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/cinnamon-bark/\n[11]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/clove-bud/\n[12]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/eucalyptus-citriodora/\n[13]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/avocado/\n[14]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/macadamia-nut/\n[15]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/sesame-oil/\n[16]: https://fairoils.com/projects/kenyan-coast-lunga-lunga-project/\n[17]: https://fairoils.com/projects/mount-kenya/\n[18]: https://fairoils.com/projects/madagascar/\n[19]: https://fairoils.com/projects/madagascar-south-mananjary-project/\n[20]: https://fairoils.com/projects/mara-location/\n[21]: https://fairoils.com/projects/thika-project/\n[22]: https://fairoils.com/projects/kenyan-coast-lunga-lunga-project/\n[23]: https://fairoils.com/projects/mount-kenya/\n[24]: https://fairoils.com/projects/madagascar/\n[25]: https://fairoils.com/projects/madagascar-south-mananjary-project/\n[26]: https://fairoils.com/projects/mara-location/\n[27]: https://fairoils.com/projects/thika-project/\n[28]: https://www.excitemedia.com.au/\n[29]: https://fairoils.com/wp-content/uploads/Fairoils-Terms-and-Conditions-of-Sale_V1.pdf\n[30]: https://www.facebook.com/Fairoils/\n[31]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/fairoils/\n[32]: #top"
