354]\n* [ Whole & Cut ][355]\n* [ Powder ][356]\n* [ Boosters ][357]\n* [ Protein Powders ][358]\n* [ Greens Powder ][359]\n* [ Fruit Powders ][360]\n* [ Coffee ][361]\n* [ Whole Bean ][362]\n* [ Instant ][363]\n* [ Tea ][364]\n* [ Leaf ][365]\n* [ Powder ][366]\n* [ Black ][367]\n* [ Green ][368]\n* [ Blends ][369]\n* [ Mushrooms ][370]\n* [ Whole & Cut ][371]\n* [ Powder ][372]\n* [ Herbal Botanicals & Spices ][373]\n* [ Whole ][374]\n* [ Cut ][375]\n* [ Powder ][376]\n* [ Extracts ][377]\n* [ Seaweeds ][378]\n* [ Whole & Flakes ][379]\n* [ Powder & Tablets ][380]\n* [ Noodle ][381]\n* [ Toasted ][382]\n* [ Blends ][383]\n* [ Bath & Body ][384]\n* [ Butter & Liquids ][385]\n* [ Clays ][386]\n* [ Bee Products ][387]\n* [ Packaging ][388]\n* [ hello@omfoods.com ][389]\n* [ Login ][390] / [ Register ][391]\nWe've sent you an email with a link to update your password.\n\n### Login\n\nPlease enter your e-mail and password:\n\nEmail\nPassword\n\n[Forgot your password?][392]\n\nLogin\n\nNew customer? [Register][393]\n\n### Reset your password\n\nWe will send you an email to reset your password.\n\nEmail\n\nSubmit\n\nBack to login\n[ [ORGANIC ELDERBERRY, whole] ][394]\n* [ Bestsellers ][395]\n* [ herbal-botanicals-spices ][396]\n* [ whole ][397]\n\n# ORGANIC ELDERBERRY, whole\n* Regular price $8.50\n* Sale -%\n\nSize :\n113g (1/4lb)\n$8.50 $74.56 / kg\n454g (1lb)\n$27.25 $59.89 / kg\n2.27kg (5lbs)\n$123.25 $54.27 / kg\n113g (1/4lb) - $8.50 CAD 454g (1lb) - $27.25 CAD 2.27kg (5lbs) - $123.25 CAD\nQuantity\nAdd to Cart Notify Availability\nWishlist\n\nInform when this item available ORGANIC ELDERBERRY, whole\n\nEmail\n[Description][398] [Ingredients & Origin][399] [Other][400] [ Reviews\n][401]\n\nWhole Elderberries are the small, bluish-black fruits of a flowering plant native to Europe,\nNorthern Africa, and Western Asia. The Elder plant produces large clusters of small, white flowers\nin the spring, followed by these unique berries. Elderberries have a long history of use in\ntraditional European preparations and contain naturally occurring vitamins A, B, and C.\n\nThese whole dried berries are incredibly versatile for both culinary and herbal applications. It is\nimportant to know that **Elderberries are always best consumed cooked**, as this process neutralizes\nthe astringency naturally present in the seeds and stems. They can be used to make **teas,\ntinctures, and traditional syrups**, or incorporated into recipes for cordials, wines, and even\nketchups. Dried berries can also be added to pancake or muffin batter for a flavour similar to, but\nless sweet than, blueberries. This historically valued, nutrient-containing whole berry is a staple\ningredient for year-round use.\n* Whole Elderberries (bluish-black fruit)\n* Native plant from Europe, Africa, and Western Asia\n* Contains naturally occurring vitamins A, B, and C\n* Best consumed cooked to neutralize astringency\n* Ideal for making syrups, teas, and tinctures\n* Can be used in wines, cordials, and baked goods\n\n**Ingredient:** Elderberry*.\n\n*Certified Organic by Pro-Cert\n\n**Origin:** Poland / Italy\n\n**Note:** This product is not intended for use as is, it is recommended to cook before consuming.\n\n**Storage:** Store in a cool, dry place, away from heat and moisture. Protect from direct sunlight.\n\n**Please note:** This product is not intended for use as is, it is recommended to cook before\nconsuming.\n\n**Disclaimer: **This information is for educational purposes only and has not been evaluated by the\nFDA or CFIA. It is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease. This product has\nbeen packaged in the same facility as peanuts, tree nuts, wheat, soy, and other potential allergens.\n\n## Customer Reviews\n\nBased on 33 reviews [Write a review][402]\n\n#### Your Cart\n\nItem(s): ****\nTotal: $0.00\n[View Cart][403] [Continue to delivery and payment][404]\n\n### Recently Viewed\n\nCustomer Reviews\n**4.9** Based on 46 Reviews\n5 \u2605\n91%\n4 