ble and essential ingredient in Italian and other\nMediterranean cuisines, prized for its deep flavour profile.\n\nThe whole leaves offer a slightly astringent, sweet, and pronounced piney flavour that is highly\nversatile in the kitchen. Rosemary is a source of **fiber, calcium, and iron**, making it a\nflavourful addition to your diet. The crushed leaves can be easily added to a wide variety of\nrecipes, including **potatoes, baked breads, soups, and savory sauces**. A whole twig can also be\nstored in vinegar to create a fragrant, flavoured infusion. This essential, whole Mediterranean herb\nis a staple for adding warmth and complexity to savory dishes.\n* Whole Rosemary Leaf (needle-like form)\n* Perennial herb from the mint family\n* Key ingredient in Italian and Mediterranean cuisine\n* Offers a sweet, piney, and slightly astringent flavour\n* Source of fiber, calcium, and iron\n* Excellent addition to potatoes, breads, soups, and sauces\n\n**Ingredient:** Rosemary* (Rosmarinus officinalis).\n\n*Certified Organic by Pro-Cert\n\n**Origin:** Morocco\n\n**Storage:** Store in a cool, dry place, away from heat and moisture. Protect from direct sunlight.\n\n**Disclaimer: **This information is for educational purposes only and has not been evaluated by the\nFDA or CFIA. It is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease. This product has\nbeen packaged in the same facility as peanuts, tree nuts, wheat, soy, and other potential allergens.\n\n## Customer Reviews\n\nBased on 8 reviews [Write a review][402]\n\n#### Your Cart\n\nItem(s): ****\nTotal: $0.00\n[View Cart][403] [Continue to delivery and payment][404]\n\n### Recently Viewed\n\nCustomer Reviews\n**5.0** Based on 8 Reviews\n5 \u2605\n100%\n4 \u2605\n3 \u2605\n2 \u2605\n1 \u2605\nCustomer Photos\nWrite a Review Ask a Question\n* Reviews\n* Questions\nWrite a review\nAuthor\nName\nEmail\nLocation\nRating\nRating\n[1][405] [2][406] [3][407] [4][408] [5][409]\nTitle of Review\nHow was your overall e