354]\n* [ Whole & Cut ][355]\n* [ Powder ][356]\n* [ Boosters ][357]\n* [ Protein Powders ][358]\n* [ Greens Powder ][359]\n* [ Fruit Powders ][360]\n* [ Coffee ][361]\n* [ Whole Bean ][362]\n* [ Instant ][363]\n* [ Tea ][364]\n* [ Leaf ][365]\n* [ Powder ][366]\n* [ Black ][367]\n* [ Green ][368]\n* [ Blends ][369]\n* [ Mushrooms ][370]\n* [ Whole & Cut ][371]\n* [ Powder ][372]\n* [ Herbal Botanicals & Spices ][373]\n* [ Whole ][374]\n* [ Cut ][375]\n* [ Powder ][376]\n* [ Extracts ][377]\n* [ Seaweeds ][378]\n* [ Whole & Flakes ][379]\n* [ Powder & Tablets ][380]\n* [ Noodle ][381]\n* [ Toasted ][382]\n* [ Blends ][383]\n* [ Bath & Body ][384]\n* [ Butter & Liquids ][385]\n* [ Clays ][386]\n* [ Bee Products ][387]\n* [ Packaging ][388]\n* [ hello@omfoods.com ][389]\n* [ Login ][390] / [ Register ][391]\nWe've sent you an email with a link to update your password.\n\n### Login\n\nPlease enter your e-mail and password:\n\nEmail\nPassword\n\n[Forgot your password?][392]\n\nLogin\n\nNew customer? [Register][393]\n\n### Reset your password\n\nWe will send you an email to reset your password.\n\nEmail\n\nSubmit\n\nBack to login\n[ [ORGANIC YERBA MATE, green] ][394]\n* [ Bestsellers ][395]\n* [ herbal-botanicals-spices ][396]\n* [ leaf ][397]\n\n# ORGANIC YERBA MATE, green\n* Regular price $4.25\n* Sale -%\n\nSize :\n113g (1/4lb)\n$4.25 $37.28 / kg\n454g (1lb)\n$14.25 $31.31 / kg\n2.27kg (5lb)\n$63.00 $27.74 / kg\n20kg (44lb)\n$398.25 $19.91 / kg\n113g (1/4lb) - $4.25 CAD 454g (1lb) - $14.25 CAD 2.27kg (5lb) - $63.00 CAD 20kg (44lb) - $398.25 CAD\nQuantity\nAdd to Cart Notify Availability\nWishlist\n\nInform when this item available ORGANIC YERBA MATE, green\n\nEmail\n[Description][398] [Ingredients & Origin][399] [Other][400] [ Reviews\n][401]\n\nGreen Yerba Mate is a celebrated cultural staple harvested from the subtropical regions of South\nAmerica. Our Mate is grown wild in Brazil among local flora and fauna, and it is harvested every two\nyears in alternating patches. This sustainable harvesting practice ensures a well-developed plant\nwith an excellent nutritional profile while preserving the area's natural ecosystem.\n\nThis traditional beverage is known for its refreshing, slightly bitter flavour and stimulating\nproperties. Yerba Mate has been consumed for centuries, first by the indigenous Guaran\u00ed and Quechua\npeople. Today, it remains a widely consumed staple across South America. Mate is a **well-balanced\nstimulant** with caffeine levels falling between those of green tea and coffee. It is commonly\nprepared as a tea, either hot or cold (terer\u00e9), and can be enjoyed with **milk, honey, lemon, or\nmint**. This culturally significant, invigorating leaf offers a traditional South American\nexperience.\n* Whole leaves from the Yerba Mate shrub\n* Sustainably harvested in Brazil from wild-grown plants\n* Harvested every two years in alternating patches\n* Historically consumed by Guaran\u00ed and Quechua people\n* Refreshing, bitter flavour with a well-balanced stimulant effect\n* Versatile preparation as hot tea or cold terer\u00e9\n\n**Ingredient:** Yerba Mate* (Ilex paraguariensis)\n\n*Certified Organic by Pro-Cert\n\n**Origin:** Brazil\n\n**Storage:** Store in a cool, dry place, away from heat and moisture. Protect from direct sunlight.\n\n**Disclaimer: **This information is for educational purposes only and has not been evaluated by the\nFDA or CFIA. It is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease. This product has\nbeen packaged in the same facility as peanuts, tree nuts, wheat, soy, and other potential allergens.\n\n## Customer Reviews\n\nBased on 7 reviews [Write a review][402]\n\n#### Your Cart\n\nItem(s): ****\nTotal: $0.00\n[View Cart][403] [Continue to delivery and payment][404]\n\n### Recently Viewed\n\nCustomer Reviews\n**4.9** Based on 13 Reviews\n5 \u2605\n92%\n4 \u2605\n3 \u2605\n2 \u2605\n1 \u2605\nCustomer Photos\nWrite a Review Ask a Question\n* Reviews\n* Questions\nWrite a review\nAuthor\nName\nEmail\nLocation\nRating\nRating\n[1][405] [2][406] [3][407] [4][408] [5][409]\nTitle of Review\nHow was your overall experience?\nQuestions Photos Upload\n\nThank you for submitting a review!\n\nYour input is very much appreciated. Share it with your friends so they can enjoy it too!\n\n[Facebook][410][Twitter][411]\nBe the first to review this item\nSort Most Recent Highest Rating Lowest Rating Most Helpful\nFilter Reviews:\nSort Most Recent Highest Rating Lowest Rating Most Helpful\nClear filter\nMore Filters\n01 Oct 2024\n**Marty K.**\nCanada\n\n### Excellent!\n\nGreat product! Very little dust and very tasty. "
