s **OMRI certified and aluminum free**.\n\nBaking soda\u2019s primary use in the kitchen is as a powerful leavening agent. When exposed to heat or\nacidic components in batters, it releases carbon dioxide gas, which causes dough and batter to\nexpand and results in a lighter texture. Sodium bicarbonate can be substituted for baking powder,\nprovided sufficient acid is added to the recipe. This versatile pantry staple has a slightly salty,\nalkaline taste and is not tested on animals.\n* Food Grade Baking Soda (Sodium Bicarbonate)\n* Pure and natural NaHCO3\n* Sourced from underground deposits in Colorado, USA\n* OMRI certified and aluminum free\n* Primary use as a leavening agent in baking\n* Releases carbon dioxide for a lighter texture\n\n**Ingredient: ** Sodium Bicarbonate (NaHCO3). OMRI certified, not tested on animals, aluminum free.\n\n**Origin:** United States\n\n**Storage:** Store in a cool, dry place, away from heat and moisture. Protect from direct sunlight.\n\n**Disclaimer: **This information is for educational purposes only and has not been evaluated by the\nFDA or CFIA. It is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease. This product has\nbeen packaged in the same facility as peanuts, tree nuts, wheat, soy, and other potential allergens.\n\n## Customer Reviews\n\nBased on 14 reviews [Write a review][402]\n\n#### Your Cart\n\nItem(s): ****\nTotal: $0.00\n[View Cart][403] [Continue to delivery and payment][404]\n\n### Recently Viewed\n\nCustomer Reviews\n**5.0** Based on 28 Reviews\n5 \u2605\n100%\n4 \u2605\n3 \u2605\n2 \u2605\n1 \u2605\nCustomer Photos\nWrite a Review Ask a Question\n* Reviews\n* Questions\nWrite a review\nAuthor\nName\nEmail\nLocation\nRating\nRating\n[1][405] [2][406] [3][407] [4][408] [5][409]\nTitle of Review\nHow was your overall experience?\nQuestions Photos Upload\n\nThank you for submitting a review!\n\nYour input is very much appreciated. Share it with your friends so they can enjoy it too!\n\n[Facebook][410][Twitter][411]\nBe the first to review this item\nSort Most Recent Highest Rating Lowest Rating Most Helpful\nFilter Reviews:\nSort Most Recent Highest Rating Lowest Rating Most Helpful\nClear filter\nMore Filters\n19 Dec 2024\n**Megan L.**\n[Canada] Canada\n\n### Excellent quality\n\nNothing better than fresh BS\n\n[BAKING SODA, food grade][412]\n2.27kg (5 lbs)\nWas this helpful? 0 0\n16 Dec 2024\n**Pat W.**\n[Canada] Canada\n\n### Baking soda\n\nStarting to faze out my use of chemical laden laundry and dish cleaners\u2026.just made diy dishwasher\npods\u2026.. work great!!!\n\n[BAKING SODA, food grade][413]\n454g (1lb)\nWas this helpful? 0 0\n"
