ght to your kitchen.\n\nSprouting these seeds is easy and takes less than a week. Seeds should be soaked for 4-6 hours to\nbegin the germination process. You\u2019ll need to **thoroughly rinse them with cool water every 8-12\nhours** until they are ready to harvest in 5-7 days. Enjoy your fresh sprouts by using them to top\nsandwiches, salads, or adding them to wraps and stir-fries. Keep these seeds on hand to ensure a\ncontinuous supply of fresh, homegrown flavor.\n* Broccoli Sprouting Seeds\n* Produces fresh sprouts with a radishy taste\n* Soaking time is 4-6 hours\n* Requires rinsing every 8-12 hours\n* Sprouts are ready to harvest in 5-7 days\n* Great for topping sandwiches, salads, and wraps\n\n**Ingredient:** Broccoli Seeds* (Brassica oleracea)\n\n*Certified Organic by Pro-Cert\n\n**Origin:** United States\n\n**Storage:** Store in a cool, dry place, away from heat and moisture. Protect from direct sunlight.\n\n**Disclaimer: **This information is for educational purposes only and has not been evaluated by the\nFDA or CFIA. It is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease. This product has\nbeen packaged in the same facility as peanuts, tree nuts, wheat, soy, and other potential allergens.\n\n## Customer Reviews\n\nBased on 22 reviews [Write a review][402]\n\n#### Your Cart\n\nItem(s): ****\nTotal: $0.00\n[View Cart][403] [Continue to delivery and payment][404]\n\n### Recently Viewed\n\nCustomer Reviews\n**4.8** Based on 28 Reviews\n5 \u2605\n89%\n4 \u2605\n3 \u2605\n2 \u2605\n1 \u2605\nCustomer Photos\nWrite a Review Ask a Question\n* Reviews\n* Questions\nWrite a review\nAuthor\nName\nEmail\nLocation\nRating\nRating\n[1][405] [2][406] [3][407] [4][408] [5][409]\nTitle of Review\nHow was your overall experience?\nQuestions Photos Upload\n\nThank you for submitting a review!\n\nYour input is very much appreciated. Share it with your friends so they can enjoy it too!\n\n[Facebook][410][Twitter][411]\nBe the first to review this item\nSort Most Recent Highest Rating Lowest Rating Most Helpful\nFilter Reviews:\nSort Most Recent Highest Rating Lowest Rating Most Helpful\nClear filter\nMore Filters\n23 Sep 2024\n**Kathryn N.**\n[Canada] Canada\n\n### Broccoli seeds\n\nSprout quite well - yummy\n\n[ORGANIC BROCCOLI SEEDS, sprouting][412]\n454g (1lb)\nWas this helpful? 0 0\n07 Sep 2024\n**Rose D.**\n[Canada] Canada\n\n### Organic broccoli seeds\n\nOnly about one quarter of the seeds sprouted. Taking longer than expected. The smell was really bad.\nHad to dump it all. The mixed sprouts were very good.\n\n[ORGANIC BROCCOLI SEEDS, sprouting][413]\n454g (1lb)\nWas this helpful? 0 "
