            "url": "https://eathealthy365.com/about/",
            "text": "[[Flavor365 Logo]Flavor365][1]\n* [Recipes][2]\n* [Breakfast][3]\n* [Lunch][4]\n* [Dinner][5]\n* [Snacks][6]\n* [Desserts][7]\n* [Drinks][8]\n* [Cocktails][9]\n* [Smoothies][10]\n* [Coffee][11]\n* [Wine][12]\n* [Cooking Tools][13]\n* [About][14]\n* [Recipes][15]\n* [Breakfast][16]\n* [Lunch][17]\n* [Dinner][18]\n* [Snacks][19]\n* [Desserts][20]\n* [Drinks][21]\n* [Cocktails][22]\n* [Smoothies][23]\n* [Coffee][24]\n* [Wine][25]\n* [Cooking Tools][26]\n* [About][27]\n[Home][28] \u203a About Flavor365 & Silas\n\n# About Flavor365 & Silas\n\n[Silas, founder of Flavor365, smiling outside a restaurant while wearing a light-colored shirt.]\n\nHey, I\u2019m Silas \u2014 the founder of Flavor365.\n\nFlavor365 is a content site focused on recipes, drinks, and everyday lifestyle ideas. I created it\nas a space to share the food and drink ideas I cook, explore, or develop through daily life \u2014 always\nkeeping things simple, practical, and easy to understand.\n\nMy goal here is pretty straightforward: to make everyday cooking and living feel more approachable,\nenjoyable, and realistic for real-life routines.\n\n## My Story\n\n[Silas, founder of Flavor365, holding a smartphone on a sunny patio.]\n\nI\u2019ve been interested in food and drinks for over a decade. My interest comes from a mix of everyday\ncooking, experimenting in the kitchen, learning from different sources, and continuously refining\nideas over time.\n\nSome ideas come from personal cooking experience, while others come from testing, inspiration, or\nideas I adapt into something practical and easy to use at home.\n\nOver time, cooking and recipe development became part of my routine \u2014 not in a formal or\nprofessional sense, but as an ongoing personal interest in making everyday food and drinks more\nenjoyable and accessible.\n\nI believe cooking doesn\u2019t need to be complicated. Most of what I share is focused on simple,\nreal-world ideas that can fit into different lifestyles and skill levels.\n\n> **Good food and simple living don\u2019t need to be perfect \u2014 just practical, enjoyable, and\n> realistic.**\n\n## What You\u2019ll Find on Flavor365\n\nFlavor365 is organized into a few main areas:\n* [Recipes:][29] Simple home-style meals inspired by everyday cooking, familiar ingredients, and\nrecipes I enjoy sharing.\n* [Breakfast:][30] Easy morning ideas for both slow weekends and busy weekdays.\n* [Lunch:][31] Simple lunch ideas for workdays or home, focused on meals that are quick to prepare\nbut still feel satisfying.\n* [Dinner:][32] Easy, relaxed dinner recipes for everyday cooking.\n* [Snacks:][33] Easy appetizers, game-day bites, and quick treats for everyday cravings.\n* [Desserts:][34] Simple cookies, cakes, pies, and no-bake sweets for home bakers.\n* [Drinks:][35] Cocktails, smoothies, coffee, and homemade wine recipes, plus simple drink ideas for\nhome.\n* [Cooking Tools:][36] Free online 4-in-1 toolkit including a Baking Converter, Air Fryer\nCalculator, Recipe Scaler, and Temperature Converter for everyday cooking adjustments.\n\n## How I Create Content\n\nThe content on Flavor365 draws from personal experience, kitchen experimentation, ongoing learning,\nand the refinement of practical ideas.\n\nNot every recipe follows the exact same process \u2014 some are developed directly from my own kitchen,\nwhile others are inspired by external sources and adapted to be practical for everyday home cooks.\n\nIf an idea or recipe doesn\u2019t feel clear or useful, I make a point to revisit, refine, or update it\nover time so it better matches real-world needs.\n\n## My Approach\n* **Practical mindset:** I focus on ideas that can realistically fit into your everyday routines.\n* **Real-world inspiration:** I draw from personal experience, ongoing learning, and ideas I refine\nover time.\n* **Simplicity:** I aim to keep everything approachable and easy to follow.\n* **Transparency:** Any sponsored content or partnerships are always clearly disclosed.\n\n## Let\u2019s Connect\n\nIf you have questions or feedback, feel free to reach out through the [contact page][37].\n\n[Instagram][38] | [Pinterest][39] | [Facebook][40] | [X][41] | [YouTube][42]\n\nThanks for stopping by \u2014 I really appreciate you being here.\n\n\u2014 Silas\n\n### Most Popular\n* [[Hero image of a classic Cuban\u2011style mojito in a Collins glass with crushed ice, lime wheel, and\nfresh mint on a wooden table.]Classic Mojito Recipe (Authentic Cuban Style)][43]\n* [[Sliced 10-pound prime rib roast glazed with herb butter on a festive serving platter, ready to\nserve.]How to Cook a 10-lb Prime Rib? Step-by-Step Cooking Guide][44]\n* [[Tall glass of iced coffee with ice cubes and a silky crema layer, styled in natural light.]How\nto Make Iced Coffee Recipe][45]\n* [[Hero image of a stack of no-bake haystack cookies on a wooden board surrounded by scattered\nrolled oats and chopped peanuts.]No-Bake Haystack Cookies: Easy Chocolate Peanut Butter\nRecipe][46]\n\n[ Flavor365 ][47]\n\nSimple recipes, refreshing drinks, and everyday cooking ideas, plus meal planning tips and daily\ninspiration for home cooks who enjoy joyful meals at home.\n\nDiscover\n* [Breakfast][48]\n* [Lunch][49]\n* [Dinner][50]\n* [Recipes][51]\n* [Drinks][52]\n\nResources\n* [About Us][53]\n* [Contact Us][54]\n* [Cooking Tools][55]\n* [Cooking Terms][56]\n* [Help Center][57]\n\nLegal\n* [Privacy Policy][58]\n* [Terms of Use][59]\n* [Cookie Policy][60]\n* [Disclosure][61]\n* [Accessibility][62]\n\nFollow\n* [Instagram][63]\n* [Pinterest][64]\n* [Facebook][65]\n* [X (Twitter)][66]\n* [YouTube][67]\n\n\u00a9 2026 Flavor365. All Rights Reserved.\n\n[1]: https://eathealthy365.com/\n[2]: https://eathealthy365.com/recipes/\n[3]: https://eathealthy365.com/recipes/breakfast/\n[4]: https://eathealthy365.com/recipes/lunch/\n[5]: https://eathealthy365.com/recipes/dinner/\n[6]: https://eathealthy365.com/recipes/snacks/\n[7]: https://eathealthy365.com/recipes/desserts/\n[8]: https://eathealthy365.com/drinks/\n[9]: https://eathealthy365.com/drinks/cocktails/\n[10]: https://eathealthy365.com/drinks/smoothies/\n[11]: https://eathealthy365.com/drinks/coffee/\n[12]: https://eathealthy365.com/drinks/wine/\n[13]: https://eathealthy365.com/online-cooking-tools/\n[14]: https://eathealthy365.com/about/\n[15]: https://eathealthy365.com/recipes/\n[16]: https://eathealthy365.com/recipes/breakfast/\n[17]: https://eathealthy365.com/recipes/lunch/\n[18]: https://eathealthy365.com/recipes/dinner/\n[19]: https://eathealthy365.com/recipes/snacks/\n[20]: https://eathealthy365.com/recipes/desserts/\n[21]: https://eathealthy365.com/drinks/\n[22]: https://eathealthy365.com/drinks/cocktails/\n[23]: https://eathealthy365.com/drinks/smoothies/\n[24]: https://eathealthy365.com/drinks/coffee/\n[25]: https://eathealthy365.com/drinks/wine/\n[26]: https://eathealthy365.com/online-cooking-tools/\n[27]: https://eathealthy365.com/about/\n[28]: https://eathealthy365.com/\n[29]: https://eathealthy365.com/recipes/\n[30]: https://eathealthy365.com/recipes/breakfast/\n[31]: https://eathealthy365.com/recipes/lunch/\n[32]: https://eathealthy365.com/recipes/dinner/\n[33]: https://eathealthy365.com/recipes/snacks/\n[34]: https://eathealthy365.com/recipes/desserts/\n[35]: https://eathealthy365.com/drinks/\n[36]: https://eathealthy365.com/online-cooking-tools/\n[37]: https://eathealthy365.com/contact/\n[38]: https://www.instagram.com/flavor365official_silas/\n[39]: https://www.pinterest.com/flavor365official_silas/\n[40]: https://www.facebook.com/Flavor365Official/\n[41]: https://x.com/flavor365_silas\n[42]: https://www.youtube.com/@Flavor365_Silas\n[43]: https://eathealthy365.com/classic-mojito-recipe-authentic-cuban-style/\n[44]: https://eathealthy365.com/how-to-cook-a-10-lb-prime-rib-step-by-step-cooking-guide/\n[45]: https://eathealthy365.com/how-to-make-iced-coffee-recipe/\n[46]: https://eathealthy365.com/no-bake-haystack-cookies-easy-chocolate-peanut-butter-recipe/\n[47]: https://eathealthy365.com/\n[48]: https://eathealthy365.com/recipes/breakfast/\n[49]: https://eathealthy365.com/recipes/lunch/\n[50]: https://eathealthy365.com/recipes/dinner/\n[51]: https://eathealthy365.com/recipes/\n[52]: https://eathealthy365.com/drinks/\n[53]: https://eathealthy365.com/about/\n[54]: https://eathealthy365.com/contact/\n[55]: https://eathealthy365.com/online-cooking-tools/\n[56]: https://eathealthy365.com/cooking-terms/\n[57]: https://eathealthy365.com/faq/\n[58]: https://eathealthy365.com/privacy-policy/\n[59]: https://eathealthy365.com/terms-of-use/\n[60]: https://eathealthy365.com/cookie-policy/\n[61]: https://eathealthy365.com/disclosure-policy/\n[62]: https://eathealthy365.com/accessibility/\n[63]: https://www.instagram.com/flavor365official_silas/\n[64]: https://www.pinterest.com/flavor365official_silas/\n[65]: https://www.facebook.com/Flavor365Official/\n[66]: https://x.com/flavor365_silas\n[67]: https://www.youtube.com/@Flavor365_Silas"
