            "url": "https://eatwellwell.com/about",
            "text": "[Skip to content][1]\n[ [Eat Well Well] ][2]\nMenu\n* [Recipes][3]\n* [Main Dishes][4]\n* [Casseroles][5]\n* [Desserts & Baking][6]\n* [Cookies][7]\n* [Salads][8]\n* [Soups][9]\n* [Air Fryer Recipes][10]\n* [Vegetarian Diet][11]\n* [Weight Loss Meals][12]\n* [Wellness][13]\n* [About Us][14]\n[][15]\n\n# About Us\n\n## Abby\u2019s Story: Founder of EATWELLWELL\n\n[Abby Pinkmann]\n\nHi there, I\u2019m **Abby Pinkmann**, a 36-year-old homegrown chef just outside Austin, Texas, and the\nfounder of **EATWELLWELL**. Cooking has always been my love language. I believe that food doesn\u2019t\nneed to be complicated to be beautiful, it just needs to be made with care. That\u2019s the heart behind\nthis site.\n\nI grew up in a big, loud family with three siblings and two hardworking parents. My mom had this\nincredible way of turning humble pantry staples into magic, dinner in 30 minutes flat, and everyone\nleft the table full and happy. She taught me that nourishment goes beyond calories. It\u2019s about\ncomfort, connection, and love.\n\nIn my twenties, a \u201cfive-ingredient dinner party\u201d challenge sparked something in me. I fell back in\nlove with food, not just cooking it, but sharing it. I started EATWELLWELL to make eating well\n**joyful, accessible, and stress-free**. Whether you\u2019re a parent trying to feed picky eaters, a\nstudent on a tight budget, or just someone tired of over-complicated meals, I\u2019ve got you.\n\nThis site began with me, but it\u2019s grown into something much richer, with the help of my two favorite\ncollaborators.\n\nEvery recipe published on EatWellWell is carefully developed and tested before it goes live. For\narticles covering nutrition, healthy eating, or weight-loss topics, we review information from\ntrusted medical and research organizations, including the [National Institutes of Health (NIH)][16],\n[Mayo Clinic][17], and [Harvard Health][18], to help ensure our content is accurate, reliable, and\nup to date.\n\nWhile we are not registered dietitians, physicians, or licensed healthcare professionals, we are\npassionate about creating practical, nutritious recipes and sharing evidence-based information about\nhealthy eating.\n\nOur goal is to present complex health information in a clear, accessible way while encouraging\nreaders to consult qualified healthcare professionals for personalized medical advice.\n\n## Our Editorial Standards\n\nAt EatWellWell, we are committed to providing accurate, trustworthy, and practical content.\n* Every recipe is tested before publication.\n* Nutrition and wellness articles are researched using reputable medical and scientific sources.\n* Content is reviewed and updated periodically to reflect current information and best practices.\n* We avoid exaggerated health claims and focus on balanced, evidence-based guidance.\n* We do not promote extreme diets, rapid weight-loss methods, or unsupported health claims.\n* Our content is intended for educational purposes and should not replace professional medical\nadvice.\n\n## Meet My Sisters: Sarah and Paula Pinkmann\n\nFamily has always been my flavor compass, so it feels natural that **EATWELLWELL is now a\nsister-powered kitchen.** My sisters, **Sarah** and **Paula**, each bring their own spice to the\npot, and I couldn\u2019t be more excited to share this space with them.\n\n**Sarah** is the heart of cozy comfort food. She\u2019s our in-house baker, big-batch brunch planner, and\nthe one most likely to say, \u201cLet\u2019s just add a little more butter.\u201d Her approach is warm, generous,\nand designed to bring people together.\n\n**Paula** is our resident meal-hacker, she makes weeknight dinners faster, easier, and more creative\nthan I ever thought possible. She\u2019s a master of the 20-minute dinner and the queen of smart grocery\nshortcuts.\n\nTogether, we test, taste, and tinker until every recipe feels like one you\u2019ll come back to again and\nagain. Because that\u2019s what this site is about: **bringing joy back to your table, one simple,\ndelicious meal at a time.**\n\n## About Sarah Pinkmann\n\n[Sarah Pinkmann author of Eatwellwell]\n\n**Co-Creator, Baker, and Brunch Architect \u2013 Age 39**\nAt 39, Sarah is the eldest of the Pinkmann siblings and the one most likely to bring a pie to your\ndoor \u201cjust because.\u201d A former elementary school teacher turned full-time home baker, Sarah\u2019s cooking\nstyle is rooted in comfort, nostalgia, and family tradition, with a twist of cinnamon.\n\nHer love for baking bloomed early. At age 12, she tried to make muffins without asking Mom first,\nand used salt instead of sugar. Everyone still jokes about \u201cthe Great Muffin Incident,\u201d but Sarah\ntook it as a challenge. She\u2019s been perfecting the art of warm, crowd-pleasing baking ever since.\n\nSarah brings the cozy factor to EATWELLWELL with her weekend brunch spreads, big-batch breakfast\nbakes, and from-scratch treats that feel like a hug. Her kitchen motto? \u201cBake more than you need,\nsomeone will always show up hungry.\n\n## About Paula Pinkmann\n\n[Paula Pinkmann author of Eatwellwell]\n\n**Co-Creator, Recipe Tester, and Time-Saving Genius \u2013 Age 29**\nPaula, the youngest of the three sisters at 29, is the queen of smart cooking. A working mom of one\nand full-time efficiency expert (in and out of the kitchen), she\u2019s known for turning \u201cwhat\u2019s in the\nfridge?\u201d into magic in under 20 minutes.\n\nHer signature story? The time she threw together a pasta dish from frozen peas, lemon, and leftover\nrotisserie chicken during a power outage, on a camp stove. It was so good, her friends demanded the\nrecipe, and it became a core EATWELLWELL favorite: \u201cStormy Day Pasta.\u201d\n\nPaula\u2019s recipes are fast, flexible, and full of flavor, designed for people who want real food\nwithout the stress. She\u2019s all about using what you have, skipping unnecessary steps, and making\ndinner feel doable even on your busiest days.\n\n[][19] [][20] [][21] [][22]\n\n[Abby pinkmann Eat well well]\n\n## Abby Pinkmann\n\nI'm Abby Pinkmann, founder of EatWellWell and a passionate home cook based near Austin, Texas. I\ncreated EatWellWell to share simple, flavorful recipes that make healthy eating enjoyable and\naccessible for everyone. Every recipe is carefully developed and tested before publication to ensure\nreliable results. For nutrition, healthy eating, and weight-loss content, we review information from\ntrusted sources such as the [National Institutes of Health (NIH)][23], [Mayo Clinic][24], and\n[Harvard Health][25] to help provide accurate, trustworthy, and up-to-date information for our\nreaders.\n[][26] [][27] [][28] [][29]\n\n## Recent Recipes\n\n[[Gluten free casserole recipe baked with chicken rice and cheese]][30]\n\n### [Gluten Free Casserole Recipe: Easy, Comforting, and Family-Friendly][31]\n\n[[Low carb casserole recipe baked with cheese, broccoli, and ground beef]][32]\n\n### [Low Carb Casserole Recipe: Easy, Cheesy, and Family-Friendly Dinner][33]\n\n[[Stuffed pepper casserole recipe with ground beef rice and melted cheese]][34]\n\n### [Stuffed Pepper Casserole Recipe: Easy Family Dinner With Classic Flavor][35]\n\n[[Cheddar bay biscuit casserole with golden garlic cheddar biscuit topping]][36]\n\n### [Cheddar Bay Biscuit Casserole: The Ultimate Comfort Food Dinner][37]\n\n[Dish image]\n\n**\u00a9 2026 Eat Well Well**\n\n[**About**][38]\n\n[**Privacy policy**][39]\n\n[**Terms & conditions**][40]\n\n[**Disclaimer**][41]\n\n[**Contact**][42]\n\nClose\n* [Recipes][43]\n* [Main Dishes][44]\n* [Casseroles][45]\n* [Desserts & Baking][46]\n* [Cookies][47]\n* [Salads][48]\n* [Soups][49]\n* [Air Fryer Recipes][50]\n* [Vegetarian Diet][51]\n* [Weight Loss Meals][52]\n* [Wellness][53]\n* [About Us][54]\nSearch for:\n\n[1]: #content\n[2]: https://eatwellwell.com/\n[3]: https://eatwellwell.com/blog/\n[4]: https://eatwellwell.com/main-dishes/\n[5]: https://eatwellwell.com/casseroles/\n[6]: https://eatwellwell.com/desserts-baking/\n[7]: https://eatwellwell.com/cookies/\n[8]: https://eatwellwell.com/salads/\n[9]: https://eatwellwell.com/soups/\n[10]: https://eatwellwell.com/air-fryer-recipes/\n[11]: https://eatwellwell.com/vegetarian-diet/\n[12]: https://eatwellwell.com/weight-loss/\n[13]: https://eatwellwell.com/wellness/\n[14]: https://eatwellwell.com/about-us/\n[15]: #\n[16]: https://www.nih.gov/\n[17]: https://www.mayoclinic.org/\n[18]: https://www.health.harvard.edu/\n[19]: https://x.com/eat_wellwell\n[20]: https://www.pinterest.com/Eatwellwell/\n[21]: https://www.facebook.com/eatwellwell/\n[22]: https://www.instagram.com/eat.well.well/\n[23]: https://www.nih.gov/\n[24]: https://www.mayoclinic.org/\n[25]: https://www.health.harvard.edu/\n[26]: https://x.com/eat_wellwell\n[27]: https://www.pinterest.com/Eatwellwell/\n[28]: https://www.instagram.com/eat.well.well/\n[29]: https://www.facebook.com/eatwellwell/\n[30]: https://eatwellwell.com/gluten-free-casserole-recipe/\n[31]: https://eatwellwell.com/gluten-free-casserole-recipe/\n[32]: https://eatwellwell.com/low-carb-casserole-recipe/\n[33]: https://eatwellwell.com/low-carb-casserole-recipe/\n[34]: https://eatwellwell.com/stuffed-pepper-casserole-recipe/\n[35]: https://eatwellwell.com/stuffed-pepper-casserole-recipe/\n[36]: https://eatwellwell.com/cheddar-bay-biscuit-casserole/\n[37]: https://eatwellwell.com/cheddar-bay-biscuit-casserole/\n[38]: https://eatwellwell.com/about-me/\n[39]: https://eatwellwell.com/privacy-policy/\n[40]: https://eatwellwell.com/terms-and-conditions/\n[41]: https://eatwellwell.com/disclaimer/\n[42]: https://eatwellwell.com/contact/\n[43]: https://eatwellwell.com/blog/\n[44]: https://eatwellwell.com/main-dishes/\n[45]: https://eatwellwell.com/casseroles/\n[46]: https://eatwellwell.com/desserts-baking/\n[47]: https://eatwellwell.com/cookies/\n[48]: https://eatwellwell.com/salads/\n[49]: https://eatwellwell.com/soups/\n[50]: https://eatwellwell.co