        "crawl_text": "Entirely Elizabeth USA Michigan, USA USA Entirely Elizabeth receives over 600,000 visitors per year from various countries. The brand has a strong social media presence with over 50,000 total followers. Emerging food blog with a focus on family recipes and sustainable living. Entirely Elizabeth - Recipes from My Family Farm to Your Family&#039;s Table\n\nSkip to content\n\nEntirely Elizabeth Instagram\n\nEntirely Elizabeth Pinterest\n\nEntirely Elizabeth Facebook\n\nHome\n\nAbout Me\n\nBuy Your Copy of The One Jar Condiments Cookbook!\n\nSubscribe\n\nMenu\n\nMenu\n\nRECIPES\n\nNA DRINKS\n\nLEMONADE\n\nMOCKTAILS\n\nSYRUP\n\nTEA\n\nSAVORY\n\nAPPETIZERS\n\nCONDIMENTS\n\nEASY MEALS\n\nSIDE DISHES\n\nSMOKED\n\nSWEET\n\nBARS\n\nCAKES\n\nCOOKIES\n\nFROSTING\n\nMUFFINS\n\nPIE DIPS\n\nPIES &amp; TARTS\n\nVIDEOS\n\nHomemade Recipes from My Family Farm to Your Family&#8217;s Table!\n\nsummer bbq FAVORITES\n\nDill Pickle Potato Salad\n\nHot Dogs on the Smoker\n\nDoctored Up Baked Beans\n\nNEW ON THE FARM\n\nApple Kale Slaw\n\nCucumber Radish Salad\n\nPeanut Butter Chocolate Chunk Bars\n\nBlueberry Mocktail\n\nIf you&#8217;re craving homemade farm-inspired recipes ,\nyou&#8217;ve come to the right place!\n\nI&#8217;m Elizabeth, 6th generation owner of my family&#8217;s farm and a &#8220;semi&#8221; homesteader.\n\nYou&#8217;ll find a large variety of sweet, savory, and non alcoholic drink recipes . I love comfort food, honoring seasonal ingredients from my garden, and helping people live a more sustainable life (like our ancestors).\n\nMY STORY\n\nRECIPES\n\nFRESH DINNERS &amp; SIDE DISHES\n\nApple Kale Slaw\n\nCucumber Radish Salad\n\nLemon Chicken Thighs\n\nWarm Quinoa Salad\n\nBLUE RIBBON BAKED GOODS\n\nPeanut Butter Chocolate Chunk Bars\n\nWhite Chocolate Raspberry Bundt Cake\n\nScoopable Cookies\n\nLemon Strawberry Muffins\n\nGrab My FREE Printable Kitchen Cheat Sheet!\n\nIt&#8217;s great for your refrigerator, and you&#8217;ll never have to Google a conversion or temperature again.\n\nSEND ME THE CHEAT SHEET!\n\nLoading&#8230;\n\nIt&#8217;s on the way!\n\nGo check your email&#8230; and thank you\nfor subscribing to my weekly email newsletter.\n\nUnsubscribe at any time.\n\nFRESH TEA &amp; LEMONADE\n\nWatermelon Limeade\n\nDandelion Lemonade\n\nBlueberry Iced Tea\n\nIced Mint Green Tea\n\nKITCHEN BASICS\n\nLavender Simple Syrup\n\nFresh Milled Banana Bread\n\nMixed Fruit Jam\n\nHomemade Chicken Stock\n\nREADER FAVORITE RECIPES\n\nSpinach Lemon Pasta\n\nEnglish Pea Salad\n\nCottage Cheese Taco Dip\n\nLOOKING FOR MORE?\n\nRecipes\n\nOne Jar Condiments Cookbook\n\nAbout Me\n\nShop &#038; Discount Codes\n\nWork With Me\n\nFOLLOW ALONG ON YOUR\nFAVORITE SOCIAL CHANNEL\n\nEntirely Elizabeth Instagram\n\nEntirely Elizabeth Pinterest\n\nEntirely Elizabeth Facebook\n\nELIZABETH'S FAVORITES\n\nCaprese Penne Pasta\n\nChocolate Chip Cookies\n\nMargarita Mocktail\n\n2026&copy; Entirely Elizabeth - All Rights Reserved -\nPrivacy and Terms of Use Policy - Nutrition Disclaimer\n\nAdvertisements displayed do not reflect endorsements or recommendations made by Entirely Elizabeth.\n\nEntirely Elizabeth Instagram\n\nEntirely Elizabeth Pinterest\n\nEntirely Elizabeth Facebook\n\nMail\n\nRECIPES\n\nNA DRINKS\n\nLEMONADE\n\nMOCKTAILS\n\nSYRUP\n\nTEA\n\nSAVORY\n\nAPPETIZERS\n\nCONDIMENTS\n\nEASY MEALS\n\nSIDE DISHES\n\nSMOKED\n\nSWEET\n\nBARS\n\nCAKES\n\nCOOKIES\n\nFROSTING\n\nMUFFINS\n\nPIE DIPS\n\nPIES &amp; TARTS\n\nVIDEOS\n\nClose\n\nSearch for: [Skip to content][1]\n* [Entirely Elizabeth Instagram][2]\n* [Entirely Elizabeth Pinterest][3]\n* [Entirely Elizabeth Facebook][4]\n* [Home][5]\n* [About Me][6]\n* [Buy Your Copy of The One Jar Condiments Cookbook!][7]\n\nSubscribe\n\n[ [Entirely Elizabeth] ][8]\n[][9]\nMenu\n[ [Entirely Elizabeth] ][10]\nMenu\n* [RECIPES][11]\n* [NA DRINKS][12]\n* [LEMONADE][13]\n* [MOCKTAILS][14]\n* [SYRUP][15]\n* [TEA][16]\n* [SAVORY][17]\n* [APPETIZERS][18]\n* [CONDIMENTS][19]\n* [EASY MEALS][20]\n* [SIDE DISHES][21]\n* [SMOKED][22]\n* [SWEET][23]\n* [BARS][24]\n* [CAKES][25]\n* [COOKIES][26]\n* [FROSTING][27]\n* [MUFFINS][28]\n* [PIE DIPS][29]\n* [PIES & TARTS][30]\n* [VIDEOS][31]\n[][32]\n\n# About Me \u2013 Entirely Elizabeth\n\n## **RECIPES MADE FOR EVERY DAY ENTERTAINING!**\n\n### My name is Elizabeth Swoish (say it like [swash][33]) and I am the founder and face behind\n### Entirely Elizabeth.\n\n### **Here we turn ordinary days into a party with \u2026**\n* easy **desserts** to sweeten things up\n* refreshing **mocktails** (and other non-alcoholic drinks) to mix it up\n* savory **appetizers** to tantalize your taste buds\n* fun hosting ideas and party hacks\n\nSo whether you are coming home from a stressful day, preparing an epic spread for girl\u2019s night, or\npacking your cooler for a party, I\u2019ve got you covered!\n\n[Elizabeth Swoish, Entirely Elizabeth pictured holding camera and taking a picture.]\n[Kitchen Cheat Sheet Freebie Mock Up Sidebar Opt In]\n\n## **Elizabeth Swoish Bio**\n\n[Elizabeth Swoish, Entirely Elizabeth pictured holding a bowl of grandma's famous cranberry relish!]\n\nI was born and raised on our family farm in Michigan where food, homesteading, and entertaining\neveryone was a normal activity. It is how we show love! As a girl I remember being in the kitchen\ncooking with my grandma quite a bit. Funny enough, I create my recipes in the same ole family\nfarmhouse kitchen where all those memories were made.\n\nWith a strong background in program management, data analysis, and a Bachelor\u2019s degree in business\nmanagement, I had no doubts when I took the leap and created Entirely Elizabeth 2 years ago. I am a\nself-taught home baker, chef, digital creator, and proud small business owner. My humble, small\ntown, farm raised roots is why I share approachable, simple, and well tested recipes for the every\nday person.\n\nToday Entirely Elizabeth gets more than 600,000 visitors per year from countries all over the world.\nWith a strong social media presence and over 50,000 total followers, I have become a respected and\nadmired upcoming food blogger in the food and mocktail community.\n\n### **FOLLOW ALONG ON YOUR FAVORITE SOCIAL CHANNEL!**\n* [Entirely Elizabeth Facebook][34]\n* [Entirely Elizabeth Instagram][35]\n* [Entirely Elizabeth Pinterest][36]\n* [Entirely Elizabeth Twitter][37]\n* [Entirely Elizabeth YouTube][38]\n* [Entirely Elizabeth Email][39]\n\n## **Brand Work**\n\nSince starting my digital creator journey 2 years ago, I have worked with a handful of national and\nlocal brands to various types of create content. Together we have collaborated on recipe\ndevelopment, food photography and videography, social media promotion, giveaways, product\nphotography, and more!\n\nCurrent and past clients include Del Monte Fresh, Kibo Foods, Scotty\u2019s Everyday, Good Karma, Finn\nCrisp, and Town Coffee Company. With social media features from Sky Valley, King Arthur Flour,\nPyrex, Fre Sutter Homes, Oregon Berries, Bob\u2019s Red Mill, Lodge Cast Iron, Aged and Charred, Rock\nTown Distilleries, Lyre\u2019s, Fleischmann\u2019s, Wilton Baking, Satin Ice, Karo, and more.\n\n### ****If you are interested in working together, [click here][40] for more information!****\n\n[Brands Entirely Elizabeth and Elizabeth Swoish has worked with and been featured by on social media\nchannels and websites.]\n\n### **BROWSE RECIPES[ HERE][41] OR SEE WHAT\u2019S NEW:**\n* [ [Apple Kale Slaw with ribbons of carrots and a honey mustard dressing.] ][42]\n[Apple Kale Slaw][43]\n* [ [Cucumber Radish Salad tossed in a sweet and creamy dressing with red onion, dill, and black\npepper.] ][44]\n[Cucumber Radish Salad][45]\n* [ [Bite taken out of a Peanut Butter Chocolate Chunk Bar. It's soft, chewy, and studded with\nchocolate chunks.] ][46]\n[Peanut Butter Chocolate Chunk Bars][47]\n* [ [A pretty magenta Blueberry Mocktail garnished with fresh blueberries, a sprig of mint, and\nslice of lemon.] ][48]\n[Blueberry Mocktail][49]\n\n## **Contact Me**\n\nYou can reach me by email at **Elizabeth (at) Entirely Elizabeth (dot) com** for any questions,\nmedia kit requests, or to discuss future partnerships. Due to the number of emails received, please\nallow time for a response. I look forward to connecting with you!\n\n### LOOKING FOR MORE?\n* [Recipes][50]\n* [One Jar Condiments Cookbook][51]\n* [About Me][52]\n* [Shop & Discount Codes][53]\n* [Work With Me][54]\n\n[Entirely Elizabeth Logo]\n\n### FOLLOW ALONG ON YOUR\n### FAVORITE SOCIAL CHANNEL\n* [Entirely Elizabeth Instagram][55]\n* [Entirely Elizabeth Pinterest][56]\n* [Entirely Elizabeth Facebook][57]\n\n### ELIZABETH'S FAVORITES\n\n[ [Plate of Caprese Penne Pasta topped with a balsamic glaze drizzle, fresh basil, mozzarella\npearls, and the roasted tomato balsamic sauce.] ][58]\n\n[Caprese Penne Pasta][59]\n\n[ [Stack of 4 no chill chocolate chip cookies with a bite taken out of the top one.] ][60]\n\n[Chocolate Chip Cookies][61]\n\n[ [Pouring the drink into an ice filled glass. The glass is garnished with flaky sea salt and lime\nzest. There are lime slices, and a plate of the salt zest mixture.] ][62]\n\n[Margarita Mocktail][63]\n\n2026\u00a9 Entirely Elizabeth - All Rights Reserved - [Privacy and Terms of Use Policy][64] - [Nutrition\nDisclaimer][65]\nAdvertisements displayed do not reflect endorsements or recommendations made by Entirely Elizabeth.\n[Entirely Elizabeth Logo]\n* [Entirely Elizabeth Instagram][66]\n* [Entirely Elizabeth Pinterest][67]\n* [Entirely Elizabeth Facebook][68]\n* [Mail][69]\n* [RECIPES][70]\n* [NA DRINKS][71]\n* [LEMONADE][72]\n* [MOCKTAILS][73]\n* [SYRUP][74]\n* [TEA][75]\n* [SAVORY][76]\n* [APPETIZERS][77]\n* [CONDIMENTS][78]\n* [EASY MEALS][79]\n* [SIDE DISHES][80]\n* [SMOKED][81]\n* [SWEET][82]\n* [BARS][83]\n* [CAKES][84]\n* [COOKIES][85]\n* [FROSTING][86]\n* [MUFFINS][87]\n* [PIE DIPS][88]\n* [PIES & TARTS][89]\n* [VIDEOS][90]\nClose\nSearch for:\n\n[1]: #content\n[2]: https://www.instagram.co