      "is_seed": false,
      "company_function": "vendor",
      "company_summary": "",
      "operational_presence": "Today, the Optima range is available in A1 and A2 materials such as PPC Aluminium, Anodised Aluminium, Pre-Paint Aluminium, ACM A2, Alpolic A1, Copper, Corte...",
      "data_sources": "discovery=ddgs_bing | enrichment=smart_crawl | page=https://sotech-optima.co.uk",
      "_crawl": {
        "founded_year": 1982,
        "headquarters": "2 Traynor Way, Peterlee, SR8 2RU, UK",
        "contact_address": "2 Traynor Way, Peterlee, SR8 2RU, UK",
        "offices": "North East England; London",
        "manufacturing_locations": "Peterlee, UK",
        "regions_served": "UK; Middle East",
        "countries": "United Kingdom",
        "ownership_parent": "",
        "company_type": "Private",
        "employee_count": "",
        "revenue": "",
        "key_numbers": "",
        "contact_person": "John Egginton",
        "contact_role": "Founder",
        "email": "technical@sotech-optima.co.uk",
        "phone": "+44 (0) 191 587 9213",
        "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/company/sotech-architectural-facade-systems/",
        "website": "https://sotech-optima.co.uk",
        "industries": "Construction; Architecture; Building Materials",
        "products": "Optima FC+; Optima TFC+; Optima Edge; Optima BrickTech; Optima Shingles; Optima Meadow",
        "certifications": "ISO9001:2015; ISO14001:2015; ISO45001",
        "distributors": "",
        "customers": "",
        "partnerships": "",
        "crawl_text": "Sotech Limited ISO9001:2015, ISO14001:2015, ISO45001 United Kingdom Middle East ISO9001:2015 ISO14001:2015 ISO45001 Manufacturing Award at North East Business Awards 3D Modelling Finite Element Modelling (FEM) Focus on fire safety Bespoke solutions Strong customer relationships CWCT certification BS8414-2 standards 2 Traynor Way, Peterlee, SR8 2RU, UK North East England London United Kingdom Peterlee, UK Middle East Sotech has over 40 years of experience in the fa\u00e7ade cladding industry. The company focuses heavily on fire safety and product innovation. Sotech has been recognized for its commitment to safety and sustainability in fa\u00e7ade cladding solutions. Continual improvement in product safety and design. Expansion into international markets, particularly the Middle East. Increasing regulatory scrutiny in the construction industry. Competition from other fa\u00e7ade cladding manufacturers. Growing demand for sustainable building materials. Potential for expansion into new geographic markets. Sotech is a leading manufacturer in the rainscreen cladding sector, known for its innovative and safe solutions. Increased construction activity in the UK and abroad. Rising demand for non-combustible fa\u00e7ade systems. Architectural Facade Cladding Experts | SOTECH OPTIMA\n\nABOUT\n\nPrivacy\n\nTerms\n\ncpd training\n\nTechnical +44 (0) 191 587 9213 | General Enquiries +44 (0) 191 587 2287\n\nSotech Optima\nBespoke Metal Rainscreen Cladding &amp; Facade Panel Systems\n\nRainscreen Solutions\n\nRainscreen Systems\n\nOptima FC+, Secret Fix Hook On Rainscreen\n\nOptima TFC+, Through Fix Cassette Rainscreen\n\nOptima Edge, SECRET FIX, FLAT PANEL APPEARANCE\n\nOptima FlatFix, Flate Plate Rainscreen\n\nOPTIMA BrickTECH, Alternative to traditional brickwork\n\nPlanks\n\nOPTIMA XTR Contour\n\nOptima Clip Plank System\n\nOptima Interlock Plank Rainscreen\n\nSpecialist Cladding\n\nOPTIMA Shingles\n\nOPTIMA MEADOW, Living Wall Rainscreen\n\nOptima Vertex Spandrel\n\nAncillaries\n\nSotech Clip on Coping\n\nSotech Perforations\n\nSotech Flashings\n\nResources\n\nWhat is Rainscreen Cladding?\n\nFire testing\n\nCWCT\n\nSAFE HANDS Promise\n\nSUSTAINABILITY\n\nEPD\n\nModelling Environment\n\nSOTECH VR\n\nLEARNING Zone &#038; Showroom\n\nCase Studies\n\nNEWS\n\nDownloads\n\nContact Us\n\nSign in\n\nSearch\n\nCart\n\nCart\n\nPhysically tested, digitally analysed, proven at full scale.\nEngineered for\n\nPerformance\nOur Systems\n\nPrecision manufacturing, backed by ISO-approved standards you can trust.\nIn house\nManufacturing\nOur Approach\n\nScaling precision in every single detail.\n\nDetails\nat Scale\nAward Winning Case studies\n\ncontact\nabout\nsystems\nprev\n0{{current_slide_index}}\nnext\n\nWELCOME TO SOTECH\n\nWhat's new?\n\nModelling Environment\n\nRainscreen Systems\n\nSafe Hands\n\nGet in Touch\n\nSAFE, SUSTAINABLE RAINSCREEN FACADE CLADDING\n\nSOTECH IS A LEADING DESIGNER AND MANUFACTURER OF THE OPTIMA RANGE OF ENGINEERED METAL RAINSCREEN FACADE CLADDING SOLUTIONS AND ARCHITECTURAL FABRICATIONS.\n\nFrom secret-fix hook on fa\u00e7ade cladding solutions to bespoke extrusion tailored to meet your design , Sotech works closely with architects, specifiers, fire consultants, main contractors and installers to specify the most suitable fa\u00e7ade cladding solution .\n\nOur expert team can provide cutting edge advice on the most suitable fa\u00e7ade cladding solution for the project, as well as fire safety, design and production.\n\nIntroducing the optima range of facade cladding systems:\n\nOptima FC+ Secret Fix Hook on Facade Cladding\n\nOptima TFC+ Through Fix Cassette Facade Cladding\n\nOptima Edge Secret Fix Rainscreen with a Flat Plate Appearance\n\nOptima XTR Contour Bespoke Tailored Extrusion\n\nOptima IPC Pressed Plank Facade Cladding\n\nOptima Shingles Discrete & Secret Fix\n\nOptima BrickTech Non-Combustible Brick System\n\nOptima Meadow Supporting Biodiversity Custom Fa\u00e7ade Cladding\n\nOptima Clip Plank Rainscreen System\n\nOptima Interlock Plank System\n\nOptima FlatFix Flat Plate Cladding System\n\nOptima Vertex Spandrels\n\nView our facade cladding systems\n\nWe are here because of our customers, and those customers contact us project after project for advice, solutions and recommendations because we care about the details in the fa\u00e7ade cladding sector. We share our industry knowledge generously and we go the extra mile to complete projects to the highest standards, protecting the building, protecting the inhabitants, and enhancing the reputation of fa\u00e7ade cladding in the industry.\n\nSotech: Details, at Scale\n\nAs regulations tighten and scrutiny intensifies, responsibility for performance is being more clearly defined across the entire supply chain. In this environment, facade performance can no longer be assumed through specification alone. It must be evidenced through testing and demonstrated in consistent delivery.\n\nAs such, facade cladding should be considered as a complete system rather than a collection of individual products. Panels, brackets, rails, insulation, cavity barriers and fixings all work together, and the performance of the facade is defined by how those elements are designed, tested and installed as a whole, across complex schemes. It is the very definition of \u2018Details at Scale\u2019.\n\nFocusing on individual components in isolation no longer reflects how facade performance is assessed, or how risk is managed in practice. Ultimately, performance is proven not just in principle, but in the execution of every detail, at scale.\n\nLearn more\n\nBespoke Facade Cladding\n\nSotech also specialises in manufacturing bespoke, complex fa\u00e7ade cladding designs, offering a wide range of architectural facade features including fins, perforations, balconies, and curves.\n\nWhether it\u2019s creating bold vertical or horizontal emphasis with feature fins, enhancing airflow and light with custom perforations, or integrating balcony cladding seamlessly with the main fa\u00e7ade, Sotech delivers innovative, high-performance fa\u00e7ade cladding solutions tailored to the most demanding design visions.\n\nUtilising fire-rated fa\u00e7ade cladding materials and systems, Sotech combines aesthetic flexibility with rigorous performance, ensuring safety and compliance across all its bespoke architectural fa\u00e7ade cladding projects.\n\nSpeak to our expert team\n\nTrusted by the Facade Cladding Industry\n\nDedicated to safety, sustainability and excellence, Sotech are committed to continually improving, testing and enhancing their fa\u00e7ade cladding solutions.\n\nHaving tested since 2006, Sotech has always put a huge focus on fire safety in the rainscreen cladding industry. Today, the Optima range is available in A1 and A2 materials such as PPC Aluminium, Anodised Aluminium, Pre-Paint Aluminium, ACM A2, Alpolic A1, Copper, Corten Steel, Stainless Steel and Zinc. Sotech can provide true A1 non-combustible fa\u00e7ade cladding systems complete with mechanical fixings in place of adhesive.\n\nAll systems carry full CWCT certification and the Optima FC+, TFC+ and Edge have been tested to BS8414-2 standards, BR135 classification. Sotech is also accredited to ISO9001:2015, ISO14001:2015, ISO45001 and we are aiming to achieve The Net Zero Carbon Buildings Commitment 2030 through our supply chain. At Sotech we are always seeking improvements to protect our environmental and natural resources. This is why we are working towards achieving a verified EPD, not just for \u2018components\u2019 but for our full rainscreen systems.\n\nLearn more\n\nWe pride ourselves on being recognised as the safe hands in the industry, committed to providing safe, sustainable fa\u00e7ade cladding solutions that are innovative and market leading in design and manufacture. With over 40 years of experience in the fa\u00e7ade cladding industry, Sotech is a leading designer and manufacturer of engineered metal fa\u00e7ade cladding and architectural fabrications.\n\nLeveraging cutting-edge 3D modelling technology\n\nOur Technical Team leverages cutting-edge 3D modelling technology to bring your architectural vision to life, ensuring precise and manufacturable rainscreen cladding solutions.\n\nBy creating interactive 3D mock-ups and performing detailed analyses, we optimise panel designs for performance and cost-efficiency.\n\nThis approach allows designers to visualise and refine their projects before production, saving time and reducing errors.\n\nDiscover how our expertise in 3D modelling can enhance your facade cladding projects with innovative and practical solutions.\n\nModelling environment\n\nFEM is crucial for analysing and optimising rainscreen panel performance and stability by breaking down complex structures into manageable elements. This advanced technique allows for precise adjustments in panel thickness, size, and fixing methods, ensuring high performance and durability.\n\nBy combining FEM simulations with expert knowledge, Sotech delivers innovative and effective facade cladding solutions tailored to meet complex design challenges. Explore how our approach can enhance your next project.\n\nLatest news, case studies and innovations in FACADE cladding\n\n10,000 Shingles Used in Hartlepool Leisure Centre\n\n10,000 Shingles Used in Landmark Coastal Facade Working alongside GT3 Architects, Wates and fa\u00e7ade installer Chemplas, Sotech has produced and supplied approximately 10,000 individual Optima Shingles (around 2,000m\u00b2) and 550 linear metres of coping for\u2026\n\nRead more\n\n * [ABOUT][1]\n* [Privacy][2]\n* [Terms][3]\n* [cpd training][4]\nTechnical +44 (0) 191 587 9213 | General Enquiries +44 (0) 191 587 2287\n[ [Sotech Optima] [Sotech Optima] ][5]\n\n[Sotech Optima][6]\n\nBespoke Metal Rainscreen Cladding & Facade Panel Systems\n* [Rainscreen Solutions][7]\n* * [Rainscreen Systems][8]\n* [Optima FC+, Secret Fix Hook On Rainscreen][9]\n* [Optima TFC+, Through Fix Cassette Rainscreen][10]\n* [Optima Edge, SECRET FIX, FLAT PANEL APPEARANCE][11]\n* [Optima FlatFix, Flate Plate Rainscreen][12]\n* [OPTIMA BrickTECH, Alternative to traditional brickwork][13]\n* [Planks][14]\n* [OPTIMA XTR Contour][15]\n* [Optima Clip Plank System][16]\n* [Optima Interlock Plank Rainscreen][17]\n* [Specialist Cladding][18]\n* [OPTIMA Shingles][19]\n* [OPTIMA MEADOW, Living Wall Rainscreen][20]\n* [Optima Vertex Spandrel][21]\n* [Ancillaries][22]\n* [Sotech Clip on Coping][23]\n* [Sotech Perforations][24]\n* [Sotech Flashings][25]\n* [Resources][26]\n* [What is Rainscreen Cladding?][27]\n* [Fire testing][28]\n* [CWCT][29]\n* [SAFE HANDS Promise][30]\n* [SUSTAINABILITY][31]\n* [EPD][32]\n* [Modelling Environment][33]\n* [SOTECH VR][34]\n* [LEARNING Zone & Showroom][35]\n* [Case Studies][36]\n* [NEWS][37]\n* [Downloads][38]\n* [Contact Us][39]\n\n[ Sign in ][40]\nSearch\n[ Cart 0 ][41]\n[ [Sotech Optima] [Sotech Optima] ][42]\n[ Cart 0 ][43]\n\n# Case Studies\n* [All][44]\n* [System][45]\n* [Material/Finish][46]\n* [Sector][47]\n* [Location][48]\n* [Recognition][49]\n* [Green Initiative][50]\n\n[Sotech Optima Shingles Hartlepool Leisure Centre 1]\n\n#### 10,000 Shingles Used in Hartlepool Leisure Centre\n\n10,000 Shingles Used in Landmark Coastal Facade Working alongside GT3 Architects, Wates and fa\u00e7ade\ninstaller Chemplas, Sotech has produced and supplied approximately 10,000 individual Optima Shingles\n(around 2,000m\u00b2) and 550 linear metres of coping for\u2026\n\n[Read more][51]\n[Stage - Facade Awards Best use of Aluminium Winner]\n\n#### The Stage\n\nWinner of the \u2018Best use of a Rainscreen System Using Aluminium\u2019 at the 2024 Facade Awards, The Stage\nhas established itself as an iconic project in Shoreditch, London. Working in collaboration with\nAlliance Facade Services\u2026\n\n[Read more][52]\n[250 City Road London]\n\n#### 250 City Road, London\n\n16,000m\u00b2 of Sotech\u2019s Optima FC+ Hook-on Rainscreen System and bespoke fa\u00e7ade detailing, fabricated\nfrom Alpolic A2 aluminium composite material, have been installed across two landmark residential\ntowers at 250 City Road in London. Designed by\u2026\n\n[Read more][53]\n[Island Quarter Nottingham-17]\n\n#### The Island Quarter\n\n1200m\u00b2 of Sotech\u2019s Optima FC+ system in PPC aluminium has been used in Island Quarter, one of the\nlargest and most transformative development projects in the UK. Designed by leading architectural\npractice Jestico + Whiles,\u2026\n\n[Read more][54]\n[Sotech rec"
