            "text": "* [ABOUT][1]\n* [Privacy][2]\n* [Terms][3]\n* [cpd training][4]\nTechnical +44 (0) 191 587 9213 | General Enquiries +44 (0) 191 587 2287\n[ [Sotech Optima] [Sotech Optima] ][5]\n\n[Sotech Optima][6]\n\nBespoke Metal Rainscreen Cladding & Facade Panel Systems\n* [Rainscreen Solutions][7]\n* * [Rainscreen Systems][8]\n* [Optima FC+, Secret Fix Hook On Rainscreen][9]\n* [Optima TFC+, Through Fix Cassette Rainscreen][10]\n* [Optima Edge, SECRET FIX, FLAT PANEL APPEARANCE][11]\n* [Optima FlatFix, Flate Plate Rainscreen][12]\n* [OPTIMA BrickTECH, Alternative to traditional brickwork][13]\n* [Planks][14]\n* [OPTIMA XTR Contour][15]\n* [Optima Clip Plank System][16]\n* [Optima Interlock Plank Rainscreen][17]\n* [Specialist Cladding][18]\n* [OPTIMA Shingles][19]\n* [OPTIMA MEADOW, Living Wall Rainscreen][20]\n* [Optima Vertex Spandrel][21]\n* [Ancillaries][22]\n* [Sotech Clip on Coping][23]\n* [Sotech Perforations][24]\n* [Sotech Flashings][25]\n* [Resources][26]\n* [What is Rainscreen Cladding?][27]\n* [Fire testing][28]\n* [CWCT][29]\n* [SAFE HANDS Promise][30]\n* [SUSTAINABILITY][31]\n* [EPD][32]\n* [Modelling Environment][33]\n* [SOTECH VR][34]\n* [LEARNING Zone & Showroom][35]\n* [Case Studies][36]\n* [NEWS][37]\n* [Downloads][38]\n* [Contact Us][39]\n\n[ Sign in ][40]\nSearch\n[ Cart 0 ][41]\n[ [Sotech Optima] [Sotech Optima] ][42]\n[ Cart 0 ][43]\n\n# Case Studies\n* [All][44]\n* [System][45]\n* [Material/Finish][46]\n* [Sector][47]\n* [Location][48]\n* [Recognition][49]\n* [Green Initiative][50]\n\n[Sotech Optima Shingles Hartlepool Leisure Centre 1]\n\n#### 10,000 Shingles Used in Hartlepool Leisure Centre\n\n10,000 Shingles Used in Landmark Coastal Facade Working alongside GT3 Architects, Wates and fa\u00e7ade\ninstaller Chemplas, Sotech has produced and supplied approximately 10,000 individual Optima Shingles\n(around 2,000m\u00b2) and 550 linear metres of coping for\u2026\n\n[Read more][51]\n[Stage - Facade Awards Best use of Aluminium Winner]\n\n#### The Stage\n\nWinner of the \u2018Best use of a Rainscreen System Using Aluminium\u2019 at the 2024 Facade Awards, The Stage\nhas established itself as an iconic project in Shoreditch, London. Working in collaboration with\nAlliance Facade Services\u2026\n\n[Read more][52]\n[250 City Road London]\n\n#### 250 City Road, London\n\n16,000m\u00b2 of Sotech\u2019s Optima FC+ Hook-on Rainscreen System and bespoke fa\u00e7ade detailing, fabricated\nfrom Alpolic A2 aluminium composite material, have been installed across two landmark residential\ntowers at 250 City Road in London. Designed by\u2026\n\n[Read more][53]\n[Island Quarter Nottingham-17]\n\n#### The Island Quarter\n\n1200m\u00b2 of Sotech\u2019s Optima FC+ system in PPC aluminium has been used in Island Quarter, one of the\nlargest and most transformative development projects in the UK. Designed by leading architectural\npractice Jestico + Whiles,\u2026\n\n[Read more][54]\n[Sotech reclad - Glasgow Harbour residential towers]\n\n#### Glasgow Harbour\n\n13,500m\u00b2 of Sotech\u2019s Optima TFC+ Through Fix Cassette system, fabricated from Novelis FF3 3mm\npre-coated aluminium, has been used in the reclad of the Glasgow Harbour residential towers,\nreplacing the non compliant material. The replacement\u2026\n\n[Read more][55]\n[The Filaments Reclad London]\n\n#### The Filaments, London: A Precision Retrofit with Optima TFC+\n\nWorking closely with installer OCL Reclad and main contractor Mount Anvil, Sotech has supplied over\n5,000m\u00b2 of Optima TFC+ in 3mm Aluminium J57S \u201cUp\u201d grade anodised aluminium for the reclad of The\nFilaments in London.\u2026\n\n[Read more][56]\n[Project Vita Coventry]\n\n#### VITA Coventry, Warwick Road\n\nA Stunning FaCade for a Landmark Development 4100m\u00b2 of Aluminium PPC (Adapta Vivendi Copper DS0010)\nin Optima FC+ has been used in the completion of the VITA Coventry student accommodation. \ufeffThe\ndevelopment consists of\u2026\n\n[Read more][57]\n[One Strawberry Lane Perforated Rainscreen]\n\n#### One Strawberry Lane\n\nBespoke perforated panels have been used in One Strawberry Lane, the new city centre HQ for Home\nGroup. Located right next to the famous Strawberry Pub and just a stone\u2019s throw from St. James\u2019\nPark\u2026\n\n[Read more][58]\n[Nottingham Trent School of Art and Design]\n\n#### Nottingham Trent University\u2019s Art and Design Building\n\nOptima TFC+ and Optima IPC (used exclusively for soffits) in 3.0mm and 2.0mm Aluminium J57S Up have\nbeen used in the design of Nottingham Trent University\u2019s Art and Design Building. The UA Regency\nGold 2\u2026\n\n[Read more][59]\n[ICOSS Sheffield University Optima TFC+ in 3mm Anodised Aluminium Rainscreen Cladding]\n\n#### ICOSS Building, Sheffield\n\nOptima TFC+ in 3mm Aluminium J57S UP Grade Anodised Blue Grey B717 has been used to reclad the ICOSS\nBuilding in Sheffield, an educational facility providing specialist research facilities and\nstate-of-the-art laboratories. Originally designed by\u2026\n\n[Read more][60]\n[Coventry University Faculty of Arts and Humanities building Gold Perforated Rainscreen Cladding]\n\n#### Coventry University, Faculty of Arts and Humanities\n\n2000m\u00b2 of 3.0mm Aluminium and 2.0mm Aluminium PPC (Interpon D2525) in Gold Splendour Y2205L and RAL\n7016 have been used in the redevelopment of Coventry University\u2019s Faculty of Arts and Humanities\nbuilding. A combination of\u2026\n\n[Read more][61]\n[Optima Shingles Napoleons Casino Leeds]\n\n#### Napoleons Casino, Leeds\n\nJ57S Anodised Aluminium SHINGLES in Regency Gold 1, 2, and 3 has been used in the refurbishment of\nNapoleon\u2019s Casino in Leeds. \ufeffThe architect Chapman Taylor selected the Optima Shingle system to\nachieve a\u2026\n\n[Read more][62]\n[Discovery Quay Phase 1 and 2]\n\n#### Discovery Quay\n\nWe\u2019re delighted to share the completed Discovery Quay phase 2 in Salford, Manchester. Sotech were\noriginally specified to provide Optima TFC in PPC Aluminium and Optima FC in Axalta PPC Aluminium in\nthe bold yellow\u2026\n\n[Read more][63]\n[Travelodge - Abbey Wood Optima TFC and Optima IPC Rainscreen Cladding 3]\n\n#### Travelodge, Abbey Wood\n\n890m2 of 3.0mm Aluminium in Optima TFC+ and 2.0mm Aluminium in Optima IPC was used in the completion\nof the bold and brand new Travelodge in Abbey Wood Retail Park. Optima TFC+ is Sotech\u2019s economical,\u2026\n\n[Read more][64]\n[Canaan Lane Primary School in Corten Edinburgh]\n\n#### Canaan Lane\n\n560m2 of 2.0mm Corten A has been used in the completion of the two-storey Canaan Lane Primary School\nin Edinburgh. Holmes Miller, the architect behind the project, opted for Corten material in a secret\nfix\u2026\n\n[Read more][65]\n[Christina Miller]\n\n#### Kings Buildings, The University of Edinburgh\n\n2200m2 Optima TFC+ 3.0mm in Aluminium Luxe Coat has been used in the reclad of the Christina Miller\nBuilding and the Alexander Graham Bell Building within The King\u2019s Buildings of Edinburgh University.\nThe buildings were\u2026\n\n[Read more][66]\n[Peterborough University Photo Credit Richard Fraser]\n\n#### Peterborough University\n\n672 m2 of Optima TFC+ in 5.0mm Aluminium PPC and 935 m2 of Optima FC+ 3.0mm Aluminium PPC* has been\nused in the completion of the \u00a330 million pound Anglia Ruskin University (ARU) in Peterborough.\u2026\n\n[Read more][67]\n[West End Quay London]\n\n#### West End Quay, London\n\n[CASE STUDY] 1100sqm of Optima FC+ in 3.0mm Aluminium Polyester Powder Coating finished in RAL 9006\nhas been used in the completion of West End Quay, situated in the heart of London. \ufeffWest End\u2026\n\n[Read more][68]\n[Ferry Lane London]\n\n#### Ferry Lane\n\n25,000m2 of 6063 T6 Aluminium Extrusions have been used in the completion of Ferry Lane in\nWalthamstow. This was the first large scale development of Sotech\u2019s extruded profiles range, now\nreferred to as Optima XTR\u2026\n\n[Read more][69]\n[40 Percival Street]\n\n#### Percival Street\n\n800sqm of Optima FC in 3mm J57S Up aluminium, anodised by United Anodisers in UnAcol\u2122 UA130-1,\nUA140-2, Anolok II \u2122 B711,B713,B715, was specified for 40 Percival Street in London. \ufeffA residential\ndevelopment owned by\u2026\n\n[Read more][70]\n[Bromley By Bow Extrusion]\n\n#### Imperial 2, Bromley by Bow\n\n300 m2 of Optima XTR Contour in 6063 T6 Aluminium Extrusion and 3000 m2 of Optima TFC+ in Aluminium\n3103 Grade has been used in the completion of Bromley-by-Bow in East London. \ufeffBromley-By-Bow is\u2026\n\n[Read more][71]\n[Abbey Place London]\n\n#### Abbey Place, London\n\n11,500m2 of Optima TFC+ in 3.0mm Aluminium PPC Interpon D2525 YW206F, Y4312I, Y4317I has been used\nin the completion of Abbey Place in London. \ufeffSitting within walking distance of Cross Rail station,\nwith excellent\u2026\n\n[Read more][72]\n[Leicester City Football Club Training Ground]\n\n#### Leicester City Football Club Training Ground\n\n5000m2 of Optima TFC+ in 3mm Aluminium PPC (Interpon) Y4207i `Corten Bond` has been used in the\ncompletion of the striking Leicester City Football Club training ground. As visible in the project\nphotos, the project\u2026\n\n[Read more][73]\n[Ashley Road East London Sotech]\n\n#### One Ashley Road, Ashley Road East\n\nOver 4000sqm of Optima TFC+ in 3mm Aluminium polyester powder coating has been used in the\ncompletion of One Ashley Road, near Tottenham\u2019s tube station in North London, with 5.0mm aluminium\nselected for column at\u2026\n\n[Read more][74]\n[Zig Zag pattern rainscreen cladding - LUSOM]\n\n#### Lancaster University School of Mathematics (LUSoM)\n\n300m2 of Optima FC+ in 3.0mm Aluminium PPC Interpon D2525 Y2217F has been used in the completion of\nLancaster University\u2019s School of Mathemtatics. Optima FC+ was specified in order to create the\nfeature `Zig-Zag` pattern.\u2026\n\n[Read more][75]\n[Spark Newcastle]\n\n#### The Spark\n\n1300m2 of Optima XPC in extruded aluminium 6063 T6 Grade has been used in the completion of The\nSpark commercial office space in Newcastle. \ufeffOptima XPC, an aluminium extrusion plank rainscreen\nsystem with a\u2026\n\n[Read more][76]\n[Kelaty House Perforation Patterned Design Rainscreen 2]\n\n#### Kelaty House, Wembley\n\nOver 9,500m2 of the brand new Optima FC+ Anodised Aluminium has been used in the ambitious\ncompletion of Kelaty House, a towering student accommodation and hotel in Wembley London. \ufeffWith three\ndifferent surface finishes\u2026\n\n[Read more][77]\n[New Bailey Plot C1 Manchester Optima FC+]\n\n#### Plot C1, English Cities Fund (ECF) \u2013 New Bailey, Salford Quays\n\n8300 SQM of Optima FC+, Optima FC+ perforated panels and Optima IPC (soffits) have been used in the\ncompletion of the 23-storey New Bailey building in Salford Quays. \ufeffOptima FC+ was selected for a\u2026\n\n[Read more][78]\n[Science Engineering and Environment Building Salford University]\n\n#### Science, Engineering & Environment Building, Salford University\n\n5500m2 of Optima TFC+ has been used in the completion of the brand new Science, Engineering and\nEnvironment building on Salford University\u2019s Peel Park campus. As you can see from the photos, a\nstriking colour\u2026\n\n[Read more][79]\n[Public Service Hub -Ellesmere Port Perforated Rainscreen Panels]\n\n#### Public Service Hub, Ellesmere Port\n\nThe striking Public Service Hub \u2013 Ellesmere Port \u2013 included 400m2 of Optima FC+ Solid & Perforated\nand Optima Clip-on Coping. Both systems were finished in Axalta\u2019s Supranodic Terra. The final\ndesign selected for the\u2026\n\n[Read more][80]\n[Vita Nottingham]\n\n#### Project Vita, Nottingham\n\n400m2 Optima TFC & 230m2 Window Panels 3mm Aluminium J57S UP in United Anodisers Anolok 543 has been\nused in the completion of Project Vita. The 323-bedroom student accommodation, located in the heart\nof Nottingham\u2026\n\n[Read more][81]\n[Project Medius Leicester]\n\n#### Project Medius, Leicester\n\n2500m2 Optima TFC in 4mm Alucobond A2 ACM Silver Metallic 500 has been used in the completion of\nProject Medius in Leicester. \ufeffPart of a wider \u00a350m project on the site of the former\u2026\n\n[Read more][82]\n[PEMC Nottingham]\n\n#### PEMC Nottingham\n\n675m2 of Sotech\u2019s Optima FC in 3.0mm PPC Aluminium 1050 Grade has been used in the completion of the\nPower Electronics, Machines and Control (PEMC) Research Group on Nottingham University\u2019s Jubilee\nCampus. Home to three\u2026\n\n[Read more][83]\n[Nottingham College City Hub]\n\n#### Nottingham College City Hub\n\n2400m2 of Optima TFC in 2mm Aluminium Axalta PPC has been used in the completion of the striking\nNottingham College City Hub, in addition to 800lm of Feature Fin Pressings & 200m2 of Optima XPC\u2026\n\n[Read more][84]\n"
