            "text": "ESE NOTES | | Civil Engineering Best Online Material\n\nSkip to content\n\nHome\nBlog\nCalculator\nAbout\nContact\n\nMenu\nCivil Engineering\nHighway Engineering\nSoil Mechanics\nSurveying\nOpen Channel Flow\nOpen Channel Flow \u2013 Introduction (Chapter-1)\nUniform Flow- Open Channel Flow (Chapter-2)\nEnergy Depth Relationship- Open Channel Flow (Chapter-3)\nGradually Varied Flow- Open Channel Flow (Chapter-4)\nRapidly Varied Flow: Hydraulic Jump- Open Channel Flow (Chapter-5)\nUnsteady Flow: Surge- Open Channel Flow (Chapter-6)\nPrevious Year Paper\nCivil Engineering PDF Notes\n\nEnvironmental Engineering Notes by Jaspal Sir\nSurveying &#038; Engineering Geology Notes by Jaspal Sir\nStructural Engineering\n[PDF] Engineering Mechanics Notes (Handwritten) by Jaspal Sir\nBuilding Construction Notes PDF by Jaspal Sir | Building Materials and Construction\nBuilding Materials PDF Handwritten Notes by Jaspal Sir | Building Materials and Construction\n[PDF] Strength of Materials PDF Notes by Jaspal Sir\n[PDF] Structure Analysis Notes by Jaspal Sir\n[PDF] Reinforced Cement Concrete Notes by Jaspal Sir\nDesign of Steel Structures PDF Notes by Jaspal Sir\nEstimation Costing and Valuation PDF Notes by Jaspal Sir\n[PDF] CPM &#038; PERT Notes by Jaspal Sir\nGeotechnical Engineering\nGeotechnical Engineering- Soil Mechanics PDF Notes by Jaspal Sir\nGeotechnical Engineering- Foundation Engineering Notes by Jaspal Sir\nTransportation Engineering\nHighway Engineering Pdf Notes by Jaspal Sir\n[PDF] Railway Engineering Notes by Jaspal Sir\nAirport Engineering Notes PDF by Jaspal Sir\nWater Resources Engineering\nFluid Mechanics Notes PDF by Jaspal Sir\n[PDF] Hydraulic Machines Notes by Jaspal Sir\n[PDF] Irrigation Engineering Notes by Jaspal Sir\nOpen Channel Flow Notes by Jaspal Sir\nEngineering Hydrology Notes by Jaspal Sir\n\nESE NOTES \u2013 One Destination for All Competitive Exams\n\ud83d\udcc4 Complete Syllabus \u2022 \u23f1 Exam Pattern \u2022 \ud83d\udcdd PYQs (10+ Years) \u2022 \ud83e\udde0 10K+ Quizzes \u2022 \ud83d\udcd8 Topic-wise Notes \u2022 &#038; More\n\nCovering 50+ Competitive Exams\n\n\ud83d\udcda SSC &#8211; CGL, CHSL, MTS &#038; More\n\ud83d\udcda RRB &#8211; NTPC, Group D, ALP &#038; More\n\ud83d\udcda UPSC &#8211; CSE, CDS, CAPF &#038; More\n\ud83d\udcda State PSC &#8211; UPPSC, BPSC, MPPSC &#038; More\n\ud83d\udcda Banking &#8211; IBPS PO, SBI Clerk &#038; More\n\ud83d\udcda ESE/IES &#8211; Technical + GS Full Coverage\n\ud83d\udcda GATE &#8211; All Branches Covered\n\ud83d\udcda More &#8211; Popular Exams\n\nStudents\n\nExams\n\nPYQs\n\nExams Overview\nExam Info \u00b7 Syllabus \u00b7 Salary \u00b7 PYQs \u00b7 Cutoff \u00b7 More\n\nExams Overview\n\nCalculator\n\nAll Exams 7\n\nSSC 3\n\nBanking 2\n\nRailway 2\n\nStart typing\u2026 Esc to close\n\nESE NOTES EDUCATION\n\nSkills Focused Online Courses\n\nCivil Engineering\n\nDownload App\n\nSTART LEARNING\n\nCalculationClub.Com\n\nIf you&#8217;re looking for a website that provides all types of calculators and conversion tools, then CalculationClub . com is your final destination. Whether you are a student, professional, or just curious, CalculationClub offers a variety of tools to help you solve any type of problem. Our collection includes unit converters , random generators, text tools, and much more.\n\nResultJano.Com Promotion\n\nResultJano.Com\n\nIf you\u2019re looking for a website that provides all types of government job updates\nand exam-related information, then ResultJano.com is your final destination.\nWhether you are a student, job seeker, or preparing for competitive exams,\nResultJano offers the latest notifications, admit cards, results, and much more.\nVisit ResultJano.Com\n\nIf you want to fill the SSC CGL 2026, then please visit Resultjano.com\nSSC CGL 2026 Recruitment &#8211; Apply Now for 12,256 Posts\n\nDirect Notes In PDF\n\nPDF Notes\n\nSurveying &#038; Engineering Geology Notes by Jaspal Sir\n\n3 July 2024\n\nHello, Engineers! Are you searching for the latest handwritten Surveying &amp; Engineering Geology Notes ? If yes, then you are on the right platform.\nRead More\n\nPDF Notes\n\nEngineering Hydrology Notes by Jaspal Sir\n\n3 July 2024\n\nHello, Engineers! Are you searching for the latest handwritten Engineering Hydrology Notes ? If yes, then you are on the right platform. A total 7 chapters are covered in these notes.\nRead More\n\nPDF Notes\n\nOpen Channel Flow Notes by Jaspal Sir\n\n3 July 2024\n\nHello, Engineers! Are you searching for the latest handwritten Open Channel Flow notes? If yes, then you are on the right platform. Total 6 Chapter Covered in this Notes.\nRead More\n\nPDF Notes\n\n[PDF] Irrigation Engineering Notes by Jaspal Sir\n\n3 July 2024\n\nHello, Engineers! Are you searching for the latest handwritten Irrigation Engineering Notes? If yes, then you are on the right platform. Total 11 Chapter Covered in this Notes.\nRead More\n\n&hellip;\nNext \u00bb\n\nSUBJECT\n\nSurveying\n\nHighway En..\n\nSoil Mech..\n\nNew Posts \u2713\n\nSSC JE PYQP\n\nSSC JE Electrical Engineering PYQ Papers PDF (2009\u20132024)\n\n26 December 2025\n\nPractice SSC JE Electrical Engineering PYQP to understand exam pattern, important topics, and question trends. Download year-wise SSC JE EE papers.\nRead More\n\nSSC JE PYQP\n\nSSC JE Mechanical Engineering PYQ Papers PDF (2008\u20132024)\n\n25 December 2025\n\nDownload SSC JE Mechanical Engineering PYQ Papers PDF (2008\u20132024) for Prelims &amp; Mains. Year-wise question papers with exam pattern &amp; preparation tips.\nRead More\n\nSSC JE PYQP\n\nSSC JE Previous Year Question Paper PDF- Civil (2010\u20132024)\n\n11 October 2025\n\nDownload SSC JE Civil previous year question papers in PDF. Understand exam pattern, important topics, and question trends for SSC JE CE.\nRead More\n\nPDF Notes\n\nSurveying &#038; Engineering Geology Notes by Jaspal Sir\n\n3 July 2024\n\nHello, Engineers! Are you searching for the latest handwritten Surveying &amp; Engineering Geology Notes ? If yes, then you are on the right platform.\nRead More\n\n&hellip;\nNext \u00bb\n\nOpen Channel Flow \u2713\n\nOpen Channel Flow\n\nOpen Channel Flow &#8211; Introduction (Chapter-1)\n\n6 June 2022\n\nOpen channel flow refers to the flow of liquid in channel open to atmosphere or in partially filled conduit (Pipe). Example- River, Flood, Rivulets, Torrent, Sewers carrying sewage, Rode side Gutter. Detailed discuss about OCF.\nRead More\n\nOpen Channel Flow\n\nUniform Flow- Open Channel Flow (Chapter-2)\n\n12 June 2022\n\nA flow in an open channel is said to be uniform if its properties remain constant with respect to space. Detailed discussion about Uniform Flow.\nRead More\n\nOpen Channel Flow\n\nEnergy Depth Relationship- Open Channel Flow (Chapter-3)\n\n12 June 2022\n\nEnergy depth relationship is the third chapter of the open channel flow. Detailed discussion about specific energy, critical depth, relationship between specific energy and depth of flow, section factor z, relation between discharge &amp; depth of flow, channel transition.\nRead More\n\nOpen Channel Flow\n\nGradually Varied Flow- Open Channel Flow (Chapter-4)\n\n12 June 2022\n\nThe gradually varied flow (GVF) is defined as steady non- uniform flow, where the depth of flow varies gradually from section to section along the length of channel. (A steady non-uniform flow in a prismatic channel with gradual changes in its water surface elevation is termed as gradually varied flow (GVF).\nRead More\n\nNext \u00bb\n\nSurveying \u2713\n\nSurveying\n\nFundamentals Of Surveying (Part-1)\n\n2 August 2021\n\nIn fundamentals of surveying (part-1), we details analysis about surveying, classification of survey, principal of surveying, instruments used for various types of measurement.Etc\nRead More\n\nSurveying\n\nFundamentals Of Surveying (Part-2)\n\n4 August 2021\n\nIn fundamentals of surveying (part-2), we details analysis about plan &amp; map, scale, representation of scale- engineer\u2019s scale, representation fraction (rf), graphical scale. Shrinkage factor or shrinkage ratio, error due to shrinkage of map, error due to wrong measuring scale, type of scales- plane scale, diagonal scale, vernier scale (direct vernier, retrograde vernier, extended vernier, double vernier).\nRead More\n\nSurveying\n\nLinear Measurements (Chain Survey)\n\n9 August 2021\n\nIn liner measurements,we details discuss about procedure in chain surveying,basic definition of chain surveying- main station, tie station, main survey line, tie line/ subsidiary line, base line, check line/ proof line, offset, chainage, well conditioned triangle.Correction in chaining,limiting length of offsets.\nRead More\n\nSurveying\n\nEquipment Used In Chain Surveying\n\n11 August 2021\n\nIn equipment used in chain surveying,we details discuss about surveying chain, types of chain- revenue chain, gunter\u2019s chain, engineer\u2019s chain, metric chain, suitability of chain, unsuitability of chain, units of measurement, tapes-cloth or linen tape, metallic tape, steel tape, invar tape, pegs, arrows, ranging rods, offset rods, plumb bob, clinometer, cross-staff, optical square, prism square, chain survey instruments, distance measuring device, instruments used for various types of measurement\nRead More\n\n&hellip;\nNext \u00bb\n\nHighway Engineering\n\nHighway Engineering\n\nPavement Design- Highway Engineering (Chapter-4)\n\n4 July 2022\n\nPavement is a load-bearing &amp; load-distributing component of a road. We need to consider all types of vehicles for the geometrical design, but only vehicles with significant heavy loads are considered for pavement design. These vehicles are generally commercial vehicles. As per IRC, vehicles having a gross load greater than 3 tons are called commercial vehicles.\nRead More\n\nHighway Engineering\n\nTraffic Engineering &#8211; Highway Engineering (Chapter-3)\n\n2 February 2022\n\nThe basic objective of traffic engineering is to achieve free &amp; rapid flow of traffic with least no of accidents. For this various studies are carried out. These studies are divided into- Traffic Characteristics, Traffic Studies and Analysis, Traffic Control Regulation.\nRead More\n\nHighway Engineering\n\nGeometric Design Of Highway- Highway Engineering (Chapter 2)\n\n31 May 2021\n\nGeometric Design of Highway Geometric Design of a highway deals with all the dimensions and layout of visual features of a highway such that it\nRead More\n\nHighway Engineering\n\nHighway Engineering: Introduction (Chapter 1)- Modes of Transportation, Development of Road, Mr. Jayakar Committee, Classification of Road, Road Patterns\n\n29 April 2021\n\nThe process of conveyance from one point to another is termed transportation. In this article, we elaborate on the first chapter of Highway Engineering in detail.\nRead More\n\nSoil Mechanics\n\nProperties of Soils\n\nDifference Between Organic and Inorganic Soils | Properties of Soil | Soil Mechanics\n\n11 April 2021\n\nLiquid limit of inorganic soil not of volcanic organic rarely has a value greater 100 %. Organic soil has a generally high value of liquid limit (liquid limit&gt;50%) but their plastic limit is also comparatively high, hence their plastic index values are not as high as its liquid limit.\nRead More\n\nProperties of Soils\n\nCollapsibility | Properties of Soil | Soil Mechanics\n\n11 April 2021\n\nThe soil which shows a large decrease in its volume due to an increase in its water content without any increase in external pressure or load is termed as collapsible soil. Ex- Loess soil, Sand Dunes, Fine sand &amp; Silt silty cemented due to the presence of calcium. And the properties of collapsible soil is called collapsibility.\nRead More\n\nProperties of Soils\n\nSensitivity, Thixotropy &#038; Activity | Properties of Soil | Soil Mechanics\n\n11 April 2021\n\nSensitivity is defined as the ratio of Unconfined Compressive Strength in an undisturbed natural state to Unconfined Compressive Strength of soil in the remolded state.\nRead More\n\nProperties of Soils\n\nConsistency Index, Liquidity Index &#038; Toughness Index | Properties of Soil | Soil Mechanics\n\n9 April 2021\n\nConsistency Index is defined as the ration of the difference of liquid limit and natural water content to the plasticity index. Toughness Index is a ratio of IP &amp; IF.\nRead More\n\n&hellip;\nNext \u00bb\n\nStay updated with what's happening at ESENOTES\n\nHome\nBlog\nCalculator\nAbout\nContact\n\nSearch for:\n\nSearch\n\nSearch\n\nFOLLOW US\n\nHome\nBlog\nAbout\nContact\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms &#038; Conditions\n\nCopyright &copy; 2026 ESE NOTES | Powered by ESE NOTES | Sarthak\n\nScroll to To"
