            "url": "https://foodbusinessmea.com/team",
            "text": "[Skip to content][1]\n[[Food Business Middle East & Africa \u2013 No.1 Food & Beverage Formulation, Processing & Packaging\nPublication ]][2]\n\n[Send Press Releases][3] | [Advertise with Us][4]\n* [HOME][5]\n* [SECTORS][6]Show sub menu\n* [BEVERAGES][7]\n* [MEAT, POULTRY & FISH][8]\n* [COFFEE, TEA & COCOA][9]\n* [SUGAR & CONFECTIONERY][10]\n* [MAGAZINE][11]Show sub menu\n* [ABOUT FOOD BUSINESS MIDDLE EAST & AFRICA][12]\n* [PAST MAGAZINE ISSUES][13]\n* [SUBSCRIBE TO OUR E-NEWSLETTERS][14]\n* [CALL FOR ARTICLE CONTRIBUTORS][15]\n* [PRESS RELEASES][16]\n* [ADVERTISE][17]Show sub menu\n* [ADVERTISE WITH US \u2013 PRINT & DIGITAL][18]\n* [MEDIA KIT & EDITORIAL CALENDAR][19]\n* [SEND ADVERTISER ENQUIRY][20]\n* OUR EVENTSShow sub menu\n* [AFRICA FOOD MANUFACTURING EXPOS][21]\n* [KENYA FOOD & DRINK FESTIVAL][22]\n* [AFRICA MANUFACTURING AWARDS][23]\n* [AFRICA PACKAGING EXPOS][24]\n* [AFRICA FARMTECH EXPOS][25]\n* [AFRICA DAIRY INNOVATIONS SUMMIT][26]\n* [AFRICA HOTELS & RESTAURANTS EXPOS][27]\n* [AFRICA FOOD SAFETY SUMMIT][28]\n* [RELATED MAGAZINES][29]Show sub menu\n* [DAIRY BUSINESS MIDDLE EAST & AFRICA][30]\n* [MILLING MIDDLE EAST & AFRICA][31]\n* [FEED BUSINESS MIDDLE EAST & AFRICA][32]\n* [SUSTAINABLE PACKAGING MIDDLE EAST & AFRICA][33]\n* [HORECA MIDDLE EAST & AFRICA][34]\n* [AGRITECH MIDDLE EAST & AFRICA][35]\n* [HOME & PERSONAL CARE MIDDLE EAST & AFRICA][36]\n* [HEALTHCARE MIDDLE EAST & AFRICA][37]\n* [CONTACTS][38]\n\nMenu\nSearch Search\n\n# Team Europe commits to supporting sustainable farming of cocoa in Ivory Coast\n\nPublished November 4, 2022\n\n**IVORY COAST \u2013 The European Union and its partners have announced they are raising 450 million\neuros (US$442 million) to support Ivory Coast\u2019s push to tackle child labour and deforestation linked\nto cocoa production, while also improving farmer pay.**\n\nTeam Europe, made up of the EU, its member states and multilateral European lenders, indicated that\nthe new funding would boost the strategy by Ivory Coast, the world\u2019s top cocoa grower, to make\nproduction of the key chocolate ingredient more sustainable, reports *Bloomberg*.\n\nThe financial backing will strengthen the partnership between Team Europe and the cocoa-producing\ncountries, and aims at ensuring a decent living income for farmers, halting deforestation and\neliminating child labour.\n\nThe announcement follows the ongoing dialogue on sustainable cocoa, dubbed the \u2018Cocoa Talks\u2019,\ninvolving the EU and public and private stakeholders, along with selected representatives of the two\nmain producing countries, Ivory Coast and Ghana.\n\nThe objective of this dialogue is to enhance cooperation and coordination to support sustainable\ncocoa production in the framework of the Living Income Differential (LID) initiative, launched by\nthe two producer countries to ensure decent revenue to local farmers.\n\nIvory Coast and Ghana boycotted last month\u2019s World Cocoa Foundation Partnership Meeting in Brussels,\nwhere a group representing 80% of the industry met to discuss sustainability issues across the\nsector.\n\nAs *ConfectioneryNews* reports, both countries told the WCF they would not attend because of pricing\nissues regarding their beans.\n\nOther than the funding, the EU, which buys about 60% of the top producers\u2019 cocoa, is planning new\nlegislation that would compel exporters to ensure all their beans are certified as early as 2024 to\nprove the supply chain didn\u2019t use child labour or cause deforestation.\n\nLess than 15% of Ivory Coast\u2019s cocoa and only approximately 12% of beans from Ghana, the world\u2019s\nsecond largest cocoa producer, are certified, according to regulators.\n\nCocoa is a major contributor to export earnings, as well as the main source of livelihoods for\nalmost seven million farmers in Ivory Coast and Ghana. Indirectly, it contributes to the livelihoods\nof further 50 million people.\n\nAt the same time, cocoa production entails particular risks relating to child labour, low revenues\nfor local farmers, deforestation and forest degradation, according to the EU \u2013 the world\u2019s largest\nimporter of cocoa, accounting for 60% of world imports.\n\nAt an individual capacity, companies such as Mondel\u0113z International are continuing to undertaken\ndifferent projects in the cocoa growing regions to ensure a more sustainable and integrated farming\napproach.\n\nThe multinational confectionery has launched the next phase of its Cocoa Life program backed by an\nadditional US$600 million through 2030, bringing its total investment to US$1 billion since the\nstart of the program.\n\nBacked by the additional financing, Mondel\u0113z seeks to increase the number of farming households\nreaching a living income, enhance child protection systems and access to quality education in Cocoa\nLife communities, and seek no deforestation on Cocoa Life farms globally.\n\nCocoa Life is helping to address these challenges holistically across six cocoa-growing countries:\nGhana, C\u00f4te d\u2019Ivoire, Indonesia, Dominican Republic, India and Brazil.\n\n*For all the latest food industry news from Africa and the World, subscribe to\nour **[NEWSLETTER][39]**, follow us on **[Twitter][40] **and **[LinkedIn][41]**, like us\non [**Facebook**][42] and subscribe to our [**YouTube** ][43]channel.*\n\nNewer Post\n\n[[Thumbnail for Team Europe commits to supporting sustainable farming of cocoa in Ivory Coast\n]][44]\nNovember 4, 2022\n\n### [Malawian small-holder farmers to benefit from US$12.3m issued by European Investment Bank][45]\n\nOlder Post\n\n[[Thumbnail for Team Europe commits to supporting sustainable farming of cocoa in Ivory Coast\n]][46]\nNovember 4, 2022\n\n### [IFAD issues US$2m to Mozambican microfinance bank to support small-scale producers][47]\n\nSearch\nSearch\n\nLATEST DIGITAL MAGAZINE\n\nUPCOMING PARTNER EVENTS\n\n[**AFMASS Food Expo Kenya & Eastern Africa**][48] \u2013 July 15-17, 2026 \u2013 Nairobi, Kenya\n\n**[Africa Manufacturing Awards][49]** \u2013 July 16, 2026 \u2013 Nairobi, Kenya\n\n[**AFMASS Food Expo Nigeria & Western Africa**][50] \u2013 September 15-17, 2026 \u2013 Lagos, Nigeria\n\n[**SIAL Paris**][51] \u2013 October 17-21, 2026 \u2013 Paris Norde Villepinte, Paris, Francs\n\n*To partner with us to promote your event, [contact us][52]. Terms and conditions apply*\n\nTRENDING NEWS TODAY\n* [Diageo CEO Dave Lewis targetting cost cuts, staff reductions ][53] June 19, 2026\n* [Campari Group Executive Patrick Piana appointed President of Spirits Europe ][54] June 19, 2026\n* [Japanese hotel chains increase certified seafood purchases][55] June 18, 2026\n* [AB InBev appoints Mondelez CEO Dirk Van de Put as Chairman ][56] June 18, 2026\n* [Tongaat Hullett avoids liquidation as IDC, Vision Consortium strike rescue deal][57] June 17,\n2026\n\nNews Archives\n\nNews Archives Select Month June 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 January 2026\nDecember 2025 November 2025 October 2025 September 2025 August 2025 July 2025 June 2025 May 2025\nApril 2025 March 2025 February 2025 January 2025 December 2024 November 2024 October 2024 September\n2024 August 2024 July 2024 June 2024 May 2024 April 2024 March 2024 February 2024 January 2024\nDecember 2023 November 2023 October 2023 September 2023 August 2023 July 2023 June 2023 May 2023\nApril 2023 March 2023 February 2023 January 2023 December 2022 November 2022 October 2022 September\n2022 August 2022 July 2022 June 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 February 2022 January 2022\nDecember 2021 November 2021 October 2021 September 2021 August 2021 July 2021 June 2021 May 2021\nApril 2021 March 2021 February 2021 January 2021 December 2020 November 2020\n\n### **ABOUT US**\n\nWe organise some of the most impactful face-to-face and virtual trade events and publish leading\nmagazines and websites that bring Africa to the World and the World to Africa. We believe that when\npeople come together, networks grow, and businesses thrive.\n\nFind more about us on our corporate website [www.fwafrica.net][58]\n\n### **QUICK LINKS**\n\n[Advertise with Us][59]\n\n[Send Us Press Releases][60]\n\n### **RELATED MAGAZINES**\n\n[Dairy Business Middle East & Africa][61]\n\n[Milling Middle East & Africa][62]\n\n[Feed Business Middle East & Africa][63]\n\n[HORECA Middle East & Africa][64]\n\n[Sustainable Packaging Middle East & Africa][65]\n\n[Home & Personal Care Middle East & Africa][66]\n\n[AgriTech Middle East & Africa][67]\n\n[HealthCare Middle East & Africa][68]\n\n### **CONTACT US**\n\nFW Africa\n\nP.O. Box 1874-00621, Nairobi, Kenya\n\nTel: +254 725 34 39 32\n\nEmail: info(at)fwafrica.net\n\n\u00a9 2026 Food Business Middle East & Africa - No.1 Food & Beverage Formulation, Processing & Packaging\nPublication .\n\n[1]: #page__main\n[2]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/\n[3]: https://foodbusinessmea.com/press-releases/\n[4]: https://foodbusinessmea.com/advertise/\n[5]: https://www.foodbusinessafrica.com/\n[6]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/beverages/\n[7]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/beverages/\n[8]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/meat-poultry/\n[9]: https://www.foodbusinessafrica.com/coffee-tea-cocoa/\n[10]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/sugar-confectionery/\n[11]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/about/\n[12]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/about/\n[13]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/past-issues/\n[14]: http://eepurl.com/HuyXT\n[15]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/contributors/\n[16]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/press-releases/\n[17]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/advertise/\n[18]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/advertise/\n[19]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/media-kit-editorial-calendar/\n[20]: https://www.fwafrica.net/advertising-webinar-enquiries/\n[21]: https://www.afmass.com\n[22]: https://www.kenyafooddrinkfestival.com\n[23]: http://www.manawards.fwafrica.net\n[24]: https://www.afripackexpo.com\n[25]: https://www.africafarmtechexpo.com\n[26]: https://africadairysummit.com\n[27]: https://www.africahorecaexpo.com\n[28]: https://www.africafoodsafetysummit.com\n[29]: https://www.foodsafetyafrica.net/\n[30]: https://www.DAIRYbusinessafrica.com\n[31]: https://www.millingmea.com\n[32]: https://animalfeedmea.com\n[33]: https://www.sustainabilitymea.com\n[34]: https://HOTELHOSPITALITYMEA.com\n[35]: https://www.agritechmea.com\n[36]: https://www.hpcmagmea.com\n[37]: https://www.healthcaremea.com\n[38]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/contact/\n[39]: https://us4.list-manage.com/subscribe?u=8dacba15942964188af1f3c10&id=529878f093\n[40]: https://twitter.com/FoodBizAfrica\n[41]: https://ke.linkedin.com/company/food-business-africa-official-page\n[42]: https://www.facebook.com/FoodBusinessAfrica\n[43]: https://www.youtube.com/c/FWAFRICATV\n[44]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/malawian-small-holder-farmers-to-benefit-from-us12-3m-issued-b\ny-european-investment-bank-2/\n[45]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/malawian-small-holder-farmers-to-benefit-from-us12-3m-issued-b\ny-european-investment-bank-2/\n[46]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/ifad-issues-us2m-to-mozambican-microfinance-bank-to-support-sm\nall-scale-producers/\n[47]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/ifad-issues-us2m-to-mozambican-microfinance-bank-to-support-sm\nall-scale-producers/\n[48]: https://www.afmass.com/east\n[49]: http://www.manawards.fwafrica.net/food\n[50]: https://www.afmass.com/west\n[51]: http://www.sialparis.com/en\n[52]: https://www.foodbusinessafrica.com/contact/\n[53]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/diageo-ceo-dave-lewis-targetting-cost-cuts-staff-reductions/\n[54]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/campari-group-executive-patrick-piana-appointed-president-of-s\npirits-europe/\n[55]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/japanese-hotel-chains-increase-certified-seafood-purchases/\n[56]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/ab-inbev-appoints-mondelez-ceo-dirk-van-de-put-as-chairman/\n[57]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/tongaat-hullett-avoids-liquidation-as-idc-vision-consortium-st\nrike-rescue-deal/\n[58]: https://www.fwafrica.net\n[59]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/advertise\n[60]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/press-releases\n[61]: https://www.dairybusinessmea.com\n[62]: https://www.millingmea.com\n[63]: https://www.feedbusinessmea.com\n[64]: https://www.horecamea.com\n[65]: https://www.sustainabilitymea.com\n[66]: https://www.hpcmagmea.com\n[67]: https://www.agritechmea.com\n["
