          {
            "url": "https://foodbusinessmea.com/leadership",
            "text": "[Skip to content][1]\n[[Food Business Middle East & Africa \u2013 No.1 Food & Beverage Formulation, Processing & Packaging\nPublication ]][2]\n\n[Send Press Releases][3] | [Advertise with Us][4]\n* [HOME][5]\n* [SECTORS][6]Show sub menu\n* [BEVERAGES][7]\n* [MEAT, POULTRY & FISH][8]\n* [COFFEE, TEA & COCOA][9]\n* [SUGAR & CONFECTIONERY][10]\n* [MAGAZINE][11]Show sub menu\n* [ABOUT FOOD BUSINESS MIDDLE EAST & AFRICA][12]\n* [PAST MAGAZINE ISSUES][13]\n* [SUBSCRIBE TO OUR E-NEWSLETTERS][14]\n* [CALL FOR ARTICLE CONTRIBUTORS][15]\n* [PRESS RELEASES][16]\n* [ADVERTISE][17]Show sub menu\n* [ADVERTISE WITH US \u2013 PRINT & DIGITAL][18]\n* [MEDIA KIT & EDITORIAL CALENDAR][19]\n* [SEND ADVERTISER ENQUIRY][20]\n* OUR EVENTSShow sub menu\n* [AFRICA FOOD MANUFACTURING EXPOS][21]\n* [KENYA FOOD & DRINK FESTIVAL][22]\n* [AFRICA MANUFACTURING AWARDS][23]\n* [AFRICA PACKAGING EXPOS][24]\n* [AFRICA FARMTECH EXPOS][25]\n* [AFRICA DAIRY INNOVATIONS SUMMIT][26]\n* [AFRICA HOTELS & RESTAURANTS EXPOS][27]\n* [AFRICA FOOD SAFETY SUMMIT][28]\n* [RELATED MAGAZINES][29]Show sub menu\n* [DAIRY BUSINESS MIDDLE EAST & AFRICA][30]\n* [MILLING MIDDLE EAST & AFRICA][31]\n* [FEED BUSINESS MIDDLE EAST & AFRICA][32]\n* [SUSTAINABLE PACKAGING MIDDLE EAST & AFRICA][33]\n* [HORECA MIDDLE EAST & AFRICA][34]\n* [AGRITECH MIDDLE EAST & AFRICA][35]\n* [HOME & PERSONAL CARE MIDDLE EAST & AFRICA][36]\n* [HEALTHCARE MIDDLE EAST & AFRICA][37]\n* [CONTACTS][38]\n\nMenu\nSearch Search\n\n# Leadership shake-up in Australian wine sector: TWE appoints Sam Fischer as CEO, Vinarchy names\n# Danny Celoni Chief Executive\n\nTwo major Australian wine companies announce new leadership as they position for future growth and\ninternational expansion.\n\nPublished May 16, 2025\n\n**AUSTRALIA \u2013 Australian wine giant Treasury Wine Estates (TWE) has announced the appointment of Sam\nFischer as its new Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director, following a strategic succession\nplanning process and a global executive search. **\n\nFischer, currently the CEO of Lion, will officially assume the role on 27 October 2025, subject to\nregulatory approvals.\n\nFischer will replace Tim Ford, who has held the position since 2020. Ford will remain in the role\nuntil 30 September to support a smooth leadership transition, according to the company\u2019s filing to\nthe Australian Securities Exchange.\n\nTWE is best known for its flagship brand Penfolds and has undergone significant transformation under\nFord\u2019s leadership, including navigating the pandemic, responding to Chinese tariffs on Australian\nwine, and implementing a divisional operating model centered around premium wine labels.\n\nTWE Chairman John Mullen praised Ford\u2019s contributions and expressed confidence in Fischer\u2019s ability\nto lead the company through its next phase.\n\n*\u201cSam brings proven CEO credentials, exceptional strategic acumen, and deep expertise in alcohol\nbeverages, consumer goods, and luxury brand building, accompanied by a strong track record of\ndriving business growth,\u201d* Mullen stated.\n\nHe added that Fischer emerged as the top candidate from a highly competitive field during the global\nsearch.\n\nFischer has over 30 years of experience in the alcoholic beverage, luxury brand, and consumer goods\nindustries.\n\nAt Lion \u2014 a subsidiary of Japan\u2019s Kirin Group \u2014 Fischer has led operations across Australia, New\nZealand, and the United States, overseeing beer, wine, spirits, and ready-to-drink products.\n\n**Vinarchy new CEO**\n\nIn a parallel development, newly formed wine company Vinarchy has appointed Danny Celoni as its CEO.\nCeloni will assume the role in August 2025, bringing with him decades of experience in the beverage\nindustry.\n\nVinarchy was established last month following the acquisition of wine assets from Pernod Ricard by\nAccolade Wines\u2019 parent company, Australian Wine Holdco Limited (AWL).\n\nCeloni\u2019s career includes 18 years in leadership roles at Diageo in the Asia-Pacific region and over\nthree years as CEO of PepsiCo Australia and New Zealand.\n\nMost recently, he served as CEO of Carlton & United Breweries, a Melbourne-based subsidiary of Asahi\nGroup.\n\nCommenting on his new role, Celoni said, *\u201cVinarchy is well positioned to play a leading role in the\nfuture growth and expansion of the wine category.\u201d ** *\n\nExecutive Chairman Ben Clarke described Celoni as a transformational leader with a growth mindset\nand a strong record of achieving category leadership through customer-focused strategies.\n\nVinarchy now includes Accolade Wines and the former Pernod Ricard wine operations in Australia, New\nZealand, and Spain.\n\nWith A$1.5 billion (US$960 million) in annual net sales, 1,600 employees, and 11 wineries across\nfour countries, the company produces more than 32 million nine-litre cases annually.\n\n*Sign up [HERE][39] to receive our email newsletters with the latest news and insights from Africa\nand around the world, and follow us on our [WhatsApp channel][40] for updates.*\n\nNewer Post\n\n[[Thumbnail for Leadership shake-up in Australian wine sector: TWE appoints Sam Fischer as CEO,\nVinarchy names Danny Celoni Chief Executive ]][41]\nMay 16, 2025\n\n### [Kenya secures US$95.09M to revive four major sugar mills under 30-year lease agreements ][42]\n\nOlder Post\n\n[[Thumbnail for Leadership shake-up in Australian wine sector: TWE appoints Sam Fischer as CEO,\nVinarchy names Danny Celoni Chief Executive ]][43]\nMay 16, 2025\n\n### [Nigerian Breweries appoints Thibaut Boidin as CEO ][44]\n\nSearch\nSearch\n\nLATEST DIGITAL MAGAZINE\n\nUPCOMING PARTNER EVENTS\n\n[**AFMASS Food Expo Kenya & Eastern Africa**][45] \u2013 July 15-17, 2026 \u2013 Nairobi, Kenya\n\n**[Africa Manufacturing Awards][46]** \u2013 July 16, 2026 \u2013 Nairobi, Kenya\n\n[**AFMASS Food Expo Nigeria & Western Africa**][47] \u2013 September 15-17, 2026 \u2013 Lagos, Nigeria\n\n[**SIAL Paris**][48] \u2013 October 17-21, 2026 \u2013 Paris Norde Villepinte, Paris, Francs\n\n*To partner with us to promote your event, [contact us][49]. Terms and conditions apply*\n\nTRENDING NEWS TODAY\n* [Diageo CEO Dave Lewis targetting cost cuts, staff reductions ][50] June 19, 2026\n* [Campari Group Executive Patrick Piana appointed President of Spirits Europe ][51] June 19, 2026\n* [Japanese hotel chains increase certified seafood purchases][52] June 18, 2026\n* [AB InBev appoints Mondelez CEO Dirk Van de Put as Chairman ][53] June 18, 2026\n* [Tongaat Hullett avoids liquidation as IDC, Vision Consortium strike rescue deal][54] June 17,\n2026\n\nNews Archives\n\nNews Archives Select Month June 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 January 2026\nDecember 2025 November 2025 October 2025 September 2025 August 2025 July 2025 June 2025 May 2025\nApril 2025 March 2025 February 2025 January 2025 December 2024 November 2024 October 2024 September\n2024 August 2024 July 2024 June 2024 May 2024 April 2024 March 2024 February 2024 January 2024\nDecember 2023 November 2023 October 2023 September 2023 August 2023 July 2023 June 2023 May 2023\nApril 2023 March 2023 February 2023 January 2023 December 2022 November 2022 October 2022 September\n2022 August 2022 July 2022 June 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 February 2022 January 2022\nDecember 2021 November 2021 October 2021 September 2021 August 2021 July 2021 June 2021 May 2021\nApril 2021 March 2021 February 2021 January 2021 December 2020 November 2020\n\n### **ABOUT US**\n\nWe organise some of the most impactful face-to-face and virtual trade events and publish leading\nmagazines and websites that bring Africa to the World and the World to Africa. We believe that when\npeople come together, networks grow, and businesses thrive.\n\nFind more about us on our corporate website [www.fwafrica.net][55]\n\n### **QUICK LINKS**\n\n[Advertise with Us][56]\n\n[Send Us Press Releases][57]\n\n### **RELATED MAGAZINES**\n\n[Dairy Business Middle East & Africa][58]\n\n[Milling Middle East & Africa][59]\n\n[Feed Business Middle East & Africa][60]\n\n[HORECA Middle East & Africa][61]\n\n[Sustainable Packaging Middle East & Africa][62]\n\n[Home & Personal Care Middle East & Africa][63]\n\n[AgriTech Middle East & Africa][64]\n\n[HealthCare Middle East & Africa][65]\n\n### **CONTACT US**\n\nFW Africa\n\nP.O. Box 1874-00621, Nairobi, Kenya\n\nTel: +254 725 34 39 32\n\nEmail: info(at)fwafrica.net\n\n\u00a9 2026 Food Business Middle East & Africa - No.1 Food & Beverage Formulation, Processing & Packaging\nPublication .\n\n[1]: #page__main\n[2]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/\n[3]: https://foodbusinessmea.com/press-releases/\n[4]: https://foodbusinessmea.com/advertise/\n[5]: https://www.foodbusinessafrica.com/\n[6]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/beverages/\n[7]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/beverages/\n[8]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/meat-poultry/\n[9]: https://www.foodbusinessafrica.com/coffee-tea-cocoa/\n[10]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/sugar-confectionery/\n[11]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/about/\n[12]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/about/\n[13]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/past-issues/\n[14]: http://eepurl.com/HuyXT\n[15]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/contributors/\n[16]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/press-releases/\n[17]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/advertise/\n[18]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/advertise/\n[19]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/media-kit-editorial-calendar/\n[20]: https://www.fwafrica.net/advertising-webinar-enquiries/\n[21]: https://www.afmass.com\n[22]: https://www.kenyafooddrinkfestival.com\n[23]: http://www.manawards.fwafrica.net\n[24]: https://www.afripackexpo.com\n[25]: https://www.africafarmtechexpo.com\n[26]: https://africadairysummit.com\n[27]: https://www.africahorecaexpo.com\n[28]: https://www.africafoodsafetysummit.com\n[29]: https://www.foodsafetyafrica.net/\n[30]: https://www.DAIRYbusinessafrica.com\n[31]: https://www.millingmea.com\n[32]: https://animalfeedmea.com\n[33]: https://www.sustainabilitymea.com\n[34]: https://HOTELHOSPITALITYMEA.com\n[35]: https://www.agritechmea.com\n[36]: https://www.hpcmagmea.com\n[37]: https://www.healthcaremea.com\n[38]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/contact/\n[39]: https://us4.list-manage.com/subscribe?u=8dacba15942964188af1f3c10&id=529878f093\n[40]: https://whatsapp.com/channel/0029VavIz0fHltYGqAjDqe1o\n[41]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/kenya-secures-us95-09m-to-revive-four-major-sugar-mills-under-\n30-year-lease-agreements/\n[42]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/kenya-secures-us95-09m-to-revive-four-major-sugar-mills-under-\n30-year-lease-agreements/\n[43]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/nigerian-breweries-appoints-thibaut-boidin-as-ceo/\n[44]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/nigerian-breweries-appoints-thibaut-boidin-as-ceo/\n[45]: https://www.afmass.com/east\n[46]: http://www.manawards.fwafrica.net/food\n[47]: https://www.afmass.com/west\n[48]: http://www.sialparis.com/en\n[49]: https://www.foodbusinessafrica.com/contact/\n[50]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/diageo-ceo-dave-lewis-targetting-cost-cuts-staff-reductions/\n[51]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/campari-group-executive-patrick-piana-appointed-president-of-s\npirits-europe/\n[52]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/japanese-hotel-chains-increase-certified-seafood-purchases/\n[53]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/ab-inbev-appoints-mondelez-ceo-dirk-van-de-put-as-chairman/\n[54]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/tongaat-hullett-avoids-liquidation-as-idc-vision-consortium-st\nrike-rescue-deal/\n[55]: https://www.fwafrica.net\n[56]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/advertise\n[57]: https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/press-releases\n[58]: https://www.dairybusinessmea.com\n[59]: https://www.millingmea.com\n[60]: https://www.feedbusinessmea.com\n[61]: https://www.horecamea.com\n[62]: https://www.sustainabilitymea.com\n[63]: https://www.hpcmagmea.com\n[64]: https://www.agritechmea.com\n[65]: https: