        "crawl_text": "Nutritionist Answers Online Resource Not Applicable 2131 W Republic Rd #548, Springfield, MO 65807 Nutritionist Answers | Learn About Food From Nutrition Experts\n\nSkip to content\n\nFoods A to Z\n\nBlog\n\nMenu Toggle\n\nFruits\n\nVegetables\n\nSeafood\n\nHerbs and Spices\n\nNuts and Seeds\n\nAbout\n\nMenu Toggle\n\nContact\n\nSearch for:\n\nSearch\n\nSearch\n\nMain Menu\n\nFoods A to Z\n\nBlog\n\nMenu Toggle\n\nFruits\n\nVegetables\n\nSeafood\n\nHerbs and Spices\n\nNuts and Seeds\n\nAbout\n\nMenu Toggle\n\nContact\n\nRESEARCH-BASED INFO\nON ALL YOUR FAVORITE FOODS\n\nExplore the World of Food.\nLearn From Nutrition Experts.\n\nOur team of Registered Dietitian Nutritionists creates the most helpful and up-to-date content on all things food. From our nutrition database to trending articles , we&rsquo;re here to help you learn about the latest health benefits of various foods and fun new ways to enjoy them.\n\nRead the Latest\n\nDoes Acai Have Protein? A Nutritionist&rsquo;s Review\n\nAmy Richter, MS, RDN\n\nJanuary 8, 2024\n\nAcai berries, known for their vibrant color and high antioxidant content, have become a staple in smoothie bowls among food enthusiasts and health-conscious consumers. But\n\nCan You Be Allergic to Acai Berries? Here&rsquo;s How to Tell\n\nAmy Richter, MS, RDN\n\nJanuary 4, 2024\n\nNavigating the world of food allergies can be a complex and sometimes daunting task, especially when it comes to less common allergens like acai berries.&nbsp;\n\nCan You Eat Acai Every Day? (Maybe, it depends)\n\nAmy Richter, MS, RDN\n\nJanuary 4, 2024\n\nAcai has soared in popularity over the past couple of decades, and many people now enjoy acai bowls as a breakfast or snack most days\n\nAre Acai Bowls Healthy? A Nutritionist&rsquo;s Review\n\nAmy Richter, MS, RDN\n\nDecember 19, 2023\n\nAcai bowls are made by blending frozen or powdered acai with a liquid base, such as juice, milk, or yogurt, pouring the puree into a\n\nIs Acai Acidic? (Yes, and Here&rsquo;s Why)\n\nAmy Richter, MS, RDN\n\nDecember 13, 2023\n\nAcai is a fruit that&rsquo;s grown in the Amazon rainforest. It&rsquo;s best known for its high antioxidant content and has gained a reputation as a\n\nDoes Acai Make You Poop? (Yes, and Here&rsquo;s Why)\n\nAmy Richter, MS, RDN\n\nDecember 13, 2023\n\nAcai berries are small, dark purple fruits best known as the key ingredient in the oh-so-popular acai bowl, but they offer more than just a\n\nPage 1\nPage 2\nPage 3\nPage 4\nPage 5\n\nView Our Web Stories!\n\nsubscribe to our newsletter\n\nEmail Address\n\nSubmit\n\nCopyright &copy; 2026 Nutritionist Answers | Privacy Policy | Terms of Use | Disclaimer\n\nCookie Policy\n\nManage Cookie Consent\n\nWe use cookies to optimize our website and our service.\n\nFunctional\n\nFunctional\n\nAlways active\n\nThe technical storage or access is strictly necessary for the legitimate purpose of enabling the use of a specific service explicitly requested by the subscriber or user, or for the sole purpose of carrying out the transmission of a communication over an electronic communications network.\n\nPreferences\n\nPreferences\n\nThe technical storage or access is necessary for the legitimate purpose of storing preferences that are not requested by the subscriber or user.\n\nStatistics\n\nStatistics\n\nThe technical storage or access that is used exclusively for statistical purposes.\nThe technical storage or access that is used exclusively for anonymous statistical purposes. Without a subpoena, voluntary compliance on the part of your Internet Service Provider, or additional records from a third party, information stored or retrieved for this purpose alone cannot usually be used to identify you.\n\nMarketing\n\nMarketing\n\nThe technical storage or access is required to create user profiles to send advertising, or to track the user on a website or across several websites for similar marketing purposes.\n\nManage options\n\nManage services\n\nManage {vendor_count} vendors\n\nRead more about these purposes\n\nAccept\nDismiss\nPreferences\nSave preferences\nPreferences\n\n{title}\n\n{title}\n\n{title}\n\nManage consent\n\nScroll to Top [ Skip to content][1]\n[[Nutritionist Answers]][2]\n* [Foods A to Z][3]\n* [Blog][4]Menu Toggle\n* [Fruits][5]\n* [Vegetables][6]\n* [Seafood][7]\n* [Herbs and Spices][8]\n* [Nuts and Seeds][9]\n* [About][10]Menu Toggle\n* [Contact][11]\nSearch for: Search\n[ Search ][12]\n[[Nutritionist Answers]][13]\nMain Menu\n* [Foods A to Z][14]\n* [Blog][15]Menu Toggle\n* [Fruits][16]\n* [Vegetables][17]\n* [Seafood][18]\n* [Herbs and Spices][19]\n* [Nuts and Seeds][20]\n* [About][21]Menu Toggle\n* [Contact][22]\n\n# Learn about food from nutrition experts.\n\nWelcome to Nutritionist Answers, your go-to resource for credible, research-based, and up to date\nscientific information about the foods you eat.\n\nWe provide the best, most trustworthy answers to questions about food so that you can learn\nsomething new and make the best choices for you and your family.\n\nFounded in 2021, our team of registered dietitian nutritionists works hard to curate cutting edge\ninformation on the wide variety of whole foods that nature provides.\n\nOur Medical Nutrition Board reviews each article to ensure its accuracy before publishing, so you\ncan be sure you\u2019re getting the most accurate information possible.\n\n# Meet our team:\n\nOur team of Registered Dietitian Nutritionists is dedicated to producing high-quality content you\ncan trust.\n\n[Erica Julson, MS, RDN]\n\n### Erica Julson, MS, RDN\n\nRegistered Dietitian Nutritionist\nMedical Review Board Member\n\n[ View Bio ][23]\n\n### Amy Richter, MS, RDN\n\nRegistered Dietitian Nutritionist\nLead Writer\n\n[ View Bio ][24]\n\n## Our Editorial Process\n\nAll our content is created by registered dietitians who have Masters degrees in nutrition, completed\nat least 1,200 hours of supervised practice through an accredited internship program, and passed a\nnational registration exam.\n\nAs dietitians, we also complete 75 hours of continuing education every 5 years to keep abreast of\ncurrent topics and maintain our credentials.\n\nArticles are reviewed and updated on an annual basis to account for new research and findings. All\nfactual information included in the articles comes from peer-reviewed research articles. Any\ninformation based on professional experience is clearly specified as such.\n\nPlease note that the content on this site is general information only and should not be taken as\npersonalized nutrition advice. Read our disclaimers for more information and consult with your\nhealthcare practitioner before making any diet or lifestyle changes.\n\n[Woman standing in a white kitchen with her back to the camera, arranging flowers in a vase][Woman\nstanding in a white kitchen with her back to the camera, arranging flowers in a vase]\n\n## Contact Us\n\nHave a question or comment? Let us know!\n\n**Email:**\n\nsupport@nutritionistanswers.com\n\n**Mailing Address:**\n\n2131 W Republic Rd #548\nSpringfield, MO 65807\n\n[ Facebook ][25] [ Instagram ][26] [ Twitter ][27]\n\nCopyright \u00a9 2026 Nutritionist Answers | [Privacy Policy][28] | [Terms of Use][29]| [Disclaimer][30]\n* [Cookie Policy][31]\n\n[][32][][33][][34]\n[[Nutritionist Answers]][35]\nManage Cookie Consent\nWe use cookies to optimize our website and our service.\nFunctional Functional Always active\nThe technical storage or access is strictly necessary for the legitimate purpose of enabling the use\nof a specific service explicitly requested by the subscriber or user, or for the sole purpose of\ncarrying out the transmission of a communication over an electronic communications network.\nPreferences Preferences\nThe technical storage or access is necessary for the legitimate purpose of storing preferences that\nare not requested by the subscriber or user.\nStatistics Statistics\nThe technical storage or access that is used exclusively for statistical purposes. The technical\nstorage or access that is used exclusively for anonymous statistical purposes. Without a subpoena,\nvoluntary compliance on the part of your Internet Service Provider, or additional records from a\nthird party, information stored or retrieved for this purpose alone cannot usually be used to\nidentify you.\nMarketing Marketing\nThe technical storage or access is required to create user profiles to send advertising, or to track\nthe user on a website or across several websites for similar marketing purposes.\n* [Manage options][36]\n* [Manage services][37]\n* [Manage {vendor_count} vendors][38]\n* [Read more about these purposes][39]\nAccept Dismiss Preferences Save preferences [Preferences][40]\n* [{title}][41]\n* [{title}][42]\n* [{title}][43]\nManage consent\nScroll to Top\n\n[1]: #content\n[2]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/\n[3]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/foods-a-to-z/\n[4]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/blog/\n[5]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/fruits/\n[6]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/vegetables/\n[7]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/seafood/\n[8]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/herbs-spices/\n[9]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/nuts-seeds/\n[10]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/about-us/\n[11]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/contact-us/\n[12]: #\n[13]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/\n[14]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/foods-a-to-z/\n[15]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/blog/\n[16]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/fruits/\n[17]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/vegetables/\n[18]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/seafood/\n[19]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/herbs-spices/\n[20]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/nuts-seeds/\n[21]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/about-us/\n[22]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/contact-us/\n[23]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/author/erica-julson-ms-rdn/\n[24]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/author/amy-richter-ms-rdn/\n[25]: https://www.facebook.com/nutritionistanswers\n[26]: https://w