on Clad Warranty][222]\n100-Year Family Heritage SteelGuard est. 2005\n4,000+ Orders Per Year Trusted by industry nationwide\nBIM\n[Revit / BIM Files][223] For architects & engineers\n\n# Construction Noise Barriers and Temporary Sound Control Curtains\n* [Construction Noise Barriers and Temporary Sound Control Curtains Steel Guard Main Image ID4339]\n* [Construction Noise Barriers and Temporary Sound Control Curtains Steel Guard Main Image ID5463]\n* [Construction Noise Barriers and Temporary Sound Control Curtains Steel Guard Main Image ID4944]\n* [Construction Noise Barriers and Temporary Sound Control Curtains Thumbnail Image ID3132]\n* [Construction Noise Barriers and Temporary Sound Control Curtains Thumbnail Image ID4339]\n* [Construction Noise Barriers and Temporary Sound Control Curtains Thumbnail Image ID5463]\n* [Construction Noise Barriers and Temporary Sound Control Curtains Thumbnail Image ID4944]\n\n## Construction Noise Barriers for Temporary Sound Control\n\nConstruction noise barriers are designed to reduce noise levels on active job sites and control\nsound from demolition, heavy equipment, and construction activities. Steel Guard Safety temporary\nsound barriers provide effective noise control solutions for contractors working in environments\nwhere noise reduction and compliance are critical.\n\nThese construction sound curtains are engineered for temporary installation on fences, walls, or job\nsite structures. While classified as temporary systems, they are built with durable materials\ndesigned to withstand outdoor conditions for extended project durations.\n\nFor permanent facility installations, explore our [outdoor sound barrier curtains][224] engineered\nfor long-term industrial noise control.\n\nFor a complete range of solutions, explore our [industrial noise control products][225] designed for\nindustrial and construction environments.\n\nConstruction noise barriers are manufactured using 1\u201d, 2\u201d, or 4\u201d quilted fiberglass sound absorbing\nmaterials, with optional mass loaded vinyl (MLV) backing to enhance sound blocking and reduce noise\ntransmission beyond the job site.\n\nThese systems can also support compliance with\n[construction noise exposure guidelines][226] helping protect workers and nearby residential or\ncommercial areas.\n\n## Benefits of Construction Noise Barriers\n* **Reduces noise from demolition, excavation, compressors, and heavy equipment**\n* **Improves communication and safety on active construction sites**\n* **Helps maintain compliant noise levels for surrounding environments**\n* **Designed for temporary installation on fences and job site structures**\n* **Custom configurations with grommets, straps, and mounting options**\n\n**FOR MORE INFORMATION ON SOUND ATTENUATION SPECS SEE MATERIALS TAB**\n\n**Download our Revit BIM files for Easy Integration into your Construction Noise Barrier Project**\n\n[[Autodesk Revit] Open Revit Library][227]\n* [REQUEST QUOTE][228]\n\n## Additional Information:\n\n### Types of Construction Noise Barriers\n* **SCC-9 EXT** \u2013 2\u2033 Fiberglass Batting with Outdoor Rated Vinyl Quilted Face Front & Back- NRC-.85,\nSTC-19 \u2013 [See More Details][229]\n* **SCC-12 EXT** -1\u2033 Fiberglass Batting with Outdoor Rated Vinyl Quilted Face Front & 1 lb sq/ft\nReinforce Mass Loaded Vinyl Back \u2013 NRC -.70, STC 27 \u2013 [See More Details][230]\n* **SCC-13 EXT** -1\u2033 Fiberglass Batting with Outdoor Rated Vinyl Quilted Face Front & 1 lb sq/ft\nReinforce Mass Loaded Vinyl Back \u2013 NRC \u2013 .85, STC 32 \u2013 [See More Details][231]\n\nFor more information on designing your Temporary Construction Noise Barriers, or do get a quote,\ncontact one of our Experienced Sales Staff at 1-800-347-8368\n* Materials\n\n### Construction Sound Barrier Materials\n\n[2\" Silicone Coated Vinyl Front and Back Quilted on FiberglassNRC .75STC 29]\n\n2\" Silicone Coated Vinyl Front and Back Quilted on Fiberglass\nNRC .75\nSTC 29\n\n[Front - 1\" Silicone Coated Vinyl Quilted Fiberglass + Interior - 1 lb/sq ft Mass Loaded Vinyl +\nBack - 1\" Vinyl Quilted FiberglassNRC .70STC 27]\n\nFront - 1\" Silicone Coated Vinyl Quilted Fiberglass + Interior - 1 lb/sq ft Mass Loaded Vinyl + Back\n- 1\" Vinyl Quilted Fiberglass\nNRC .70\nSTC 27\n\n[Front - 2\" Silicone Coated Vinyl Quilted Fiberglass + Interior - 1 lb/sq ft Mass Loaded Vinyl +\nBack - 1\" Vinyl Quilted FiberglassNRC .85STC 32]\n\nFront - 2\" Silicone Coated Vinyl Quilted Fiberglass + Interior - 1 lb/sq ft Mass Loaded Vinyl + Back\n- 1\" Vinyl Quilted Fiberglass\nNRC .85\nSTC 32\n\n### SCC-9 EXT, SCC-12"
          },
