][163]\n* [Machine Safety Fencing \u2013 Premium][164]\n* [Machine Safety Fencing \u2013 Economy][165]\n* [Clear Vinyl Curtains][166]\n* [Clear PVC Strip Curtains][167]\n* [Food & Beverage][168]\n* [Food Safety Clean Curtains][169]\n* [Clear PVC Strip Curtains][170]\n* [Freezer Strip Curtains][171]\n* [Insulated Warehouse Curtains \u2013 Foldable][172]\n* [Dock Door Screens][173]\n* [Insulated Pallet Covers][174]\n* [Insulatied Warehouse Curtains \u2013 Stationary][175]\n* [Vinyl Pallet Covers][176]\n* [Manufacturing & Industrial][177]\n* [Accordion Fold Curtains][178]\n* [Anti Static Curtains][179]\n* [Industrial Blackout Curtains][180]\n* [Industrial Roll Up Curtains][181]\n* [Canvas Weld Curtains][182]\n* [Welding Screens][183]\n* [Welding Booth Enclosures][184]\n* [Welding Curtain Rolls][185]\n* [Welding Curtain Partitions][186]\n* [Welding Strip Curtains][187]\n* [Welding Blankets][188]\n* [Welding Blanket Rolls][189]\n* [Machine Equipment Covers][190]\n* [Machine Safety Fencing \u2013 Premium][191]\n* [Machine Safety Fencing \u2013 Economy][192]\n* [Clear PVC Strip Curtains][193]\n* [Bollard Post Covers][194]\n* [Warehouse Curtains & Enclosures][195]\n* [Acoustic Screens][196]\n* [Sound Blankets][197]\n* [Sound Curtains \u2013 Folding][198]\n* [Sound Curtains][199]\n* [Outdoor Sound Curtains][200]\n* [Construction Sound Curtains][201]\n* [Pharmaceutical][202]\n* [Accordion Fold Curtains][203]\n* [Anti Static Curtains][204]\n* [Chemical Safety Curtains][205]\n* [Clear PVC Strip Curtains][206]\n* [Transportation][207]\n* [Trailer Strip Curtains][208]\n* [Loading Dock Enclosures][209]\n* [Request a Quote][210]\n* [Resources][211]\n* * [Revit BIM Models][212]\n* [Catalogs][213]\n* [Blog][214]\n* [Fabric Specifications & Data Sheets][215]\n* [Hardware Specifications & Data Sheets][216]\n* [Guides & Calculators][217]\n* [Installation Instructions][218]\n* [FAQ][219]\n* [About Us][220]\n* [Contact][221]\n[U.S. Manufacturer]\nU.S. Manufacturer American made \u00b7 [Iron Clad Warranty][222]\n100-Year Family Heritage SteelGuard est. 2005\n4,000+ Orders Per Year Trusted by industry nationwide\nBIM\n[Revit / BIM Files][223] For architects & engineers\n\n# Woodworking Dust Curtains for Sawdust Containment & Shop Separation\n* [Woodworking Dust Curtains for Sawdust Containment & Shop Separation Steel Guard Main Image\nID4315]\n* [Woodworking Dust Curtains for Sawdust Containment & Shop Separation Steel Guard Main Image\nID1396]\n* [Woodworking Dust Curtains for Sawdust Containment & Shop Separation Steel Guard Main Image\nID1397]\n* [Woodworking Dust Curtains for Sawdust Containment & Shop Separation Thumbnail Image ID5386]\n* [Woodworking Dust Curtains for Sawdust Containment & Shop Separation Thumbnail Image ID4315]\n* [Woodworking Dust Curtains for Sawdust Containment & Shop Separation Thumbnail Image ID1396]\n* [Woodworking Dust Curtains for Sawdust Containment & Shop Separation Thumbnail Image ID1397]\n\n**Woodworking dust curtains** from **Steel Guard Safety** help contain sawdust, wood particles, and\ndebris in busy shop environments. These curtain systems create cleaner, safer, and more organized\nwork areas without the cost or disruption of permanent walls.\n\nFor facilities looking for broader dust management solutions across multiple operations, explore our\n[dust control curtains][224]. As part of our complete line of [industrial curtain systems][225],\nwoodworking curtains provide targeted containment for wood shops, fabrication areas, and production\nspaces.\n\n**Request a Quote or Configure Your Woodworking Dust Curtain System Today**\n\n## Contain Sawdust & Wood Particles at the Source\n\n**Dust curtains for woodworking** help isolate cutting, sanding, routing, and finishing operations\nthat generate airborne dust and debris. By separating these areas, facilities can reduce dust\nmigration and maintain cleaner surrounding workspaces.\n* Contain sawdust and airborne wood particles\n* Reduce debris spread into nearby work areas\n* Improve shop cleanliness and organization\n* Help create more controlled production zones\n\nAirborne wood dust can pose safety and respiratory risks in woodworking environments, as highlighted\nby the [Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA)][226], making proper containment\nessential.\n\n## Built for Woodworking Shops & Production Areas\n\nOur **woodworking dust curtains** are designed for demanding shop environments where machinery,\ndust, and frequent workflow movement are part of daily operations.\n* Table saw and panel saw areas\n* Sanding and finishing stations\n* CNC router zones\n* Wood cutting and shaping areas\n* Assembly and prep spaces\n\n## Improve Separation Without Permanent Construction\n\nUnlike fixed walls, **sawdust containment curtains** offer a flexible solution that can be installed\nquickly and adapted as your layout changes. This makes them ideal for woodworking operations that\nneed both containment and accessibility.\n\nThese woodworking dust curtain systems are often used with broader [dust containment curtain\nsystems][227] to support facility-wide dust control strategies.\n* Lower cost than permanent walls\n* Fast installation with minimal downtime\n* Flexible layouts for changing work areas\n* Custom sizing for shop-specific applications\n\n### Stock Woodworking Dust Curtains\n* **Color:** White Top \u2013 Clear Middle \u2013 Blue Bottom\n* **Materials:** Top & Bottom \u2013 18 oz Coated Vinyl \u2014 Middle \u2013 20 Mil Clear \u2013 All Materials Meet\nNFPA-701 Flame Retardant Standards.\n* **Kit Includes**: Curtain Wall (Woodworking Curtains) w/ Vision Panel, Grommets Set on Top, Chain\nWeight in Bottom Hem, Velcro on Sides \u2014 Galvanized Steel Track, 2-Wheel Nylon Roller Hooks,\nUniversal Splice & Mount Connectors (Works in place of Threaded Rod, Beam to Chain & Wall Mounts),\nEnd Stops.\n* **Panels:** Connect Multiple Woodworking Curtains Panels Modularly\n\n**Ships In: 2 -3 Business Days**\n* [REQUEST QUOTE][228]\n\n## Additional Information:\n\n## Protect Equipment, Inventory & Work Areas\n\n**Woodworking shop curtains** do more than contain dust. They also help protect nearby tools,\nproducts, and workstations from excess sawdust buildup and debris transfer.\n* Reduce contamination of finished materials\n* Help protect nearby equipment\n* Support cleaner surrounding production areas\n* Improve visibility between separated spaces when clear panels are used\n\n## Custom Woodworking Curtain Systems\n\nEvery **woodworking dust curtain** system is built to match your exact ap"
