][163]\n* [Machine Safety Fencing \u2013 Premium][164]\n* [Machine Safety Fencing \u2013 Economy][165]\n* [Clear Vinyl Curtains][166]\n* [Clear PVC Strip Curtains][167]\n* [Food & Beverage][168]\n* [Food Safety Clean Curtains][169]\n* [Clear PVC Strip Curtains][170]\n* [Freezer Strip Curtains][171]\n* [Insulated Warehouse Curtains \u2013 Foldable][172]\n* [Dock Door Screens][173]\n* [Insulated Pallet Covers][174]\n* [Insulatied Warehouse Curtains \u2013 Stationary][175]\n* [Vinyl Pallet Covers][176]\n* [Manufacturing & Industrial][177]\n* [Accordion Fold Curtains][178]\n* [Anti Static Curtains][179]\n* [Industrial Blackout Curtains][180]\n* [Industrial Roll Up Curtains][181]\n* [Canvas Weld Curtains][182]\n* [Welding Screens][183]\n* [Welding Booth Enclosures][184]\n* [Welding Curtain Rolls][185]\n* [Welding Curtain Partitions][186]\n* [Welding Strip Curtains][187]\n* [Welding Blankets][188]\n* [Welding Blanket Rolls][189]\n* [Machine Equipment Covers][190]\n* [Machine Safety Fencing \u2013 Premium][191]\n* [Machine Safety Fencing \u2013 Economy][192]\n* [Clear PVC Strip Curtains][193]\n* [Bollard Post Covers][194]\n* [Warehouse Curtains & Enclosures][195]\n* [Acoustic Screens][196]\n* [Sound Blankets][197]\n* [Sound Curtains \u2013 Folding][198]\n* [Sound Curtains][199]\n* [Outdoor Sound Curtains][200]\n* [Construction Sound Curtains][201]\n* [Pharmaceutical][202]\n* [Accordion Fold Curtains][203]\n* [Anti Static Curtains][204]\n* [Chemical Safety Curtains][205]\n* [Clear PVC Strip Curtains][206]\n* [Transportation][207]\n* [Trailer Strip Curtains][208]\n* [Loading Dock Enclosures][209]\n* [Request a Quote][210]\n* [Resources][211]\n* * [Revit BIM Models][212]\n* [Catalogs][213]\n* [Blog][214]\n* [Fabric Specifications & Data Sheets][215]\n* [Hardware Specifications & Data Sheets][216]\n* [Guides & Calculators][217]\n* [Installation Instructions][218]\n* [FAQ][219]\n* [About Us][220]\n* [Contact][221]\n[U.S. Manufacturer]\nU.S. Manufacturer American made \u00b7 [Iron Clad Warranty][222]\n100-Year Family Heritage SteelGuard est. 2005\n4,000+ Orders Per Year Trusted by industry nationwide\nBIM\n[Revit / BIM Files][223] For architects & engineers\n\n# Acrylic Coated Welding Blankets | Slag Shield Fiberglass\n* [Acrylic Coated Welding Blankets | Slag Shield Fiberglass Steel Guard Main Image ID3953]\n* [Acrylic Coated Welding Blankets | Slag Shield Fiberglass Steel Guard Main Image ID3954]\n* [Acrylic Coated Welding Blankets | Slag Shield Fiberglass Thumbnail Image ID3953]\n* [Acrylic Coated Welding Blankets | Slag Shield Fiberglass Thumbnail Image ID3953]\n* [Acrylic Coated Welding Blankets | Slag Shield Fiberglass Thumbnail Image ID3954]\n\nSteel Guard\u2019s Slag Shield acrylic coated fiberglass welding blankets deliver medium-duty protection\nagainst sparks, spatter, and medium slag in MIG, TIG, and stick welding applications. The heavy\nacrylic coating applied over the fiberglass base adds abrasion resistance and improved slag shedding\ncompared to uncoated heat cleaned fiberglass \u2014 making Slag Shield the right choice when standard\nfiberglass isn\u2019t holding up but a full silicone coating isn\u2019t required. Rated to **1,000\u00b0F** and\nmanufactured from **28 oz heavy acrylic coated fiberglass** at .050 inches thick.\n\nSlag Shield blankets are sewn with high-heat thread and include grommets set every 24\u2033 on all sides\nfor secure attachment in horizontal and vertical applications. All blankets meet **FM Global and\nNFPA-701** flame retardancy certifications and are manufactured in the USA. Note \u2014 Slag Shield is\nnot suitable for heat treating or stress relief applications. Part of the [Steel Guard welding\nblanket lineup][224] \u2014 compare all materials to find the right protection level for your\napplication.\n\n## Slag Shield Acrylic Coated Welding Blanket Specifications\n* **Material:** 28 oz heavy acrylic coated fiberglass, .050 inch thick\n* **Temperature rating:** 1,000\u00b0F\n* **Construction:** Sewn with high-heat thread \u2014 grommets set every 24\u2033 on all sides\n* **Size note:** Finished blanket sizes run 2\u2033\u20134\u2033 shorter than nominal dimensions\n* **Certifications:** FM Global and NFPA-701 flame retardancy certified\n* **Handling note:** Contains fiberglass \u2014 handle with safety gloves at all times\n* **Not suitable for:** Heat treating or stress relief applications\n* **Ships in:** 7\u201310 business da\n* [REQUEST QUOTE][225]\n\n## Additional Information:\n\n## What the Acrylic Coating Adds\n\nThe acrylic coating on Slag Shield blankets provides meaningful performance improvements over\nuncoated heat cleaned fiberglass in medium-duty welding environments:\n* **Medium slag resistance** \u2014 the acrylic surface layer helps slag bead up and roll off rather than\nadhering to and burning through the fiberglass base\n* **Improved abrasion resistance** \u2014 the coating protects the fiberglass weave from physical wear\nwhen blankets are dragged, repositioned, or used in abrasive environments\n* **Better spatter shedding** \u2014 coated surface makes it easier to shake off accumulated spatter and\ndebris, extending blanket service life\n* **Enhanced flexibility** \u2014 acrylic coating maintains flexibility better than uncoated fiberglass\nin cold shop environments\n\n## Where Slag Shield Fits in the Welding Blanket Lineup\n\nSteel Guard manufactures fiberglass welding blankets in multiple weights and coatings. Here\u2019s where\nSlag Shield fits:\n* **18 oz uncoated (Weld Armor)** \u2014 light to medium duty, everyday MIG/TIG/stick welding, most\neconomical, 2\u20133 day ship\n* **28 oz acrylic coated (Slag Shield)** \u2014 medium duty, improved slag and abrasion resistance, step\nup from uncoated fiberglass\n* **35 oz uncoated (Arc-Tex)** \u2014 heavy duty, maximum fiberglass thickness, best for high-output\nwelding and asbestos blanket replacement\n* **32 oz silicone coated (Red Spark)** \u2014 heavy duty with silicone rubber coating, maximum abrasion\nand chemical resistance, meets Mil-Y-1140C\n\nChoose Slag Shield when your application regularly produces medium slag and your 18 oz uncoated\nblankets are wearing out faster than expected \u2014 but you don\u2019t need the full silicone coating of Red\nSpark.\n\n## Slag Shield Acrylic Coated Welding Blanket Applications\n* MIG, TIG, and stick welding with medium slag production\n* Arc welding heat shield barriers in fabrication environments\n* Equipment and machinery protection in abrasive welding environments\n* Vertical curtain applications requiring improved slag shedding\n* Pipe and structural steel welding with moderate spatter\n* F"
