on Clad Warranty][222]\n100-Year Family Heritage SteelGuard est. 2005\n4,000+ Orders Per Year Trusted by industry nationwide\nBIM\n[Revit / BIM Files][223] For architects & engineers\n\n# **About Us**\n\n## The Beginning\n\nAs a Young College Graduate (well, almost I was trying to pass Calculus 2) from Purdue University I\ncame home to finish my last credits and worked for the Summer at my Families Tent and Awning\nCompany. I realized that Summer that Finance was maybe not for me, and Entrepreneurship was. I loved\nto work with tangible products since I was a child, I was infatuated with Legos, and Constructs.\nThat year, I made the choice to Start my own Industrial Sewing Line. At this point, I knew Tents &\nAwnings was not the way for me, as the local Business my family had was starting to struggle a lot.\nAfter much trial and error, I found that Safety Products were a good Niche, and there was room for\ngrowth, as well as Custom, American Made Products.\n\n[[Terra Haute Tent]][224]\n\n## Pioneering the Online World\n\nI started selling on a Lead Generation website in 2004. For a Small Startup Industrial Manufacturing\nCompany this was a real rarity. Learning the ins and outs of Digital marketing was daunting, but\nended up paying off. We were able to make connections and sales with regular Industrial Customers\nand eventually Distributors.\n\n## Standing Out from the Crowd\n\nI found success in Selling Barrier Protection Products, and a year and half later in 2006, I worked\nwith a Manufacturing firm to design our own custom made Coated (Knife over Roll) Vinyl. I named it\nSteel-Scrim, to go along with our brand as well as its uniquely strong tensile strength.\n\n## Keeping American Ingenuity & Production Alive\n\nLong story short, I made it work, but not with out our Family of Employees. We Strive to have the\nhighest quality crafted Product with Local Employees and Fair Wages. Thank you so much for reading\nthis and visiting our site.\n\n[[Steelguard Employee]][225][[Steelguard Employees - Man And Woman]][226][[Rolling\nCurtain]][227][[Woman At Machine]][228]\n\n## Our Team\n\n[President Greg Pretsch]\n\n### Gregory Pretsch \u2013 President\n\nI am avid innovator of products. My Families lineage stretches through lots of Entrepreneurs. You\ncould say its in my blood. I enjoy time with my Family and Friends. And have dabble in hobbies like\nGolfing, Koi Fish, Landscape Architecture, and a love for all types of Cars.\n\n[[Img 3717]][229]\n\n### Sabrina Pretsch \u2013 VP / Controller\n\nYou could say I have a talent with Numbers and Math, and an Obsessive Organizer. I am a Graduate of\nThe School of the Art Institute of Chicago (I know doesn\u2019t translate to math). Design is somewhat in\nmy blood. My Father, Uncle, and Grandfather Edo Belli, designed churches hospitals and schools all\nover the world.\n\nI have worked with Small Businesses my whole life, and then, I married into one. I love design,\nInterior Architecture, and Perspective Art. I have been extensively self trained in Illustrator, and\nlove doing graphic design.\n\n**[[Aaron Ortega]][230]**\n\n### Aaron Ortega \u2013 Production Manager / Sales\n\nI have my Bachelors in Logistics, that has prepared myself for Management, in some ways. I am a\nNative of Chicagoland, and Family and my Heritage is of Core Importance. If you need an Ear to\nListen I am your guy. Soccer is my passion, and life style, in playing and watching talent. I enjoy\nTraveling, the Outdoors, and now during COVID, Golfing. E: [[email protected]][231]\n\n**[[Anita Miller]][232]**\n\n### Anita Miller \u2013 Sales Executive\n\nMy history is as an Educator, I love to learn and some would say I\u2019m a Free Spirit. I enjoy meeting\nnew people on a daily basis, some great, some not so great. I Enjoy Nature, Four Wheeling, and\nGinseng & Mushroom Hunting. I also have extensive knowledge of Herbs and Its Natural Remedies.\nE:[[email protected]][233]\n\n**[[Fernando Perea]][234]**\n\n### Fernando Perea \u2013 Floor Manager\n\nI enjoy dealing with screaming people. I know how to handle children, you could say it\u2019s a gift. I\nlove Soccer, the lifestyle, the game, and the camaraderie. I have been into running and physical\nfitness my whole life. Even at 66 I am able to keep up with those younger. I enjoy traveling, family\ngatherings, and my Grandkids. Email: [[email protected]][235]\n\n**[[Sandy Sosa]][236]**\n\n### Sandy Sosa \u2013 Customer Service & Administration\n\nEmail: [[email protected]][237]\n\nCatalogs\n\nFind out all the details to properly design your barrier protection "
          },
