od pressure. It\u2019s high in rich Oleic Acid, a very healthy fat. The essential fats found\navocados are essential for digestion and nutrient absorption because they nourish the lining of the\ngut. It\u2019s an all-round super food!\n\n### IT HAS A HIGH SMOKE POINT\n\nNot every oil is created equal. The benefit of avocado oil is that it can be heated to very high\ntemperatures. Why is this good? When oil is heated past its smoke point, the fat starts to break\ndown, releasing free radicals and any health benefit that the oil had is lost.\n\n### EXTRA VIRGIN COLD PRESSED\n\nExtra Virgin is the highest grade of avocado oil, produced from the pressing of good quality\navocados. Produced at low temperatures, without chemicals the oil is 100% pure and natural. Cold\npressing from the first press of the avocado fruit means retains the same high level of nutrients,\nnatural flavour, aroma and colour found in fresh avocado.\n\n### 16 AVOCADOS IN EVERY BOTTLE\n\nEvery one of our 250ml bottles contains 16 cold pressed avocados. Quality Avocado Oil should have a\ntaste and colour characteristics of the fresh avocado fruit and be a dark vibrant green. We house\nour oil in dark glass bottles, which keeps out light and oxygen retaining the quality of the oil\n\n### IT\u2019S GOOD FOR YOU\n\nThe amazing avocado has many distinctive health benefits and is classed as a superfood by many. On\ntop of the many health benefits here are a few: It may reduce cholesterol, improve heart health and\nlower blood pressure. It\u2019s high in rich Oleic Acid, a very healthy fat. The essential fats found\navocados are essential for digestion and nutrient absorption because they nourish the lining of the\ngut. It\u2019s an all-round super food!\n\n### EXTRA VIRGIN COLD PRESSED\n\nExtra Virgin is the highest grade of avocado oil, produced from the pressing of good quality\navocados. Produced at low temperatures, without chemicals the oil is 100% pure and natural. Cold\npressing from the first press of the avocado fruit means retains the same high level of nutrients,\nnatural flavour, aroma and colour found in fresh avocado.\n\n### IT HAS A HIGH SMOKE POINT\n\nNot every oil is created equal. The benefit of avocado oil is that it can be heated to very high\ntemperatures. Why is this good? When oil is heated past its smoke point, the fat starts to break\ndown, releasing free radicals and any health benefit that the oil had is lost.\n\n### 16 AVOCADOS IN EVERY BOTTLE\n\nEvery one of our 250ml bottles contains 16 cold pressed avocados. Quality Avocado Oil should have a\ntaste and colour characteristics of the fresh avocado fruit and be a dark vibrant green. We house\nour oil in dark glass bottles, which keeps out light and oxygen retaining the quality of the oil\n\n## Why Avocado Oil?\n\n[ Our Story ][81]\n\n# Be Inspired\n\nAvocado Oil inspired recipes\n\n[\nHearty Mushroom Bolognese\n][82]\n[\nVegan & GF Cinnamon Sugar Doughnuts\n][83]\n[\nSmoked Salmon\n][84]\n[\nBlackberry, Thyme and Cheese Avocado Oil Cake\n][85]\n[\nAvocanana-Bread\n][86]\n[ See More ][87]\n\n## Reviews\n\nLast year I made the switch from using Olive Oil to using Grove Avocado Oil. I have never looked\nback - I love using it in cooking and for salad dressings.\n[Grace L]\nGrace L\nTrouble is I use it in everything. So I go through 2-3 bottles a week!\n[Christine C]\nChristine C\nWhen cooking rice for an Asian dish; I always put Lime Avocado Oil in the rice. One tablespoon per\ncup of rice.\n[Carla G]\nCarla G\nEasily the best oil for cooking. I use it regularly and have done for a few years now. Totally\nrecommend it.\nJohn H\nMy pantry staple. I won\u2019t use any other oil now.\nTracey C\nI love it with Dukkah and bread, it brings so much flavour to every meal.\nViv C\nThe Lime Avo Oil is my favourite. Drizzled over salads \u2013 yum!\nSue C\nUnmatched anywhere in the world. The most incredible taste experience I have ever had!\nBea M\n[ Weeknight dinner just got a glow-up: juicy meatbal [Weeknight dinner just got a glow-up: juicy\nmeatballs simmered in a tangy tomato cream sauce, topped with fresh parsley & mint \ud83c\udf45\ud83c\udf3f All made\nirresistible with the golden touch of Grove Avocado Oil. \ud83d\udc9a Our secret? A high-heat sear with\nGrove\u2019s avocado oil gives these meatballs a perfect crust, while the creamy tomato base brings a\nburst of comfort with every bite. \ud83c\udf74 INGREDIENTS For the meatballs: - 450g ground beef (or a mix of\nbeef and pork) - 1 egg - 1/3 cup "
