, 6th generation owner of my family\u2019s farm and a \u201csemi\u201d homesteader.**\n\nYou\u2019ll find a large variety of **sweet, savory, and non alcoholic drink recipes**. I love comfort\nfood, honoring seasonal ingredients from my garden, and **helping people live a more sustainable\nlife** (like our ancestors).\n\n[Entirely Elizabeth Swoish Headshot]\n[MY STORY][47] [RECIPES][48]\n[ [Introducing my New Cookbook! The One Jar Condiments Cookbook. Real condiments you can feel good\nabout feeding to your family. 38+ beginner-friendly recipes. Printable Jar Labels. Instant digital\ndownload. Order it Now!] ][49]\n\n## FRESH DINNERS & SIDE DISHES\n* [ [Apple Kale Slaw with ribbons of carrots and a honey mustard dressing.] ][50]\n  [Apple Kale Slaw][51]\n* [ [Cucumber Radish Salad tossed in a sweet and creamy dressing with red onion, dill, and black\n  pepper.] ][52]\n  [Cucumber Radish Salad][53]\n* [ [Six baked Lemon Chicken Thighs with roasted lemons and thyme. Ready for serving and eating.]\n  ][54]\n  [Lemon Chicken Thighs][55]\n* [ [Bowl of Warm Quinoa Salad with spinach, herbs, and sweet bell peppers that are red, yellow, and\n  orange.] ][56]\n  [Warm Quinoa Salad][57]\n\n## BLUE RIBBON BAKED GOODS\n* [ [Bite taken out of a Peanut Butter Chocolate Chunk Bar. It's soft, chewy, and studded with\n  chocolate chunks.] ][58]\n  [Peanut Butter Chocolate Chunk Bars][59]\n* [ [A slice of Raspberry White Chocolate Bundt Cake on a plate with additional fresh raspberries on\n  the side. There is another slice of cake on a plate in the background as well as the whole cake.]\n  ][60]\n  [White Chocolate Raspberry Bundt Cake][61]\n* [ [Baked Scoopable Cookies topped with flaky sea salt in a baking dish. There is some removed so\n  you can see the gooey, chocolatey, texture of it.] ][62]\n  [Scoopable Cookies][63]\n* [ [Stack of Lemon Strawberry Muffins. The top one has a bite taken from it and you can see the\n  soft, tender insides with chunks of strawberries and flecks 