        "crawl_text": "[Skip to content][1]\n\n# Home\n\n## Pure, natural oils. Ethically produced.\n\nFairoils leads the way in the responsible and ethical production of quality essential and vegetable\noils. Our partnerships support local growers and strengthen communities in Africa.\n\n[ Get in touch ][2]\n[ Learn about our impact ][3]\n[ ][4]\n\n### We believe that responsible business makes the world a better place.\n\nAt the heart of Fairoils is the determination to help farmers and communities in Africa.\n\nFrom seed through to supply, we manage every step of the production process. This stewardship allows\nus to embed ethics and quality at every stage.\n\nThe result is pure, natural oils, produced to the highest ethical standards.\n\n##### Fairoils embraces the United Nations\u2019 Sustainable Development Goals as a clear blueprint for\n##### the prosperity of people and our planet. We\u2019re advancing these goals across our operations.\n\n[ Find out how ][5]\n[cooperatives large]\n\n### Local cooperatives with real reach.\n\nWe know what\u2019s possible when people work together, bonded by a common goal. Fairoils unites the\nefforts of small-scale growers, commercial farms and local processing facilities to make a\ndifference.\n\n##### Small scale grower projects\n\nOur growers work as a collective, gaining a secure, additional income. [Learn about our impact][6]\n\n##### Commercial farms\n\nCommercial farms help secure supply and demonstrate co-commitment.\n\n[Learn about how we farm][7]\n\n##### Processing facilities\n\nCrops are processed in state-of-the-art processing facilities in Kenya & Madagascar.\n\n[Learn about processing][8]\n\n### Our projects in Africa\n\nEach of our projects is shaped by the local community.\nThrough careful design, we create meaningful impact at every step.\n[ Learn about our impact ][9]\n[africa_map@2x]\n\n### Skills and income for farmers.\n\nOur grower projects establish a farming cooperative between small-scale farmers. We foster the\nskills farmers need to successfully grow crops for essential and vegetable oils. We also make\nresources more accessible\u2014seed, organic fertiliser, equipment and education.\n\nAnd we help local farmers find new ways to work together, so they can collectively reach new\nmarkets. Fairoils ensures that farmers gain secure, reliable income. Our farmers are paid quickly,\nreceiving a fair and transparent price for their crop.\n\n[ Our fair trade commitment ][10]\nOUR PROJECTS\n\n### Madagascar\n\nOur grower projects establish a farming cooperative between small-scale farmers. We foster the\nskills farmers need to successfully grow crops for essential and vegetable oils. We also make\nresources more accessible\u2014seed, organic fertiliser, equipment and education.\n\nAnd we help local farmers find new ways to work together, so they can collectively reach new\nmarkets. Fairoils ensures that farmers gain secure, reliable income. Our farmers are paid quickly,\nreceiving a fair and transparent price for their crop.\n\n### Over 50 pure, natural oils.\n\nWe\u2019re proud to supply essential and vegetable oils to world-leading brands that share our commitment\nto ethical production. We produce oils of the highest quality and purity. Our innovative business\nmodel allows us to supply large volumes of vegetable and essential oils, year round.\n[ Explore our full range of oils ][11]\n[ Our quality assurance ][12]\n\n#### 8\n\nEthical out-\ngrower projects\n\n#### 12,137\n\nSmall scale farmers\nworking with Fairoils\n\n#### 389\n\nFairoils employees\nbased in Africa\n\n## Farming for good.\n\nFairoils is committed to producing the highest quality natural oils for the cosmetic and personal\ncare industry, with a particular emphasis on products with an ethical farming story.\n[ View Projects ][13]\n[ Watch our video ][14]\n\n## We see a bright future for Africa\n\nPartner with us to strengthen local communities.\n\n[ Get in touch ][15]\n[ Learn about our impact ][16]\n\n###### Our key oils\n\n###### Current projects\n\n###### [Contact us][17]\n\n###### Our key oils\n\n[Ylang ylang][18]\n[Fresh ginger][19]\n[Tea tree][20]\n[Rose geranium][21]\n[Cinnamon bark][22]\n[Clove bud][23]\n[Eucalyptus citriodora][24]\n[Avocado][25]\n[Macadamia nut][26]\n[Sesame][27]\n\n###### Current projects\n* [Lunga Lunga \u2013 Kenyan Coast][28]\n* [Mt Kenya \u2013 Kenyan Highlands][29]\n* [Nosy Be \u2013 Madagascar North][30]\n* [Mananjary \u2013 Madagascar South][31]\n* [Mara \u2013 Western Kenya][32]\n* [Thika \u2013 Central Kenya][33]\n* [Lunga Lunga \u2013 Kenyan Coast][34]\n* [Mt Kenya \u2013 Kenyan Highlands][35]\n* [Nosy Be \u2013 Madagascar North][36]\n* [Mananjary \u2013 Madagascar South][37]\n* [Mara \u2013 Western Kenya][38]\n* [Thika \u2013 Central Kenya][39]\n\n###### Contact us\n\nDistribution\nFairoils SRL\nAvenue de l\u2019Innovation 5\n7822 Ghislenghien \u2013 Belgium\nE: info@fairoils.com\nP: + 32 68 28 43 16\n\n\u00a9 2026\u00a0Fairoils Limited | [Web design][40] by Excite Media | [Fairoils Terms and Conditions of\nsale][41]\n\n[ Facebook ][42] [ Linkedin ][43]\n[ ][44]\n\n[1]: #content\n[2]: https://www.fairoils.com/contact/\n[3]: https://www.fairoils.com/our-impact/\n[4]: #section-1st\n[5]: https://www.fairoils.com/un-goals/\n[6]: https://www. [Skip to content][1]\n\n# Home\n\n## Pure, natural oils. Ethically produced.\n\nFairoils leads the way in the responsible and ethical production of quality essential and vegetable\noils. Our partnerships support local growers and strengthen communities in Africa.\n\n[ Get in touch ][2]\n[ Learn about our impact ][3]\n[ ][4]\n\n### We believe that responsible business makes the world a better place.\n\nAt the heart of Fairoils is the determination to help farmers and communities in Africa.\n\nFrom seed through to supply, we manage every step of the production process. This stewardship allows\nus to embed ethics and quality at every stage.\n\nThe result is pure, natural oils, produced to the highest ethical standards.\n\n##### Fairoils embraces the United Nations\u2019 Sustainable Development Goals as a clear blueprint for\n##### the prosperity of people and our planet. We\u2019re advancing these goals across our operations.\n\n[ Find out how ][5]\n[cooperatives large]\n\n### Local cooperatives with real reach.\n\nWe know what\u2019s possible when people work together, bonded by a common goal. Fairoils unites the\nefforts of small-scale growers, commercial farms and local processing facilities to make a\ndifference.\n\n##### Small scale grower projects\n\nOur growers work as a collective, gaining a secure, additional income. [Learn about our impact][6]\n\n##### Commercial farms\n\nCommercial farms help secure supply and demonstrate co-commitment.\n\n[Learn about how we farm][7]\n\n##### Processing facilities\n\nCrops are processed in state-of-the-art processing facilities in Kenya & Madagascar.\n\n[Learn about processing][8]\n\n### Our projects in Africa\n\nEach of our projects is shaped by the local community.\nThrough careful design, we create meaningful impact at every step.\n[ Learn about our impact ][9]\n[africa_map@2x]\n\n### Skills and income for farmers.\n\nOur grower projects establish a farming cooperative between small-scale farmers. We foster the\nskills farmers need to successfully grow crops for essential and vegetable oils. We also make\nresources more accessible\u2014seed, organic fertiliser, equipment and education.\n\nAnd we help local farmers find new ways to work together, so they can collectively reach new\nmarkets. Fairoils ensures that farmers gain secure, reliable income. Our farmers are paid quickly,\nreceiving a fair and transparent price for their crop.\n\n[ Our fair trade commitment ][10]\nOUR PROJECTS\n\n### Madagascar\n\nOur grower projects establish a farming cooperative between small-scale farmers. We foster the\nskills farmers need to successfully grow crops for essential and vegetable oils. We also make\nresources more accessible\u2014seed, organic fertiliser, equipment and education.\n\nAnd we help local farmers find new ways to work together, so they can collectively reach new\nmarkets. Fairoils ensures that farmers gain secure, reliable income. Our farmers are paid quickly,\nreceiving a fair and transparent price for their crop.\n\n### Over 50 pure, natural oils.\n\nWe\u2019re proud to supply essential and vegetable oils to world-leading brands that share our commitment\nto ethical production. We produce oils of the highest quality and purity. Our innovative business\nmodel allows us to supply large volumes of vegetable and essential oils, year round.\n[ Explore our full range of oils ][11]\n[ Our quality assurance ][12]\n\n#### 8\n\nEthical out-\ngrower projects\n\n#### 12,137\n\nSmall scale farmers\nworking with Fairoils\n\n#### 389\n\nFairoils employees\nbased in Africa\n\n## Farming for good.\n\nFairoils is committed to producing the highest quality natural oils for the cosmetic and personal\ncare industry, with a particular emphasis on products with an ethical farming story.\n[ View Projects ][13]\n[ Watch our video ][14]\n\n## We see a bright future for Africa\n\nPartner with us to strengthen local communities.\n\n[ Get in touch ][15]\n[ Learn about our impact ][16]\n\n###### Our key oils\n\n###### Current projects\n\n###### [Contact us][17]\n\n###### Our key oils\n\n[Ylang ylang][18]\n[Fresh ginger][19]\n[Tea tree][20]\n[Rose geranium][21]\n[Cinnamon bark][22]\n[Clove bud][23]\n[Eucalyptus citriodora][24]\n[Avocado][25]\n[Macadamia nut][26]\n[Sesame][27]\n\n###### Current projects\n* [Lunga Lunga \u2013 Kenyan Coast][28]\n* [Mt Kenya \u2013 Kenyan Highlands][29]\n* [Nosy Be \u2013 Madagascar North][30]\n* [Mananjary \u2013 Madagascar South][31]\n* [Mara \u2013 Western Kenya][32]\n* [Thika \u2013 Central Kenya][33]\n* [Lunga Lunga \u2013 Kenyan Coast][34]\n* [Mt Kenya \u2013 Kenyan Highlands][35]\n* [Nosy Be \u2013 Madagascar North][36]\n* [Mananjary \u2013 Madagascar South][37]\n* [Mara \u2013 Western Kenya][38]\n* [Thika \u2013 Central Kenya][39]\n\n###### Contact us\n\nDistribution\nFairoils SRL\nAvenue de l\u2019Innovation 5\n7822 Ghislenghien \u2013 Belgium\nE: info@fairoils.com\nP: + 32 68 28 43 16\n\n\u00a9 2026\u00a0Fairoils Limited | [Web design][40] by Excite Media | [Fairoils Terms and Conditions of\nsale][41]\n\n[ Facebook ][42] [ Linkedin ][43]\n[ ][44]\n\n[1]: #content\n[2]: https://www.fairoils.com/contact/\n[3]: https://www.fairoils.com/our-impact/\n[4]: #section-1st\n[5]: https://www.fairoils.com/un-goals/\n[6]: https://www.fairoils.com/our-impact/\n[7]: https://www.fairoils.com/farming/\n[8]: https://www.fairoils.com/our-processing-facilities/\n[9]: https://www.fairoils.com/our-impact/\n[10]: https://www.fairoils.com/our-commitment-to-fairtrade/\n[11]: https://www.fairoils.com/wp-content/uploads/Product-List-for-web-1.pdf\n[12]: /our-quality-and-technical-specifications/\n[13]: https://www.fairoils.com/projects/\n[14]: #elementor-action%3Aaction%3Dpopup%3Aopen%26settings%3DeyJpZCI6Ijc1MiIsInRvZ2dsZSI6ZmFsc2V9\n[15]: https://www.fairoils.com/contact/\n[16]: https://www.fairoils.com/our-impact/\n[17]: /contact\n[18]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/ylang-ylang/\n[19]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/ginger/\n[20]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/tea-tree/\n[21]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/rose-geranium/\n[22]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/cinnamon-bark/\n[23]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/clove-bud/\n[24]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/eucalyptus-citriodora/\n[25]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/avocado/\n[26]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/macadamia-nut/\n[27]: https://www.fairoils.com/products/sesame-oil/\n[28]: https://fairoils.com/projects/kenyan-coast-lunga-lunga-project/\n[29]: https://fairoils.com/projects/mount-kenya/\n[30]: https://fairoils.com/projects/madagascar/\n[31]: https://fairoils.com/projects/madagascar-south-mananjary-project/\n[32]: https://fairoils.com/projects/mara-location/\n[33]: https://fairoils.com/projects/thika-project/\n[34]: https://fairoils.com/projects/kenyan-coast-lunga-lunga-project/\n[35]: https://fairoils.com/projects/mount-kenya/\n[36]: https://fairoils.com/projects/madagascar/\n[37]: https://fairoils.com/projects/madagascar-south-mananjary-project/\n[38]: https://fairoils.com/projects/mara-location/\n[39]: https://fairoils.com/projects/thika-project/\n[40]: https://www.excitemedia.com.au/\n[41]: https://fairoils.com/wp-content/uploads/Fairoils-Terms-and-Conditions-of-Sale_V1.pdf\n[42]: https://www.facebook.com/Fairoils/\n[43]: https://www.linkedin.com"
