        "crawl_text": "[Skip to main content][1]\nHit enter to search or ESC to close\n[Close Search ][2]\n[ [GrowthRomeo] ][3]\n[search][4]\n[ Menu ][5]\n* Services\n  * [Content Marketing][6]\n    * [Content Strategy][7]\n    * [SEO][8]\n    * [B2B Lead Generation][9]\n  * [Technology Writing][10]\n    * [SaaS Content Writing][11]\n    * [IT Content Writing][12]\n    * [Technical Writing][13]\n    * [AI-led Content Creation][14]\n* Industries\n  * [SaaS][15]\n  * [Information Technology][16]\n  * [DevTech][17]\n  * [Travel Tech][18]\n  * [HR Tech][19]\n* Resources\n  * [Insights][20]\n    * [Glossary][21]\n    * [Marketing Blog][22]\n    * [LinkedIn Blog][23]\n  * Tools\n    * [Word Counter][24]\n    * [Text Styling][25]\n    * [Case Convertor][26]\n* [Let\u2019s Talk?\ud83d\udd25\ud83d\ude80][27]\n* [linkedin ][28][email ][29]\n* [search][30]\nDigital Marketing Agency\n\n# {Content, Product, Brand} Marketing for Tech Startups\n\n[About GrowthRomeo][31]\n[Discuss Requirements ][32]\n[Hatica]\n[MagicPin]\n[LambdaTest]\n[Octoparse]\n[Redsteep]\n\n##### Experienced. On-demand.\n\n## What\u2019s GrowthRomeo?\n\nGrowthRomeo is a technology marketing agency that helps IT, SaaS, and AI startups grow with content,\nproduct, and brand marketing.\n\n##### [Let's Talk More?][33]\n\n##### Creative. Cool. Classy.\n\n## Why GrowthRomeo?\n\nWe *drive your pipeline* by enhancing your brand\u2019s visibility across marketing channels while being\n**cost-effective**, **creative**, and **consistent**.\n\n##### [Content Marketing Services][34]\n\n### **Get your business rocket to the desired growth velocity!**\n\n[Let's talk?][35]\n\n#### Content Marketing\n\nBrackish content to keep them drooling for more.\n\n#### SEO\n\nMaximise intent-ful discovery.\n\n#### Content Strategy\n\nRent our cortex, do it right.\n\n#### SEM\n\nSpell some inorganic magic.\n\n#### Marketing Automation\n\nFind time to talk with him/her.\n\n#### Landing pages\n\nActionable. Evocative. Enticing. Copy.\n\n## How GrowthRomeo Helps You Grow Your Startup?\n\n### ICP Research\n\nKnow your ICP in-and-out. You need to find your tribe before you can vibe.\n\n### Demand Generation\n\nOne of the foundational pillars of highly effective lead generation strategies is to attract your\nICP with quality content and clear communication.\n\n### SEO Content\n\nCreate quality content and optimise for maximum visibility on search engines. The more relevant\ntraffic you get, the more relevant leads you can generate.\n\n### Email Marketing\n\nNo hacks. No sales. Only relationship building, problem solving, and value delivery.\n\n### PPC campaigns\n\nMoney makes money; this adage holds true in the paid advertising world.\n\n### Case Studies\n\nMoney goes where trust flows. What better way to win trust than to let your work do the talking?\n\n### Social Media Marketing\n\nThought leadership on social media, especially, LinkedIn and Twitter can be a great lead magnet.\n\n### Conversion Optimisation\n\nRely on data-driven approach to content and funnel optimisation for the best conversion rate.\n\n**Testimonials**\n\n## Our Clients Absolutely Adore Us\n\n> \"...He also came up with unique storytelling style for different kind of blogs such as an industry\n> blog, or an opinionated blog or a tool relate blog which made the end out put read very credible.\n> We could see his blogs seeing Avg. Engagement time of more than 90 seconds (with some leading to\n> max of 4+minutes). Sometimes, he would take longer than usual to write a blog and produce the\n> final output but the wait was always worth it...\"\n> \n> Karanvir GuptaMarketing Director, Hatica\n\n> \"Nishant worked with me as a freelance writer during my time at magicpin, and he was a valuable\n> contributor to our blog content. His ability to craft engaging, SEO-friendly articles made a\n> strong impact on our content strategy. Reliable, creative, and deadline-oriented, he was a\n> pleasure to work with. I highly recommend him for any writing projects!\"\n> \n> Suhani GuptaCommunity Manager, Magicpin\n\n> It has been an absolute pleasure working with Nishant! His deep technical understanding and\n> ability to break complex concepts into engaging content are exceptional. An added advantage of\n> Nishant is that he understands the ICP well and helps you with possible content ideas. This is\n> really helpful!\n> \n> Ritesh ShettyContent Marketing Manager, LambdaTest\n\n\u23f3 Scheduling form is loading\u2026\nIf this takes long, open it in a new tab.\n[Open scheduler in new tab][36]\n\n## Marketing & Business Growth Insights To Help You Scale With Content\n\n#### Filter\n\n[Marketing][37]\n\n### [Unconscious Branding \u2013 Book Summary & Takeaways for Extraordinary Marketers][38]\n\nNote: As Amazon Affiliate, I'll earn commission for sales made through Amazon links shared on\u2026\n[Read More][39]\n\n### [7 Crazy Secrets to Writing SaaS Content that Converts][40]\n\nPeople don't read blogs anymore. SEO is dead. Marketing doesn't work for our niche. The\u2026\n[Read More][41]\n\n### [Guide For Founders To Assess SEO Agencies Without Being A Crass][42]\n\n37% of B2B marketers say that growing a high-quality lead pipeline is their #1 priority\u2026\n[Read More][43]\n\n### [Is SEO Really Going [Skip to main content][1]\nHit enter to search or ESC to close\n[Close Search ][2]\n[ [GrowthRomeo] ][3]\n[search][4]\n[ Menu ][5]\n* Services\n  * [Content Marketing][6]\n    * [Content Strategy][7]\n    * [SEO][8]\n    * [B2B Lead Generation][9]\n  * [Technology Writing][10]\n    * [SaaS Content Writing][11]\n    * [IT Content Writing][12]\n    * [Technical Writing][13]\n    * [AI-led Content Creation][14]\n* Industries\n  * [SaaS][15]\n  * [Information Technology][16]\n  * [DevTech][17]\n  * [Travel Tech][18]\n  * [HR Tech][19]\n* Resources\n  * [Insights][20]\n    * [Glossary][21]\n    * [Marketing Blog][22]\n    * [LinkedIn Blog][23]\n  * Tools\n    * [Word Counter][24]\n    * [Text Styling][25]\n    * [Case Convertor][26]\n* [Let\u2019s Talk?\ud83d\udd25\ud83d\ude80][27]\n* [linkedin ][28][email ][29]\n* [search][30]\nDigital Marketing Agency\n\n# {Content, Product, Brand} Marketing for Tech Startups\n\n[About GrowthRomeo][31]\n[Discuss Requirements ][32]\n[Hatica]\n[MagicPin]\n[LambdaTest]\n[Octoparse]\n[Redsteep]\n\n##### Experienced. On-demand.\n\n## What\u2019s GrowthRomeo?\n\nGrowthRomeo is a technology marketing agency that helps IT, SaaS, and AI startups grow with content,\nproduct, and brand marketing.\n\n##### [Let's Talk More?][33]\n\n##### Creative. Cool. Classy.\n\n## Why GrowthRomeo?\n\nWe *drive your pipeline* by enhancing your brand\u2019s visibility across marketing channels while being\n**cost-effective**, **creative**, and **consistent**.\n\n##### [Content Marketing Services][34]\n\n### **Get your business rocket to the desired growth velocity!**\n\n[Let's talk?][35]\n\n#### Content Marketing\n\nBrackish content to keep them drooling for more.\n\n#### SEO\n\nMaximise intent-ful discovery.\n\n#### Content Strategy\n\nRent our cortex, do it right.\n\n#### SEM\n\nSpell some inorganic magic.\n\n#### Marketing Automation\n\nFind time to talk with him/her.\n\n#### Landing pages\n\nActionable. Evocative. Enticing. Copy.\n\n## How GrowthRomeo Helps You Grow Your Startup?\n\n### ICP Research\n\nKnow your ICP in-and-out. You need to find your tribe before you can vibe.\n\n### Demand Generation\n\nOne of the foundational pillars of highly effective lead generation strategies is to attract your\nICP with quality content and clear communication.\n\n### SEO Content\n\nCreate quality content and optimise for maximum visibility on search engines. The more relevant\ntraffic you get, the more relevant leads you can generate.\n\n### Email Marketing\n\nNo hacks. No sales. Only relationship building, problem solving, and value delivery.\n\n### PPC campaigns\n\nMoney makes money; this adage holds true in the paid advertising world.\n\n### Case Studies\n\nMoney goes where trust flows. What better way to win trust than to let your work do the talking?\n\n### Social Media Marketing\n\nThought leadership on social media, especially, LinkedIn and Twitter can be a great lead magnet.\n\n### Conversion Optimisation\n\nRely on data-driven approach to content and funnel optimisation for the best conversion rate.\n\n**Testimonials**\n\n## Our Clients Absolutely Adore Us\n\n> \"...He also came up with unique storytelling style for different kind of blogs such as an industry\n> blog, or an opinionated blog or a tool relate blog which made the end out put read very credible.\n> We could see his blogs seeing Avg. Engagement time of more than 90 seconds (with some leading to\n> max of 4+minutes). Sometimes, he would take longer than usual to write a blog and produce the\n> final output but the wait was always worth it...\"\n> \n> Karanvir GuptaMarketing Director, Hatica\n\n> \"Nishant worked with me as a freelance writer during my time at magicpin, and he was a valuable\n> contributor to our blog content. His ability to craft engaging, SEO-friendly articles made a\n> strong impact on our content strategy. Reliable, creative, and deadline-oriented, he was a\n> pleasure to work with. I highly recommend him for any writing projects!\"\n> \n> Suhani GuptaCommunity Manager, Magicpin\n\n> It has been an absolute pleasure working with Nishant! His deep technical understanding and\n> ability to break complex concepts into engaging content are exceptional. An added advantage of\n> Nishant is that he understands the ICP well and helps you with possible content ideas. This is\n> really helpful!\n> \n> Ritesh ShettyContent Marketing Manager, LambdaTest\n\n\u23f3 Scheduling form is loading\u2026\nIf this takes long, open it in a new tab.\n[Open scheduler in new tab][36]\n\n## Marketing & Business Growth Insights To Help You Scale With Content\n\n#### Filter\n\n[Marketing][37]\n\n### [Unconscious Branding \u2013 Book Summary & Takeaways for Extraordinary Marketers][38]\n\nNote: As Amazon Affiliate, I'll earn commission for sales made through Amazon links shared on\u2026\n[Read More][39]\n\n### [7 Crazy Secrets to Writing SaaS Content that Converts][40]\n\nPeople don't read blogs anymore. SEO is dead. Marketing doesn't work for our niche. The\u2026\n[Read More][41]\n\n### [Guide For Founders To Assess SEO Agencies Without Being A Crass][42]\n\n37% of B2B marketers say that growing a high-quality lead pipeline is their #1 priority\u2026\n[Read More][43]\n\n### [Is SEO Really Going To Be Dead in 2025?][44]\n\nSEO is not going anywhere, anytime soon. That\u2019s a bold statement to make. You would\u2026\n[Read More][45]\n\n### [Major Google SEO Updates Timeline][46]\n\nSearch engines have been rolling out new improved versions of themselves at regular intervals since\u2026\n[Read More][47]\n\n## Content-led Growth\n\nContent Marketing\n\nContent Strategy\n\nSearch Engine Optimisation\n\nEmail Marketing\n\nB2B Lead Generation\n\nPerformance Marketing\n\nSocial Media Marketing\n\nSales Enablement\n\nProduct Marketing\n\nPodcast Marketing\n\nWebinar Marketing\n\nBlog Marketing\n\nThought Leadership\n\nCase Studies\n\nGraphic Design\n\nUI/UX/CX\n\nProduct Videos\n\nIT Content Writing\n\nLanding Pages Content\n\nAPI Documentation\n\nTechnical Content Writing\n\nB2B Technology Content Writing\n\nContent Revamping\n\nAI Content Creation & Editing\n\nProduct Documentation\n\n## Industries\n\nIT Consulting & Services\n\nSoftware as a Service (SaaS)\n\nNetwork Infrastructure\n\nCloud Migration & Hybrid IT\n\nEnterprise Software (ERP, CRM)\n\nData Centers & Hosting\n\nDevOps & Automation\n\nMarTech\n\nSales Tech\n\nHR Tech\n\nEdTech\n\nLegalTech\n\nCollaboration Tools\n\nProductivity & Office Tools\n\nAnalytics & BI Tools\n\nCustomer Support\n\neCommerce SaaS\n\nAPI Management Platforms\n\nApp Development Platforms\n\nServerless Platforms\n\nDevOps Platforms\n\nIntegration Platforms\n\nAI/ML Platforms\n\nMobile Backend as a Service (MBaaS)\n\