        "crawl_text": "[ Skip to content][1]\n[[Nutritionist Answers]][2]\n* [Foods A to Z][3]\n* [Blog][4]Menu Toggle\n  * [Fruits][5]\n  * [Vegetables][6]\n  * [Seafood][7]\n  * [Herbs and Spices][8]\n  * [Nuts and Seeds][9]\n* [About][10]Menu Toggle\n  * [Contact][11]\nSearch for: Search\n[ Search ][12]\n[[Nutritionist Answers]][13]\nMain Menu\n* [Foods A to Z][14]\n* [Blog][15]Menu Toggle\n  * [Fruits][16]\n  * [Vegetables][17]\n  * [Seafood][18]\n  * [Herbs and Spices][19]\n  * [Nuts and Seeds][20]\n* [About][21]Menu Toggle\n  * [Contact][22]\n\n## RESEARCH-BASED INFO\n## ON ALL YOUR FAVORITE FOODS\n\n# Explore the World of Food.\n# Learn From Nutrition Experts.\n\nOur team of Registered Dietitian Nutritionists creates the most helpful and up-to-date content on\nall things food. From our [nutrition database][23] to [trending articles][24], we\u2019re here to help\nyou learn about the latest health benefits of various foods and fun new ways to enjoy them.\n\n[ Read the Latest ][25]\n[\n[Does Acai Have Protein?][Does Acai Have Protein?]\n][26]\n\n### [ Does Acai Have Protein? A Nutritionist\u2019s Review ][27]\n\nAmy Richter, MS, RDN January 8, 2024\n\nAcai berries, known for their vibrant color and high antioxidant content, have become a staple in\nsmoothie bowls among food enthusiasts and health-conscious consumers. But\n\n[\n[Can You Be Allergic To Acai Berries?][Can You Be Allergic To Acai Berries?]\n][28]\n\n### [ Can You Be Allergic to Acai Berries? Here\u2019s How to Tell ][29]\n\nAmy Richter, MS, RDN January 4, 2024\n\nNavigating the world of food allergies can be a complex and sometimes daunting task, especially when\nit comes to less common allergens like acai berries.\u00a0\n\n[\n[Can You Eat Acai Every Day?][Can You Eat Acai Every Day?]\n][30]\n\n### [ Can You Eat Acai Every Day? (Maybe, it depends) ][31]\n\nAmy Richter, MS, RDN January 4, 2024\n\nAcai has soared in popularity over the past couple of decades, and many people now enjoy acai bowls\nas a breakfast or snack most days\n\n[\n[Are Acai Bowls Healthy? A Nutritionist's Review][Are Acai Bowls Healthy? A Nutritionist's Review]\n][32]\n\n### [ Are Acai Bowls Healthy? A Nutritionist\u2019s Review ][33]\n\nAmy Richter, MS, RDN December 19, 2023\n\nAcai bowls are made by blending frozen or powdered acai with a liquid base, such as juice, milk, or\nyogurt, pouring the puree into a\n\n[\n[Is Acai Acidic?][Is Acai Acidic?]\n][34]\n\n### [ Is Acai Acidic? (Yes, and Here\u2019s Why) ][35]\n\nAmy Richter, MS, RDN December 13, 2023\n\nAcai is a fruit that\u2019s grown in the Amazon rainforest. It\u2019s best known for its high antioxidant\ncontent and has gained a reputation as a\n\n[\n[Does Acai Make You Poop? (Yes, and Here's Why)][Does Acai Make You Poop? (Yes, and Here's Why)]\n][36]\n\n### [ Does Acai Make You Poop? (Yes, and Here\u2019s Why) ][37]\n\nAmy Richter, MS, RDN December 13, 2023\n\nAcai berries are small, dark purple fruits best known as the key ingredient in the oh-so-popular\nacai bowl, but they offer more than just a\n\nPage1 [Page2][38] [Page3][39] [Page4][40] [Page5][41]\n[ View Our Web Stories! ][42]\n\n## subscribe to our newsletter\n\nEmail Address\nSubmit\n\nCopyright \u00a9 2026 Nutritionist Answers | [Privacy Policy][43] | [Terms of Use][44]| [Disclaimer][45]\n* [Cookie Policy][46]\n\n[][47][][48][][49]\n[[Nutritionist Answers]][50]\nManage Cookie Consent\nWe use cookies to optimize our website and our service.\nFunctional Functional Always active\nThe technical storage or access is strictly necessary for the legitimate purpose of enabling the use\nof a specific service explicitly requested by the subscriber or user, or for the sole purpose of\ncarrying out the transmission of a communication over an electronic communications network.\nPreferences Preferences\nThe technical storage or access is necessary for the legitimate purpose of storing preferences that\nare not requested by the subscriber or user.\nStatistics Statistics\nThe technical storage or access that is used exclusively for statistical purposes. The technical\nstorage or access that is used exclusively for anonymous statistical purposes. Without a subpoena,\nvoluntary compliance on the part of your Internet Service Provider, or additional records from a\nthird party, information stored or retrieved for this purpose alone cannot usually be used to\nidentify you.\nMarketing Marketing\nThe technical storage or access is required to create user profiles to send advertising, or to track\nthe user on a website or across several websites for similar marketing purposes.\n* [Manage options][51]\n* [Manage services][52]\n* [Manage {vendor_count} vendors][53]\n* [Read more about these purposes][54]\nAccept Dismiss Preferences Save preferences [Preferences][55]\n* [{title}][56]\n* [{title}][57]\n* [{title}][58]\nManage consent\nScroll to Top\n\n[1]: #content\n[2]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/\n[3]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/foods-a-to-z/\n[4]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/blog/\n[5]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/fruits/\n[6]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/vegetables/\n[7]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/seafood/\n[8]: https://nutritionistanswers.com/herbs-spices/\n[9]: ht [ Skip to content][1]\n[[Nutritionist Answers]][2]\n* [Foods A to Z][3]\n* [Blog][4]Menu Toggle\n  * [Fruits][5]\n  * [Vegetables][6]\n  * [Seafood][7]\n  * [Herbs and Spices][8]\n  * [Nuts and Seeds][9]\n* [About][10]Menu Toggle\n  * [Contact][11]\nSearch for: Search\n[ Search ][12]\n[[Nutritionist Answers]][13]\nMain Menu\n* [Foods A to Z][14]\n* [Blog][15]Menu Toggle\n  * [Fruits][16]\n  * [Vegetables][17]\n  * [Seafood][18]\n  * [Herbs and Spices][19]\n  * [Nuts and Seeds][20]\n* [About][21]Menu Toggle\n  * [Contact][22]\n\n## RESEARCH-BASED INFO\n## ON ALL YOUR FAVORITE FOODS\n\n# Explore the World of Food.\n# Learn From Nutrition Experts.\n\nOur team of Registered Dietitian Nutritionists creates the most helpful and up-to-date content on\nall things food. Fr