Wine Italia\nmagazine and at Travel + Leisure Italia, she also contributes as a freelance to many\nother\u00a0publications and guides, both in Italy and abroad, print and online.\n\n[Read more \u2192][66]\nMarch 27, 2025\n[\n][67]\nMarch 27, 2025\n[ Isabel Putinja ][68]\nMarch 27, 2025\n\nIsabel Putinja has been a freelance writer for two decades, penning articles on topics related to\ntravel, art & culture, and food for a variety of international publications.\n\n[Read more \u2192][69]\nMarch 27, 2025\n[\n][70]\nMarch 27, 2025\n[ Giuliana Mackler ][71]\nMarch 27, 2025\n\nGiuliana Mackler is an olive oil specialist, writer, and educator with a background in hospitality\nmanagement. She holds certifications from the\u00a0Universit\u00e0 di Scienze Gastronomiche, Universidad de\nJa\u00e9n, International Olive Council, Organizzazione Nazionale Assaggiatori Olio Di Oliva and many\nmore.\n\n[Read more \u2192][72]\nMarch 27, 2025\n[\n][73]\nMarch 27, 2025\n[ Shoshi Parks ][74]\nMarch 27, 2025\n\nShoshi Parks is a Bay Area-based freelance writer specializing in food, travel and history. Her work\nhas appeared at NPR, Smithsonian, Gastro Obscura, Civil Eats, Vinepair, Vice and a variety of other\noutlets. Find her online at\u00a0[www.shoshiparks.net][75].\n\n[Read more \u2192][76]\nMarch 27, 2025\n[\n][77]\nMarch 27, 2025\n[ Megan Lloyd ][78]\nMarch 27, 2025\n\nMegan Lloyd is a freelance journalist living in Sevilla, Spain. She specializes in food, drink,\ntravel, and her work has appeared in\u00a0publications\u00a0like National Geographic Traveler, Bon App\u00e9tit,\nand Cond\u00e9 Nast Traveler.\n\n[Read more \u2192][79]\nMarch 27, 2025\n[\n][80]\nMarch 27, 2025\n[ Robin Catalano ][81]\nMarch 27, 2025\n\nRobin Catalano is a Solas, SATW, and ASJA Award-winning travel, culture, and food journalist. Her\nstories have appeared in the New York Times, National Geographic, Travel + Leisure, Washington Post,\nSmithsonian, Conde Nast Traveler, TIME, AFAR, Hemispheres, Robb Report,