[36] [alcohol professor][37] [vinegar professor][38]\n[ [The Olive Oil Professor ] ][39]\nScroll\n\u00a0\n\nElevate Your Olive Oil Knowledge\n\n# **Welcome to the Olive oil professor**\n\n[ featured articles ][40]\n\u00a0\n\u00a0\n\n## *\u2014hot off the presses\u2014*\n\nBlog\n[\n][41]\nJune 17, 2026\n[Pamela Vachon][42]\n[ How Chefs Use Olive Oil in Desserts Beyond Cake ][43]\nJune 17, 2026\n[Pamela Vachon][44]\nJune 17, 2026\n[Pamela Vachon][45]\n[\n][46]\nJune 10, 2026\n[Alisa Scerrato][47]\n[ 6 Ways to Use Your Best Olive Oil ][48]\nJune 10, 2026\n[Alisa Scerrato][49]\nJune 10, 2026\n[Alisa Scerrato][50]\n[\n][51]\nJune 3, 2026\n[Amber Selene Turpin][52]\n[ 5 California Resorts for Olive Oil Lovers ][53]\nJune 3, 2026\n[Amber Selene Turpin][54]\nJune 3, 2026\n[Amber Selene Turpin][55]\n[\n][56]\nMay 27, 2026\n[Pamela Vachon][57]\n[ Biancolilla: The Sicilian Olive to Watch ][58]\nMay 27, 2026\n[Pamela Vachon][59]\nMay 27, 2026\n[Pamela Vachon][60]\n\u00a0\n[ view all articles ][61]\n\u00a0\n\u00a0\n\u00a0\n\n# **USI Olive OIL Competition**\n\n## **June 5, 2026**\n\n[ Enter Now ][62]\n\u00a0\n\n## \u00a0The faculty\n\n[*See All Contributing Editors*][63]\n\nAuthors\n[\n][64]\nMarch 27, 2025\n[ Luciana Squadrilli ][65]\nMarch 27, 2025\n\nLuciana Squadrilli is a food and travel writer based in Rome. Senior editor at Food&Wine Italia\nmagazine and at Travel + Leisure Italia, she also contributes as a freelance to many\nother\u00a0publications and guides, both in Italy and abroad, print and online.\n\n[Read more \u2192][66]\nMarch 27, 2025\n[\n][67]\nMarch 27, 2025\n[ Isabel Putinja ][68]\nMarch 27, 2025\n\nIsabel Putinja has been a freelance writer for two decades, penning articles on topics related to\ntravel, art & culture, and food for a variety of international publications.\n\n[Read more \u2192][69]\nMarch 27, 2025\n[\n][70]\nMarch 27, 2025\n[ Giuliana Mackler ][71]\nMarch 27, 2025\n\nGiuliana Mackler is an olive oil specialist, writer, and educator with a background in hospitality\nmanagement. She holds certifications from the\u00a0Universit\u00e0 di Scienze Gastronomiche, Universidad de\nJa\u00e9n, International Olive Council, Organizzazione Nazionale Assaggiatori Olio Di Oliva and many\nmore.\n\n[Read more \u2192][72]\nMarch 27, 2025\n[\n][73]\nMarch 27, 2025\n[ Shoshi Parks ][74]\nMarch 27, 2025\n\nShoshi Parks is a Bay Area-based freelance writer specializing in food, travel and history. Her work\nhas appeared at NPR, Smithsonian, Gastro Obscura, Civil Eats, Vinepair, Vice and a variety of other\noutlets. Find her online at\u00a0[www.shoshiparks.net][75].\n\n[Read more \u2192][76]\nMarch 27, 2025\n[\n][77]\nMarch 27, 2025\n[ Megan Lloyd ][78]\nMarch 27, 2025\n\nMegan Lloyd is a freelance journalist living in Sevilla, Spain. She specializes in food, drink,\ntravel, and her work has appeared in\u00a0publications\u00a0like National Geographic Traveler, Bon App\u00e9tit,\nand Cond\u00e9 Nast Traveler.\n\n[Read more \u2192][79]\nMarch 27, 2025\n[\n][80]\nMarch 27, 2025\n[ Robin Catalano ][81]\nMarch 27, 2025\n\nRobin Catalano is a Solas, SATW, and ASJA Award-winning travel, culture, and food journalist. Her\nstories have appeared in the New York Times, National Geographic, Travel + Leisure, Washington Post,\nSmithsonian, Conde Nast Traveler, TIME, AFAR, Hemispheres, Robb Report, Fodor's, Food & Wine, and\nmany more.\n\n[Read more \u2192][82]\nMarch 27, 2025\n\u00a0\nBrowse by Topic\n* [ Confections ][83]\n* [ Cooking ][84]\n* [ Culture ][85]\n* [ Education ][86]\n* [ Health ][87]\n* [ Most Popular ][88]\n* [ News ][89]\n* [ Pairing ][90]\n* [ Producer ][91]\n* [ Product ][92]\n* [ Profile ][93]\n* [ Recipe ][94]\n* [ Travel ][95]\nBrowse by Author\n* [ Alisa Scerrato ][96]\n* [ Alix Wall ][97]\n* [ Amber Selene Turpin ][98]\n* [ Amy Sherman ][99]\n* [ Amy Beth Wright ][100]\n* [ Anna Mindess ][101]\n* [ Ansley Ansley Evans ][102]\n* [ Brenda Wilkinson ][103]\n* [ Carissa Chesanek ][104]\n* [ Cori Solomon ][105]\n* [ Elisa